[{"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Thayer", "NNP"]], ["&", "CC"], ["Eldridge", "NNP"]]], "people": ["Walt Whitman", "Vol"], "money": [], "year": "1860", "locations": ["West"], "month": "lat", "parties": ["Walt Whitman", "Thayer"], "properDate": "lat 0, 1860", "gpe": ["Grass"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [], "text": " ...are already getting to be pretty numerous and outspoken     Walt Whitman  Sometimes I think it would be better still to make a compact and finished Vol. of the whole issue of \"Leaves of Grass,\" including the former ones with the new ones, for they are all of a uniform pattern.   This would afford a splendid living American Vol. that would go like the devil through the West, and among the young men everywhere.     ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["...", ":"], ["are", "VBP"], ["already", "RB"], ["getting", "VBG"], ["to", "TO"], ["be", "VB"], ["pretty", "RB"], ["numerous", "JJ"], ["and", "CC"], ["outspoken", "VBN"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["Sometimes", "NNP"], ["I", "NNP"], ["think", "VBP"], ["it", "PRP"], ["would", "MD"], ["be", "VB"], ["better", "JJR"], ["still", "RB"], ["to", "TO"], ["make", "VB"], ["a", "DT"], ["compact", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["finished", "VBD"], [["Vol", "NNP"]], [".", "."]], [["of", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["whole", "JJ"], ["issue", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["``", "``"], ["Leaves", "NNPS"], ["of", "IN"], [["Grass", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["''", "''"], ["including", "VBG"], ["the", "DT"], ["former", "JJ"], ["ones", "NNS"], ["with", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["new", "JJ"], ["ones", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["for", "IN"], ["they", "PRP"], ["are", "VBP"], ["all", "RB"], ["of", "IN"], ["a", "DT"], ["uniform", "NN"], ["pattern", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["This", "DT"], ["would", "MD"], ["afford", "VB"], ["a", "DT"], ["splendid", "JJ"], ["living", "NN"], [["American", "NNP"], ["Vol", "NNP"]], [".", "."]], [["that", "DT"], ["would", "MD"], ["go", "VB"], ["like", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["devil", "NN"], ["through", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], [["West", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["and", "CC"], ["among", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["young", "JJ"], ["men", "NNS"], ["everywhere", "RB"], [".", "."]]], "sentences": [" ...are already getting to be pretty numerous and outspoken     Walt Whitman  Sometimes I think it would be better still to make a compact and finished Vol.", "of the whole issue of \"Leaves of Grass,\" including the former ones with the new ones, for they are all of a uniform pattern.", "This would afford a splendid living American Vol.", "that would go like the devil through the West, and among the young men everywhere.     "], "words": ["...", "are", "already", "getting", "to", "be", "pretty", "numerous", "and", "outspoken", "Walt", "Whitman", "Sometimes", "I", "think", "it", "would", "be", "better", "still", "to", "make", "a", "compact", "and", "finished", "Vol.", "of", "the", "whole", "issue", "of", "``", "Leaves", "of", "Grass", ",", "''", "including", "the", "former", "ones", "with", "the", "new", "ones", ",", "for", "they", "are", "all", "of", "a", "uniform", "pattern.", "This", "would", "afford", "a", "splendid", "living", "American", "Vol.", "that", "would", "go", "like", "the", "devil", "through", "the", "West", ",", "and", "among", "the", "young", "men", "everywhere", "."], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.0", "recipient": "Thayer", "organizations": ["American Vol"], "sender": "Walt Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/yal.00098.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Walt Whitman to Thayer & Eldridge"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], ["the", "DT"], [["Editors", "NNP"]], ["of", "IN"], [["Harper", "NNP"]], ["'s", "POS"], [["Magazine", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Maine", "Will", "Walt"], "money": [], "year": "1860", "locations": [], "month": "Jan", "parties": ["Walt Whitman", "Editors", "Harper", "Magazine"], "properDate": "Jan 7, 1860", "gpe": ["South", "West", "North", "East", "Kanada", "Texas", "Virginia", "America", "America", "American", "Furthermore", "American", "Cash"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[22.5009081, 114.1558258], [37.4315734, -78.6568942]], "text": " The theory of \"A Chant of National Feuillage\"2 is to bring in, (devoting a line, or two or three lines, to each,) a comprehensive collection of touches, local\u00e9s, incidents, idiomatic scenes, from every section, South, West, North, East, Kanada, Texas, Maine, Virginia, the Mississippi Valley, &c. &c. &c.   all intensely fused to the urgency of compact America, \"America always\"   all in a vein of graphic, short, clear, hasting along   as having a huge bouquet to collect, and quickly taking and binding in every characteristic subject that offers itself   making a compact, the-whole-surrounding, National Poem, after its sort, after my own style. Is there any other poem of the sort extant   or indeed hitherto attempted? You may start at the style. Yes, it is a new style, of course, but that is necessitated by new theories, new themes   or say the new treatment of themes, forced upon us for American purposes. Every really new person, (poet or other,) makes his style   sometimes a little way removed from the previous models   sometimes very far removed. Furthermore, I have surely attained headway enough with the American public, especially with the literary classes, to make it worth your while to give them a sight of me with all my neologism. The price is $40. Cash down on acceptance. I reserve the use of the piece in any collection of my poems I may publish in future. Should my name be printed in the programme of contributors at any time it must not be lower down than third in the list. If the piece is declined, please keep the MS. for me to be called for. Will send, or call, last of next week. Walt WhitmanJan. 7th, '60. ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["The", "DT"], ["theory", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["``", "``"], ["A", "DT"], ["Chant", "NNP"], ["of", "IN"], [["National", "NNP"]], ["Feuillage", "NNP"], ["''", "''"], ["2", "CD"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["to", "TO"], ["bring", "VB"], ["in", "IN"], [",", ","], ["(", "CC"], ["devoting", "VBG"], ["a", "DT"], ["line", "NN"], [",", ","], ["or", "CC"], ["two", "CD"], ["or", "CC"], ["three", "CD"], ["lines", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["to", "TO"], ["each", "DT"], [",", ","], [")", ":"], ["a", "DT"], ["comprehensive", "JJ"], ["collection", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["touches", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["local\u00e9s", "NNP"], [",", ","], ["incidents", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["idiomatic", "JJ"], ["scenes", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["from", "IN"], ["every", "DT"], ["section", "NN"], [",", ","], [["South", "NNP"]], [",", ","], [["West", "NNP"]], [",", ","], [["North", "NNP"]], [",", ","], [["East", "NNP"]], [",", ","], [["Kanada", "NNP"]], [",", ","], [["Texas", "NNP"]], [",", ","], [["Maine", "NNP"]], [",", ","], [["Virginia", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["the", "DT"], [["Mississippi", "NNP"], ["Valley", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["c.", "NNP"], ["&", "CC"], ["c.", "NNP"], ["&", "CC"], ["c.", "NNP"], ["all", "DT"], ["intensely", "RB"], ["fused", "VBN"], ["to", "TO"], ["the", "DT"], ["urgency", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["compact", "NN"], [["America", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["``", "``"], [["America", "NNP"]], ["always", "RB"], ["''", "''"], ["all", "DT"], ["in", "IN"], ["a", "DT"], ["vein", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["graphic", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["short", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["clear", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["hasting", "VBG"], ["along", "IN"], ["as", "IN"], ["having", "VBG"], ["a", "DT"], ["huge", "JJ"], ["bouquet", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["collect", "VB"], [",", ","], ["and", "CC"], ["quickly", "RB"], ["taking", "VBG"], ["and", "CC"], ["binding", "VBG"], ["in", "IN"], ["every", "DT"], ["characteristic", "JJ"], ["subject", "NN"], ["that", "WDT"], ["offers", "VBZ"], ["itself"