"], [["Treasury", "NNP"]], [".", "."]]], "sentences": ["  Concord Massachusetts | 10 January 2, 1863  Dear Sir,2 Mr Walt Whitman, of New York, writes me that he is seeking employment in the public service in Washington, & perhaps some application on his part has already been made to yourself.", "Will you permit me to say that he is known to me as a man of strong original genius, combining, with marked eccentricities, great powers & valuable traits of character: a self-relying large-hearted man, much beloved by his friends; entirely patriotic & benevolent in his theory, tastes, & practice.", "If his writings are in certain points open to criticism, they show extraordinary power, & are more deeply American, democratic, & in the interest of political liberty, than those of any other poet.", "A man of his talents & dispositions will quickly make himself useful, and, if the government has work that he can do, I think it may easily find that it has called to its side more valuable aid than it bargained for.", "With entire respect, Your obedient servant, R. W. Emerson.", "Hon Salmon P. Chase, | Secretary of the Treasury.  "], "words": ["Concord", "Massachusetts", "|", "10", "January", "2", ",", "1863", "Dear", "Sir,2", "Mr", "Walt", "Whitman", ",", "of", "New", "York", ",", "writes", "me", "that", "he", "is", "seeking", "employment", "in", "the", "public", "service", "in", "Washington", ",", "&", "perhaps", "some", "application", "on", "his", "part", "has", "already", "been", "made", "to", "yourself.", "Will", "you", "permit", "me", "to", "say", "that", "he", "is", "known", "to", "me", "as", "a", "man", "of", "strong", "original", "genius", ",", "combining", ",", "with", "marked", "eccentricities", ",", "great", "powers", "&", "valuable", "traits", "of", "character", ":", "a", "self-relying", "large-hearted", "man", ",", "much", "beloved", "by", "his", "friends", ";", "entirely", "patriotic", "&", "benevolent", "in", "his", "theory", ",", "tastes", ",", "&", "practice.", "If", "his", "writings", "are", "in", "certain", "points", "open", "to", "criticism", ",", "they", "show", "extraordinary", "power", ",", "&", "are", "more", "deeply", "American", ",", "democratic", ",", "&", "in", "the", "interest", "of", "political", "liberty", ",", "than", "those", "of", "any", "other", "poet.", "A", "man", "of", "his", "talents", "&", "dispositions", "will", "quickly", "make", "himself", "useful", ",", "and", ",", "if", "the", "government", "has", "work", "that", "he", "can", "do", ",", "I", "think", "it", "may", "easily", "find", "that", "it", "has", "called", "to", "its", "side", "more", "valuable", "aid", "than", "it", "bargained", "for.", "With", "entire", "respect", ",", "Your", "obedient", "servant", ",", "R.", "W.", "Emerson.", "Hon", "Salmon", "P.", "Chase", ",", "|", "Secretary", "of", "the", "Treasury", "."], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.150414796682", "recipient": "Salmon P. Chase", "organizations": ["Massachusetts", "Treasury"], "sender": "Ralph Waldo Emerson", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/nar.00002.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Ralph Waldo Emerson to Salmon P. Chase ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Ralph", "NNP"], ["Waldo", "NNP"], ["Emerson", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["William", "NNP"], ["H.", "NNP"], ["Seward", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Masstts", "Emerson", "William"], "money": [], "year": "1863", "locations": [], "month": "Jan", "parties": ["Ralph Waldo Emerson", "William H. Seward"], "properDate": "Jan 10, 1863", "gpe": ["New York", "Washington", "Permit", "American", "Hon"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[40.7143528, -74.00597309999999], [38.8951118, -77.0363658]], "text": "  Concord | Masstts |  Jan. 10 | 1863  Dear Sir, Mr Walt Whitman, of New York, writes me, that he wishes to obtain employment in the public service in Washington, & has made, or is about making some application to yourself. Permit me to say that he is known to me as a man of strong original genius, combining, with marked eccentricities, great powers & valuable traits of character: a self-relying, large-hearted man, much beloved by his friends; entirely patriotic & benevolent in his theory, tastes, & practice. If his writings are in certain points open to criticism, they yet show extraordinary power, & are more deeply American, democratic, & in the interest of political liberty, than those of any other poet. He is indeed a child of the people, & their champion. A man of his talents & dispositions will quickly make himself useful, and, if the Government has work that he can do, I think it may easily find, that it has called to its side more valuable aid than it bargained for. With great respect, Your obedient servant, R. W. Emerson.      Hon. William H. Seward2, | Secretary of State.  ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Concord", "NNP"]], ["|", ":"], [["Masstts", "NNP"]], ["|", ":"], ["Jan.", "NNP"], ["10", "CD"], ["|", "CD"], ["1863", "CD"], ["Dear", "NNP"], ["Sir", "NNP"], [",", ","], ["Mr", "NNP"], ["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"], [",", ","], ["of", "IN"], [["New", "NNP"], ["York", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["writes", "VBZ"], ["me", "PRP"], [",", ","], ["that", "IN"], ["he", "PRP"], ["wishes", "VBZ"], ["to", "TO"], ["obtain", "VB"], ["employment", "NN"], ["in", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["public", "NN"], ["service", "NN"], ["in", "IN"], [["Washington", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["has", "VBZ"], ["made", "VBN"], [",", ","], ["or", "CC"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["about", "IN"], ["making", "VBG"], ["some", "DT"], ["application", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["yourself", "PRP"], [".", "."]], [[["Permit", "NN"]], ["me", "PRP"], ["to", "TO"], ["say", "VB"], ["that", "IN"], ["he", "PRP"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["known", "VBN"], ["to", "TO"], ["me", "PRP"], ["as", "IN"], ["a", "DT"], ["man", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["strong", "JJ"], ["original", "JJ"], ["genius", "NN"], [",", ","], ["