", "he", "has", "been", "lying", "panting", "for", "breath", "a", "pitiful", "sight.", "I", "have", "been", "with", "him", "some", "every", "day", "or", "night", "since", "he", "arrived.", "He", "suffers", "a", "great", "deal", "with", "the", "heat", "says", "little", "or", "nothing", "is", "flighty", "the", "last", "three", "days", ",", "at", "times", "knows", "me", "always", ",", "however", "calls", "me", "``", "Walter", "''", "(", "sometimes", "calls", "the", "name", "over", "and", "over", "and", "over", "again", ",", "musingly", ",", "abstractly", ",", "to", "himself.", ")", "His", "father", "lives", "at", "Breesport", ",", "Chemung", "county", ",", "N.", "Y.", ",", "is", "a", "mechanic", "with", "large", "family", "is", "a", "steady", ",", "religious", "man", ";", "his", "mother", "too", "is", "living.", "I", "have", "written", "to", "them", ",", "and", "shall", "write", "again", "to-day", "Erastus", "has", "not", "receiv", "'d", "a", "word", "from", "home", "for", "months.", "As", "I", "sit", "here", "writing", "to", "you", ",", "M.", ",", "I", "wish", "you", "could", "see", "the", "whole", "scene.", "This", "young", "man", "lies", "within", "reach", "of", "me", ",", "flat", "on", "his", "back", ",", "his", "hands", "clasp", "'d", "across", "his", "breast", ",", "his", "thick", "hair", "cut", "close", ";", "he", "is", "dozing", ",", "breathing", "hard", ",", "every", "breath", "a", "spasm", "it", "looks", "so", "cruel.", "He", "is", "a", "noble", "youngster", ",", "I", "consider", "him", "past", "all", "hope.", "Often", "there", "is", "no", "one", "with", "him", "for", "a", "long", "while.", "I", "am", "here", "as", "much", "as", "possible", "."], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.177478580171", "recipient": "Louisa Van Velsor Whitman", "organizations": ["Breesport"], "sender": "Walt Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/med.00302.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Walt Whitman to Louisa Van Velsor Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["William", "NNP"], ["E.", "NNP"], ["Vandemark", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": [], "money": [], "year": "1863", "locations": [], "month": "Jul", "parties": ["William E. Vandemark", "Walt Whitman"], "properDate": "Jul 31, 1863", "gpe": ["Friend"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [], "text": " Friend witman I now take the plesure of fulfilling my promace of writing to yo hoping to find yo en Joying good hlth I am not very well i am worse now than wen i got out of bed i tore my wound acoming home the hole is a bout half an inch square I hante ben noware sence i have been home i have had the docter and he ordered me to bathe in sider soaky i will hef to have my furlow exstended I would have written be fore but i was not able to do it yo must exscuse me    the crops look much better here than they do in washington I find a grate many that donte know me when i arrived in york my cosin was thare and he brought me to my home it has ben rainy ever since I have been home    give my love to the boys in ward B I will be back Just as soon as i am able to come No more at present Good by answer by return mail from a friend and ever shall be ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Friend", "NN"]], ["witman", "NN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["now", "RB"], ["take", "VBP"], ["the", "DT"], ["plesure", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["fulfilling", "VBG"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["promace", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["writing", "VBG"], ["to", "TO"], ["yo", "VB"], ["hoping", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["find", "VB"], ["yo", "NN"], ["en", "NN"], ["Joying", "NNP"], ["good", "JJ"], ["hlth", "NN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["not", "RB"], ["very", "RB"], ["well", "RB"], ["i", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["worse", "JJ"], ["now", "RB"], ["than", "IN"], ["wen", "NNS"], ["i", "PRP"], ["got", "VBD"], ["out", "RP"], ["of", "IN"], ["bed", "VBN"], ["i", "PRP"], ["to