G"], ["the", "DT"], ["army", "NN"], ["on", "IN"], ["furlough", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["re-enlisting", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["going", "VBG"], ["north", "JJ"], ["for", "IN"], ["a", "DT"], ["while", "NN"], ["they", "PRP"], ["pass", "VBP"], ["through", "IN"], ["here", "RB"], ["quite", "RB"], ["largely", "RB"], [["Mother", "NNP"]], [",", ","], [["Lewis", "NNP"], ["Brown", "NNP"]], ["is", "VBZ"], ["getting", "VBG"], ["quite", "RB"], ["well", "RB"], [",", ","], ["he", "PRP"], ["will", "MD"], ["soon", "RB"], ["be", "VB"], ["able", "JJ"], ["to", "TO"], ["have", "VB"], ["a", "DT"], ["wooden", "JJ"], ["leg", "NN"], ["put", "VBD"], ["on", "IN"], [",", ","], ["he", "PRP"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["very", "RB"], ["restless", "JJ"], ["&", "CC"], ["active", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["wants", "NNS"], ["to", "TO"], ["go", "VB"], ["around", "IN"], ["all", "DT"], ["the", "DT"], ["time", "NN"], [["Sam", "NNP"], ["Beatty2", "NNP"]], ["is", "VBZ"], ["here", "RB"], ["in", "IN"], [["Washington", "NNP"]], ["We", "NNP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["had", "VBN"], ["quite", "RB"], ["a", "DT"], ["snow", "NN"], ["storm", "NN"], [",", ","], ["but", "CC"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["clear", "JJ"], ["&", "CC"], ["sunny", "JJ"], ["to-day", "JJ"], ["here", "RB"], [",", ","], ["but", "CC"], ["sloshy", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["wearing", "VBG"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["army", "NN"], ["boots", "NNS"], ["any", "DT"], ["thing", "NN"], ["but", "CC"], ["the", "DT"], ["dust", "NN"], ["Dear", "NNP"], ["mother", "NN"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["want", "VBP"], ["to", "TO"], ["see", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["&", "CC"], [["Sis", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], [["Mat", "NNP"]], ["&", "CC"], ["all", "DT"], ["very", "RB"], ["much", "JJ"], ["if", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["can", "MD"], ["get", "VB"], ["a", "DT"], ["chance", "NN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["think", "VBP"], ["I", "PRP"], ["shall", "MD"], ["come", "VB"], ["home", "NN"], ["for", "IN"], ["a", "DT"], ["while", "NN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["want", "VBP"], ["to", "TO"], ["try", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["bring", "VB"], ["out", "RP"], ["a", "DT"], ["book", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["poems", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["a", "DT"], ["new", "JJ"], ["one", "CD"], ["to", "TO"], ["be", "VB"], ["called", "VBN"], ["``", "``"], [["Drum", "NNP"], ["Taps", "NNP"]], ["''", "''"], ["&", "CC"], ["I", "PRP"], ["want", "VBP"], ["to", "TO"], ["come", "VB"], ["to", "TO"], [["New", "NNP"], ["York", "NNP"]], ["for", "IN"], ["that", "DT"], ["purpose", "NN"], ["too", "RB"], [["Mother", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["hav", "VBP"], ["n't", "RB"], ["given", "VBN"], ["up", "RP"], ["the", "DT"], ["project", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], [["lecturing3", "NNP"]], ["either", "CC"], ["but", "CC"], ["whatever", "RB"], ["I", "PRP"], ["do", "VBP"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["shall", "MD"], ["for", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["main", "JJ"], ["thing", "NN"], ["devote", "NN"], ["myself", "NN"], ["for", "IN"], ["years", "NNS"], ["to", "TO"], ["come", "VB"], ["to", "TO"], ["these", "DT"], ["wounded", "JJ"], ["&", "CC"], ["sick", "NN"], [",", ","], ["what", "WP"], ["little", "RB"], ["I", "PRP"], ["can", "MD"], ["Well", "NNP"], ["good", "JJ"], ["bye", "NN"], [",", ","], ["dear", "JJ"], ["mother", "NN"], [",", ","], ["for", "IN"], ["present", "NN"], ["write", "NN"], ["soon", "RB"], [["Walt", "NNP"]]]], "sentences": ["  Washington |   March 2 1864  Dear mother You or Jeff must try to write as soon as you receive this & let me know how little Sis is, tell me if she got entirely over the croup & how she is   also about George's trunks,1 I do hope he recovered them, it was such a misfortune   I want to hear the end of it, I am in hopes I shall hear that he has got them   I have not seen in the papers whether the 51st has left New York yet   Mother, I want to hear all about home & all the occurrences, especially the two things I have just mentioned, & how you are, dearest mother, you must write me exactly how you are for somehow I was thinking from your letters lately whether you was as well as usual or not   write how my dear sister Mat is too, & whether you are still going to stay there in Portland av.", "the coming year   Well, dear mother, I am just the same here, nothing new, I am well & hearty, & constantly moving around among the wounded & sick   there are a great many of the latter coming up   the hospitals here are quite full   lately they have [been] picking out in the hospitals all that had pretty well recovered, & sending them back to their regiments, they seem to be determined to strengthen the army this spring, to the utmost   they are sending down many to their reg'ts that are not fit to go, in my opinion   then there are squads & companies & reg'ts too passing through here in one steady stream going down to front, returning from furlough home   but then there are quite a number leaving the army on furlough, re-enlisting, & going north for a while   they pass through here quite largely    Mother, Lewis Brown is getting quite well, he will soon be able to have a wooden leg put on, he is very restless & active, & wants to go around all the time    Sam Beatty2 is here in Washington   We have had quite a snow storm, but is clear & sunny to-day here, but sloshy, I am wearing my army boots   any thing but the dust   Dear mother, I want to see you & Sis, & Mat & all very much   if I can get a chance I think I shall come home for a while   I want to try to bring out a book of poems, a new one to be called \"Drum Taps\" & I want to come to New York for that purpose too    Mother, I havn't given up the project of lecturing3 either   but whatever I do, I shall for the main thing devote myself for years to come to these wounded & sick, what little I can   Well good bye, dear mother, for present   write soon    Walt "], "words": ["Washington", "|", "March", "2", "1864", "Dear", "mother", "You", "or", "Jeff", "must", "try", "to", "write", "as", "soon", "as", "you", "receive", "this", "&", "let", "me", "know", "how", "little", "Sis", "is", ",", "tell", "me", "if", "she", "got", "entirely", "over", "the", "croup", "&", "how", "she", "is", "also", "about", "George", "'s", "trunks,1", "I", "do", "hope", "he", "recovered", "them", ",", "it", "was", "such", "a", "misfortune", "I", "want", "to", "hear", "the", "end", "of", "it", ",", "I", "am", "in", "hopes", "I", "shall", "hear", "that", "he", "has", "got", "them", "I", "have", "not", "seen", "in", "the", "papers", "whether", "the", "51st", "has", "left", "New", "York", "yet", "Mother", ",", "I", "want", "to", "hear", "all", "about", "home", "&", "all", "the", "occurrences", ",", "especially", "the", "two", "things", "I", "have", "just", "mentioned", ",", "&", "how", "you", "are", ",", "dearest", "mother", ",", "you", "must", "write", "me", "exactly", "how", "you", "are", "for", "somehow", "I", "was", "thinking", "from", "your", "letters", "lately", "whether", "you", "was", "as", "well", "as", "usual", "or", "not", "write", "how", "my", "dear", "sister", "Mat", "is", "too", ",", "&", "whether", "you", "are", "still", "going", "to", "stay", "there", "in", "Portland", "av.", "the", "coming", "year", "Well", ",", "dear", "mother", ",", "I", "am", "just", "the", "same", "here", ",", "nothing", "new", ",", "I", "am", "well", "&", "hearty", ",", "&", "constantly", "moving", "around", "among", "the", "wounded", "&", "sick", "there", "are", "a", "great", "many", "of", "the", "latter", "coming", "up", "the", "hospitals", "here", "are", "quite", "full", "lately", "they", "have", "[", "been", "]", "picking", "out", "in", "the", "hospitals", "all", "that", "had", "pretty", "well", "recovered", ",", "&", "sending", "them", "back", "to", "their", "regiments", ",", "they", "seem", "to", "be", "determined", "to", "strengthen", "the", "army", "this", "spring", ",", "to", "the", "utmost", "they", "are", "sending", "down", "many", "to", "their", "reg'ts", "that", "are", "not", "fit", "to", "go", ",", "in", "my", "opinion", "then", "there", "are", "squads", "&", "companies", "&", "reg'ts", "too", "passing", "through", "here", "in", "one", "steady", "stream", "going", "down", "to", "front", ",", "returning", "from", "furlough", "home", "but", "then", "there", "are", "quite", "a", "number", "leaving", "the", "army", "on", "furlough", ",", "re-enlisting", ",", "&", "going", "north", "for", "a", "while", "they", "pass", "through", "here", "quite", "largely", "Mother", ",", "Lewis", "Brown", "is", "getting", "quite", "well", ",", "he", "will", "soon", "be", "able", "to", "have", "a", "wooden", "leg", "put", "on", ",", "he", "is", "very", "restless", "&", "active", ",", "&", "wants", "to", "go", "around", "all", "the", "time", "Sam", "Beatty2", "is", "here", "in", "Washington", "We", "have", "had", "quite", "a", "snow", "storm", ",", "but", "is", "clear", "&", "sunny", "to-day", "here", ",", "but", "sloshy", ",", "I", "am", "wearing", "my", "army", "boots", "any", "thing", "but", "the", "dust", "Dear", "mother", ",", "I", "want", "to", "see", "you", "&", "Sis", ",", "&", "Mat", "&", "all", "very", "much", "if", "I", "can", "get", "a", "chance", "I", "think", "I", "shall", "come", "home", "for", "a", "while", "I", "want", "to", "try", "to", "bring", "out", "a", "book", "of", "poems", ",", "a", "new", "one", "to", "be", "called", "``", "Drum", "Taps", "''", "&", "I", "want", "to", "come", "to", "New", "York", "for", "that", "purpose", "too", "Mother", ",", "I", "hav", "n't", "given", "up", "the", "project", "of", "lecturing3", "either", "but", "whatever", "I", "do", ",", "I", "shall", "for", "the", "main", "thing", "devote", "myself", "for", "years", "to", "come", "to", "these", "wounded", "&", "sick", ",", "what", "little", "I", "can", "Well", "good", "bye", ",", "dear", "mother", ",", "for", "present", "write", "soon", "Walt"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.207126342989", "recipient": "Louisa Van Velsor Whitman", "organizations": ["lecturing3"], "sender": "Walt Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/loc.00811.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Walt Whitman to Louisa Van Velsor Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Alfred", "NNP"], ["L.", "NNP"], ["Larr", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Bush", "Yours Truly"], "money": [], "year": "1864", "locations": [], "month": "Mar", "parties": ["Alfred L. Larr", "Walt Whitman"], "properDate": "Mar 5, 1864", "gpe": [], "facility": [], "latlngs": [], "text": "   My Dear Sir I had the honor to recive the fiew lines you addressed to me, which was delivered by my particular friend Bush through whose instrumentality I am doubtless indebted for this kind and highly appreciated favor from you.2 In my humble opinion there is nothing so well calculated to inspire a soldier with new courage and fresh detirmanation and fit him for the performance of his duty under all circumstances; as the assurance that he has the sympathy and friendship of the aged, who by the infirmaties of age are rendered unfit and incapable of sharing his hard life but are ever ready and willing when occasion offers to extend a word of friendly greeting and bid him God speed Then kneed I tell you that your friendship is most cordialy accepted and mine freely and cheerfuly given in return with the hope that this partial acquaintance may ripen into a mutual attachment The preasent you sent me I received for which accept my profound thanks   With the hope of hearing from you soon I'll close Yours Truly   ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["My", "PRP$"], ["Dear", "NNP"], ["Sir", "NNP"], ["I", "NNP"], ["had", "VBD"], ["the", "DT"], ["honor", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["recive", "VB"], ["the", "DT"], ["fiew", "NN"], ["lines", "NNS"], ["you", "PRP"], ["addressed", "VBD"], ["to", "TO"], ["me", "PRP"], [",", ","], ["which", "WDT"], ["was", "VBD"], ["delivered", "VBN"], ["by", "IN"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["particular", "JJ"], ["friend", "NN"], [["Bush", "NNP"]], ["through", "IN"], ["whose", "WP$"], ["instrumentality", "NN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["doubtless", "JJ"], ["indebted", "VBN"], ["for", "IN"], ["this", "DT"], ["kind", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["highly", "RB"], ["appreciated", "VBN"], ["favor", "NN"], ["from", "IN"], ["you.2", "-NONE-"], ["In", "IN"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["humble", "JJ"], ["opinion", "NN"], ["there", "EX"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["nothing", "NN"], ["so", "RB"], ["well", "RB"], ["calculated", "VBN"], ["to", "TO"], ["inspire", "VB"], ["a", "DT"], ["soldier", "JJR"], ["with", "IN"], ["new", "JJ"], ["courage", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["fresh", "JJ"], ["detirmanation", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["fit", "NN"], ["him", "PRP"], ["for", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["performance", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["his", "PRP$"], ["duty", "NN"], ["under", "IN"], ["all", "DT"], ["circumstances", "NNS"], [";", ":"], ["as", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["assurance", "NN"], ["that", "IN"], ["he", "PRP"], ["has", "VBZ"], ["the", "DT"], ["sympathy", "JJ"], ["and", "CC"], ["friendship", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["aged", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["who", "WP"], ["by", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["infirmaties", "NNS"], ["of", "IN"], ["age", "NN"], ["are", "VBP"], ["rendered", "VBN"], ["unfit", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["incapable", "JJ"], ["of", "IN"], ["sharing", "NN"], ["his", "PRP$"], ["hard", "NN"], ["life", "NN"], ["but", "CC"], ["are", "VBP"], ["ever", "RB"], ["ready", "JJ"], ["and", "CC"], ["willing", "JJ"], ["when", "WRB"], ["occasion", "NN"], ["offers", "VBZ"], ["to", "TO"], ["extend", "VB"], ["a", "DT"], ["word", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["friendly", "JJ"], ["greeting", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["bid", "NN"], ["him", "PRP"], ["God", "NNP"], ["speed", "VBD"], ["Then", "NNP"], ["kneed", "NN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["tell", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], ["that", "IN"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["friendship", "NN"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["most", "JJS"], ["cordialy", "RB"], ["accepted", "VBN"], ["and", "CC"], ["mine", "JJ"], ["freely", "RB"], ["and", "CC"], ["cheerfuly", "RB"], ["given", "VBN"], ["in", "IN"], ["return", "NN"], ["with", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["hope", "NN"], ["that", "IN"], ["this", "DT"], ["partial", "JJ"], ["acquaintance", "NN"], ["may", "MD"], ["ripen", "VB"], ["into", "IN"], ["a", "DT"], ["mutual", "JJ"], ["attachment", "NN"], ["The", "DT"], ["preasent", "NN"], ["you", "PRP"], ["sent", "VBD"], ["me", "PRP"], ["I", "PRP"], ["received", "VBD"], ["for", "IN"], ["which", "WDT"], ["accept", "NN"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["profound", "NN"], ["thanks", "NNS"], ["With", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["hope", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["hearing", "NN"], ["from", "IN"], ["you", "PRP"], ["soon", "RB"], ["I", "PRP"], ["'ll", "MD"], ["close", "VB"], [["Yours", "NNP"], ["Truly", "NNP"]]]], "sentences": ["   My Dear Sir I had the honor to recive the fiew lines you addressed to me, which was delivered by my particular friend Bush through whose instrumentality I am doubtless indebted for this kind and highly appreciated favor from you.2 In my humble opinion there is nothing so well calculated to inspire a soldier with new courage and fresh detirmanation and fit him for the performance of his duty under all circumstances; as the assurance that he has the sympathy and friendship of the aged, who by the infirmaties of age are rendered unfit and incapable of sharing his hard life but are ever ready and willing when occasion offers to extend a word of friendly greeting and bid him God speed Then kneed I tell you that your friendship is most cordialy accepted and mine freely and cheerfuly given in return with the hope that this partial acquaintance may ripen into a mutual attachment The preasent you sent me I received for which accept my profound thanks   With the hope of hearing from you soon I'll close Yours Truly   "], "words": ["My", "Dear", "Sir", "I", "had", "the", "honor", "to", "recive", "the", "fiew", "lines", "you", "addressed", "to", "me", ",", "which", "was", "delivered", "by", "my", "particular", "friend", "Bush", "through", "whose", "instrumentality", "I", "am", "doubtless", "indebted", "for", "this", "kind", "and", "highly", "appreciated", "favor", "from", "you.2", "In", "my", "humble", "opinion", "there", "is", "nothing", "so", "well", "calculated", "to", "inspire", "a", "soldier", "with", "new", "courage", "and", "fresh", "detirmanation", "and", "fit", "him", "for", "the", "performance", "of", "his", "duty", "under", "all", "circumstances", ";", "as", "the", "assurance", "that", "he", "has", "the", "sympathy", "and", "friendship", "of", "the", "aged", ",", "who", "by", "the", "infirmaties", "of", "age", "are", "rendered", "unfit", "and", "incapable", "of", "sharing", "his", "hard", "life", "but", "are", "ever", "ready", "and", "willing", "when", "occasion", "offers", "to", "extend", "a", "word", "of", "friendly", "greeting", "and", "bid", "him", "God", "speed", "Then", "kneed", "I", "tell", "you", "that", "your", "friendship", "is", "most", "cordialy", "accepted", "and", "mine", "freely", "and", "cheerfuly", "given", "in", "return", "with", "the", "hope", "that", "this", "partial", "acquaintance", "may", "ripen", "into", "a", "mutual", "attachment", "The", "preasent", "you", "sent", "me", "I", "received", "for", "which", "accept", "my", "profound", "thanks", "With", "the", "hope", "of", "hearing", "from", "you", "soon", "I", "'ll", "close", "Yours", "Truly"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.207534339725", "recipient": "Walt Whitman", "organizations": [], "sender": "Alfred L. Larr", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/tex.00142.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Alfred L. Larr to Walt Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["George", "NNP"], ["Washington", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Louisa", "NNP"], ["Van", "NNP"], ["Velsor", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Nashville", "Tennessee", "Hotel", "George W. Whitman"], "money": [], "year": "1864", "locations": [], "month": "Mar", "parties": ["George Washington Whitman", "Louisa Van Velsor Whitman"], "properDate": "Mar 6, 1864", "gpe": ["Louisville", "Knoxville", "Walt", "Mother", "Knoxville", "Walt", "Han", "Kind"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[38.2526647, -85.7584557], [35.9606384, -83.9207392], [35.9606384, -83.9207392], [35.9606384, -83.9207392]], "text": "  Nashville Tennessee   March 6th/64 Dear Mother We arrived here last night, and will leave for Knoxville in the course of an hour or two. I am very well indeed and we have had a very pleasant trip out this far. We staid in Louisville Ky. 4 days, boarding at a first rate Hotel, and I am trying to eat enough to last me for a week or two after I get to the front. I found my trunk up at Fort Schuyler all right the morning I left home. Everything seems to be quiet just now in this Department  we are ordered to proceed to Knoxville by way of Chatanooga. I have not written to Walt since I left home but I shall write as soon as we get to our destination. Mother when you write  direct to Knoxville and when you write to Walt tell him to not wait to get a letter from me, but to let me hear from him immediately. How are you all at home  the baby you know was not well when I left, but I hope she is all right before now,  When you write to Han tell her I shall write to her Soon, and if you hear from her tell me all about her in your next letter. I must stop now as it is about time for me to get ready to start. Kind regards to all George W. Whitman", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Nashville", "NNP"]], [["Tennessee", "NNP"]], ["March", "NNP"], ["6th/64", "CD"], ["Dear", "NNP"], ["Mother", "NNP"], ["We", "NNP"], ["arrived", "VBD"], ["here", "RB"], ["last", "JJ"], ["night", "NN"], [",", ","], ["and", "CC"], ["will", "MD"], ["leave", "VB"], ["for", "IN"], [["Knoxville", "NNP"]], ["in", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["course", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["an", "DT"], ["hour", "NN"], ["or", "CC"