"'d", "your", "letter", "&", "Han", "'s", "&", "was", "glad", "indeed", "to", "get", "both", "Mother", ",", "you", "must", "not", "be", "under", "such", "apprehension", ",", "as", "I", "think", "it", "is", "not", "warranted2", "So", "far", "as", "we", "get", "news", "here", ",", "we", "are", "gaining", "the", "day", ",", "so", "far", ",", "decidedly", "if", "the", "news", "we", "hear", "is", "true", "that", "Lee", "has", "been", "repulsed", "&", "driven", "back", "by", "Grant", ",", "&", "that", "we", "are", "masters", "of", "the", "field", ",", "&", "pursuing", "them", "then", "I", "think", "Lee", "will", "retreat", ",", "south", "&", "Richmond", "will", "be", "abandoned", "by", "the", "rebs", "but", "of", "course", "time", "only", "can", "develope", "what", "will", "happen", "Mother", ",", "I", "will", "write", "again", "Wednesday", ",", "or", "before", "if", "I", "hear", "any", "thing", "to", "write", "love", "to", "Jeff", "&", "Mat", "&", "all", "Walt"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.216374269006", "recipient": "Louisa Van Velsor Whitman", "organizations": ["N", "warranted2 So"], "sender": "Walt Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/loc.00824.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Walt Whitman to Louisa Van Velsor Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Reuben", "NNP"], ["Farwell", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Dear", "Morrow Night", "Ward", "Reuben Farwell"], "money": [], "year": "1864", "locations": [], "month": "May", "parties": ["Reuben Farwell", "Walt Whitman"], "properDate": "May 10, 1864", "gpe": ["Camp", "Believe"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [], "text": "   Dear Comrad Yours received last night. and need I tell you that I am unwilling to answer yours. When there is so much stir & confusion No I will tell you that we are about to leave this Camp for better or worse To the front I suppose is the place of our destination Last Night we went to the wharf to get each a horse But I had to returne to camp with out one because there were not enough to supply us all This Morning we the Veterans or old Soldiers have to take horses & the New recruits remain in Camp We will be sent a way from here before to Morrow Night I think, which would suit me very well for I am sick of staying around this cursed place  I will try & see you before I cross the long Bridge but if I can not get a chance, I hope you will write whenever convient   Give my best respects to the Boys on Ward. A.  Believe me ever Your Friend  Reuben Farwell  I will try & write you when to the front   In hast  ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Dear", "NNP"]], [["Comrad", "NNP"], ["Yours", "NNP"]], ["received", "VBD"], ["last", "JJ"], ["night", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["and", "CC"], ["need", "VBP"], ["I", "PRP"], ["tell", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], ["that", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["unwilling", "VBG"], ["to", "TO"], ["answer", "VB"], ["yours", "NNS"], [".", "."]], [["When", "WRB"], ["there", "EX"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["so", "RB"], ["much", "RB"], ["stir", "JJ"], ["&", "CC"], ["confusion", "NN"], ["No", "DT"], ["I", "PRP"], ["will", "MD"], ["tell", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["that", "IN"], ["we", "PRP"], ["are", "VBP"], ["about", "IN"], ["to", "TO"], ["leave", "VB"], ["this", "DT"], ["Camp", "NNP"], ["for", "IN"], ["better", "JJR"], ["or", "CC"], ["worse", "JJR"], ["To", "TO"], ["the", "DT"], ["front", "NN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["suppose", "VBP"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["the", "DT"], ["place", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["our", "PRP$"], ["destination", "NN"], ["Last", "JJ"], ["Night", "NN"], ["we", "PRP"], ["went", "VBD"], ["to", "TO"], ["the", "DT"], ["wharf", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["get", "VB"], ["each", "DT"], ["a", "DT"], ["horse", "NN"], ["But", "CC"], ["I", "PRP"], ["had", "VBD"], ["to", "TO"], ["returne", "VB"], ["to", "TO"], ["camp", "VB"], ["with", "IN"], ["out", "IN"], ["one", "CD"], ["because", "IN"], ["there", "EX"], ["were", "VBD"], ["not", "RB"], ["enough", "RB"], ["to", "TO"], ["supply", "RB"], ["us", "PRP"], ["all", "DT"], ["This", "DT"], ["Morning", "NNP"], ["we", "PRP"], ["the", "DT"], ["Veterans", "NNPS"], ["or", "CC"], ["old", "JJ"], ["Soldiers", "NNS"], ["have", "VBP"], ["to", "TO"], ["take", "VB"], ["horses", "NNS"], ["&", "CC"], ["the", "DT"], [["New", "NNP"]], ["recruits", "VBZ"], ["remain", "NN"], ["in", "IN"], [["Camp", "NNP"]], ["We", "NNP"], ["will", "MD"], ["be", "VB"], ["sent", "VBN"], ["a", "DT"], ["way", "NN"], ["from", "IN"], ["here", "RB"], ["before", "IN"], ["to", "TO"], [["Morrow", "NNP"], ["Night", "NNP"]], ["I", "NNP"], ["think", "VBP"], [",", ","], ["which", "WDT"], ["would", "MD"], ["suit", "VB"], ["me", "PRP"], ["very", "RB"], ["well", "RB"], ["for", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["sick", "JJ"], ["of", "IN"], ["staying", "NN"], ["around", "IN"], ["this", "DT"], ["cursed", "VBN"], ["place", "NN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["will", "MD"], ["try", "VB"], ["&", "CC"], ["see", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["before", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["cross", "VBP"], ["the", "DT"], ["long", "JJ"], ["Bridge", "NNP"], ["but", "CC"], ["if", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["can", "MD"], ["not", "RB"], ["get", "VB"], ["a", "DT"], ["chance", "NN"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["hope", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], ["will", "MD"], ["write", "VB"], ["whenever", "RB"], ["convient", "JJ"], ["Give", "NNP"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["best", "JJS"], ["respects", "NNS"], ["to", "TO"], ["the", "DT"], [["Boys", "NNP"]], ["on", "IN"], [["Ward", "NNP"]], [".", "."]], [["A", "DT"], [".", "."]], [[["Believe", "NNP"]], ["me", "PRP"], ["ever", "RB"], ["Your", "PRP$"], ["Friend", "NNP"], [["Reuben", "NNP"], ["Farwell", "NNP"]], ["I", "NNP"], ["will", "MD"], ["try", "VB"], ["&", "CC"], ["write", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["when", "WRB"], ["to", "TO"], ["the", "DT"], ["front", "NN"], ["In", "IN"], ["hast", "NN"]]], "sentences": ["   Dear Comrad Yours received last night.", "and need I tell you that I am unwilling to answer yours.", "When there is so much stir & confusion No I will tell you that we are about to leave this Camp for better or worse To the front I suppose is the place of our destination Last Night we went to the wharf to get each a horse But I had to returne to camp with out one because there were not enough to supply us all This Morning we the Veterans or old Soldiers have to take horses & the New recruits remain in Camp We will be sent a way from here before to Morrow Night I think, which would suit me very well for I am sick of staying around this cursed place  I will try & see you before I cross the long Bridge but if I can not get a chance, I hope you will write whenever convient   Give my best respects to the Boys on Ward.", "A.", "Believe me ever Your Friend  Reuben Farwell  I will try & write you when to the front   In hast  "], "words": ["Dear", "Comrad", "Yours", "received", "last", "night.", "and", "need", "I", "tell", "you", "that", "I", "am", "unwilling", "to", "answer", "yours.", "When", "there", "is", "so", "much", "stir", "&", "confusion", "No", "I", "will", "tell", "you", "that", "we", "are", "about", "to", "leave", "this", "Camp", "for", "better", "or", "worse", "To", "the", "front", "I", "suppose", "is", "the", "place", "of", "our", "destination", "Last", "Night", "we", "went", "to", "the", "wharf", "to", "get", "each", "a", "horse", "But", "I", "had", "to", "returne", "to", "camp", "with", "out", "one", "because", "there", "were", "not", "enough", "to", "supply", "us", "all", "This", "Morning", "we", "the", "Veterans", "or", "old", "Soldiers", "have", "to", "take", "horses", "&", "the", "New", "recruits", "remain", "in", "Camp", "We", "will", "be", "sent", "a", "way", "from", "here", "before", "to", "Morrow", "Night", "I", "think", ",", "which", "would", "suit", "me", "very", "well", "for", "I", "am", "sick", "of", "staying", "around", "this", "cursed", "place", "I", "will", "try", "&", "see", "you", "before", "I", "cross", "the", "long", "Bridge", "but", "if", "I", "can", "not", "get", "a", "chance", ",", "I", "hope", "you", "will", "write", "whenever", "convient", "Give", "my", "best", "respects", "to", "the", "Boys", "on", "Ward.", "A.", "Believe", "me", "ever", "Your", "Friend", "Reuben", "Farwell", "I", "will", "try", "&", "write", "you", "when", "to", "the", "front", "In", "hast"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.216510267918", "recipient": "Walt Whitman", "organizations": ["Comrad Yours", "New", "Boys"], "sender": "Reuben Farwell", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/duk.00370.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Reuben Farwell to Walt Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Louisa", "NNP"], ["Van", "NNP"], ["Velsor", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Dearest Mother", "Meade", "Richmond", "Mother", "George", "Walt Mother", "Jeff", "Oscar Cunningham"], "money": [], "year": "1864", "locations": [], "month": "May", "parties": ["Walt Whitman", "Louisa Van Velsor Whitman"], "properDate": "May 10, 1864", "gpe": ["Washington", "Richmond", "Fredericksburgh", "Washington"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[38.8951118, -77.0363658], [37.5407246, -77.4360481], [38.8951118, -77.0363658]], "text": "  Washington |  May 10 '64 (\u00bd past 2 | p m)  Dearest Mother, There is nothing perhaps more than you see in the N Y papers   the fighting down in the field on the 6th I think ended in our favor, though with pretty severe losses to some of our divisions   the fighting is about 70 miles from here & 50 from Richmond   on the 7th & 8th followed up by the rebel army hauling off, they say retreating, & Meade pursuing   it is quite mixed yet, but I guess we have the best of it   if we really have, Richmond is a goner, for they cannot do any better than they have done   how much the 9th corps was in the fight, & where, I cannot tell yet, but from the wounded I have seen I dont think that corps was deeply in   I have seen 300 wounded, they came in last night, I asked for men of 9th corps, but could not find any at all   these 300 men were not badly wounded, mostly in arms, hands, trunk of body, &c.   they could all walk, though some had an awful time of it   they had to fight their way, with the worst in the middle, out of the region of Fredericksburgh, & so on where they could get across the Rappahannock & get where they found transportation to Washington   the gov't has decided (or rather Gen Meade has) to occupy Fredericksburgh,1 for depot & hospitals   (I think that a first rate decision)   so the wounded men will receive quick attention & surgery, instead of being racked through the long journey up here   still may come in here   Mother, my impression is that we have no great reason for alarm or sadness about George so far   of course I know nothing   Well good by, dearest mother, Walt    Mother, I wrote you yesterday too   tell dear brother Jeff to write me   love to Mat   the poor diarrhea man2 died, & it was a boon   Oscar Cunningham, 82d Ohio, has had a relapse, I fear it is going bad with him   lung diseases are quite plenty   night before last I staid in hospital all night tending a poor fellow   it has been awful hot here   milder to-day    ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Washington", "NNP"]], ["|", ":"], ["May", "NNP"], ["10", "CD"], ["'64", "-NONE-"], ["(", ":"], ["\u00bd", ":"], ["past", "JJ"], ["2", "CD"], ["|", "CD"], ["p", "NN"], ["m", "NN"], [")", ":"], [["Dearest", "NNP"], ["Mother", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["There", "EX"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["nothing", "NN"], ["perhaps", "RB"], ["more", "RBR"], ["than", "IN"], ["you", "PRP"], ["see", "VBP"], ["in", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], [["N", "NNP"]], ["Y", "NNP"], ["papers", "NNS"], ["the", "DT"], ["fighting", "VBG"], ["down", "RP"], ["in", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["field", "NN"]