erness", "Fredericksburgh", "Wilderness"], "sender": "Walt Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/loc.00833.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Walt Whitman to Louisa Van Velsor Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Reuben", "NNP"], ["Farwell", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Dear", "Armory Square Hospital"], "money": [], "year": "1864", "locations": [], "month": "Jun", "parties": ["Reuben Farwell", "Walt Whitman"], "properDate": "Jun 8, 1864", "gpe": ["Woodwurth"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[48.21474509999999, -101.5805256]], "text": " Dear Friend I once promised to write you & as often as convient So far I have fullfulled my part. Since my joineing My Regiment It has been nothing but marching & fighting the Johnnys. I can say that we are enough for them if not too much There has not been a fight but what they have been worsted Our Cavalry forces have started on an other raid of 10 days rations I left the Regiment last Monday. The reason of my leaveing was because I could not see to ride or walk. I was poisioned how or in what manner I can not tell. I will write to you as often as possible Even if it is pencil marks I hope that this may find you enjoying good health    Give my respects to the inmates of Ward. A, of Armory Square Hospital & tell Thom. Woodwurth that I would be very glad to hear from him. I will close by hopeing to see you before long   ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Dear", "NNP"]], ["Friend", "NNP"], ["I", "NNP"], ["once", "RB"], ["promised", "VBD"], ["to", "TO"], ["write", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["&", "CC"], ["as", "IN"], ["often", "RB"], ["as", "IN"], ["convient", "NN"], ["So", "NNP"], ["far", "RB"], ["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["fullfulled", "VBN"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["part", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["Since", "IN"], ["my", "PRP$"], [