 "sender": "Hannah Heyde", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/loc.01001.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Hannah Heyde to Walt Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["William", "NNP"], ["E.", "NNP"], ["Babcock", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Poplar Grove Church Va", "Whitman", "Dear Sir", "Soon", "Soon", "William"], "money": [], "year": "1864", "locations": [], "month": "Oct", "parties": ["William E. Babcock", "Walt Whitman"], "properDate": "Oct 18, 1864", "gpe": ["Us"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [], "text": "  Headquarters 51st N.YVNear Poplar Grove Church Va October 18th 1864  Walt. Whitman Dear Sir Your Letter came to hand this morning and I hasten to answer the Same. Your Brothers Effects will be Sent forward to Your Mothers address, Soon as we can get a permit from the Provost Marshall General, which I have this day Sent a request for. I was much pleased to hear from him and the rest of the Officers that were taken prisoners with him. And I know they were neither wounded nor killed, as we had no chance of hearing from them until your Letter Arrived. Every thing is quiet with Us and no news. So I will bring this to a close, by requesting you to write Soon.  Yours &c. William E Babcock1st Lieut 51 N.YV  P.S. Letters from You will at all Times be received & Answered with pleasureWE Babcock  ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["Headquarters", "NNS"], ["51st", "CD"], ["N.YVNear", "JJ"], [["Poplar", "NNP"], ["Grove", "NNP"], ["Church", "NNP"], ["Va", "NNP"]], ["October", "NNP"], ["18th", "CD"], ["1864", "CD"], ["Walt", "NNP"], [".", "."]], [[["Whitman", "NNP"]], [["Dear", "NNP"], ["Sir", "NNP"]], ["Your", "NNP"], ["Letter", "NNP"], ["came", "VBD"], ["to", "TO"], ["hand", "VB"], ["this", "DT"], ["morning", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["I", "PRP"], ["hasten", "VBP"], ["to