 "recipient": "Walt Whitman", "organizations": [], "sender": "Peter Eckler", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/loc.00853.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Peter Eckler to Walt Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Peter", "NNP"], ["Eckler", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Mr. Whitman", "Old Theater", "Eckler"], "money": [], "year": "1865", "locations": [], "month": "Apr", "parties": ["Peter Eckler", "Walt Whitman"], "properDate": "Apr 26, 1865", "gpe": ["New York", "Washington", "Beckman", "Johnston"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[40.7143528, -74.00597309999999], [38.8951118, -77.0363658], [41.8205199, -71.51261699999999]], "text": "  New York April 22, 1865  Mr. Whitman Your book is now to proofs & will be ready for the Binder next Monday morning. As there was nothing done yesterday & the day before on account of the funeral, my waiting for your reply did not retard the book much. Alvords foreman promises to do a good job & I hope he will [illegible] I sent you record of [illegible] page Mr Belts [illegible] Send you a copy as soon as published & another copy to Congressional Library of Washington. What will complete your copyright   His office is in Beckman [01   in Johnston's ?] Old Theater.  Respectfully P. Eckler  ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["New", "NNP"], ["York", "NNP"]], ["April", "NNP"], ["22", "CD"], [",", ","], ["1865", "CD"], [["Mr.", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["Your", "NNP"], ["book", "NN"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["now", "RB"], ["to", "TO"], ["proofs", "NNS"], ["&", "CC"], ["will", "MD"], ["be", "VB"], ["ready", "RB"], ["for", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], [["Binder", "NNP"]], ["next", "JJ"], ["Monday", "NNP"], ["morning", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["As", "IN"], ["there", "EX"], ["was", "VBD"], ["nothing", "NN"], ["done", "NN"], ["yesterday", "NN"], ["&", "C