o", "RB"], ["Col.", "NNP"], ["Wright", "NNP"], ["Tuesday", "NNP"], ["night", "NN"], ["they", "PRP"], ["said", "VBD"], ["they", "PRP"], ["all", "DT"], ["have", "VBP"], ["pleasant", "JJ"], ["quarters", "NNS"], ["over", "IN"], ["there", "EX"], [".", "."]], [[["Dear", "NNP"]], ["brother", "NN"], [["Jeff", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["was", "VBD"], ["very", "RB"], ["sorry", "JJ"], ["you", "PRP"], ["was", "VBD"], ["n't", "RB"], ["able", "JJ"], ["to", "TO"], ["come", "VB"], ["on", "IN"], ["to", "TO"], ["see", "VB"], ["the", "DT"], ["Review", "NNP"], ["we", "PRP"], ["had", "VBD"], ["perfect", "VBN"], ["weather", "NN"], ["&", "CC"], ["every", "DT"], ["thing", "NN"], ["just", "RB"], ["as", "IN"], ["it", "PRP"], ["should", "MD"], ["be", "VB"], ["the", "DT"], ["streets", "NNS"], ["now", "RB"], ["are", "VBP"], ["full", "JJ"], ["of", "IN"], ["soldiers", "NNS"], ["scattered", "VBN"], ["around", "IN"], ["loose", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["as", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["armies", "NNS"], ["are", "VBP"], ["in", "IN"], ["camp", "NN"], ["near", "IN"], ["here", "RB"], [",", ","], ["getting", "VBG"], ["ready", "RB"], ["to", "TO"], ["be", "VB"], ["mustered", "VBN"], ["out", "RP"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["quite", "RB"], ["well", "RB"], ["&", "CC"], ["visit", "NN"], ["the", "DT"], ["Hospitals", "NNS"], ["the", "DT"], ["same", "JJ"], [".", "."]], [[["Mother", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["you", "PRP"], ["did", "VBD"], ["n't", "RB"], ["write", "VB"], ["whether", "IN"], ["you", "PRP"], ["got", "VBD"], ["the", "DT"], ["package", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["5", "CD"], ["Drum-Taps", "NNS"], ["I", "PRP"], ["keep", "VBP"], ["thinking", "VBG"], ["about", "IN"], ["you", "PRP"], ["every", "DT"], ["few", "JJ"], ["minutes", "NNS"], ["all", "DT"], ["day", "NN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["wish", "VBP"], ["I", "PRP"], ["was", "VBD"], ["home", "RB"], ["a", "DT"], ["couple", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["days", "NNS"], [["Jeff", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["you", "PRP"], ["will", "MD"], ["take", "VB"], ["this", "DT"], ["acc't", "JJ"], ["of", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], [["Review", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["same", "JJ"], ["as", "IN"], ["if", "IN"], ["it", "PRP"], ["was", "VBD"], ["written", "VBN"], ["to", "TO"], ["you", "PRP"], [".", "."]], [[["Walt", "NNP"]]]], "sentences": ["  Indian Bureau, basement of Patent Office.", "house 468 M st 2d door west of 12th Washington, Thursday, May 25, '65  Dear Mother, I received your letter of the 22d   I feel uneasy about you all the time, & hope I shall get a letter to-day, & find you have recovered.", "Well, the Review is over, & it was very grand   it was too much & too impressive, to be described   but you will see a good deal about it in the papers.", "If you can imagine a great wide avenue like Flatbush avenue, quite flat, & stretching as far as you can see, with a great white building half as big as fort Greene on a hill at the commencement of the avenue, & then through this avenue marching solid ranks of soldiers, 20 or 25 abreast, just marching steady all day long for two days, without intermission, one regiment after another, real war-worn soldiers, that have been marching & fighting for years   sometimes for an hour nothing but cavalry, just solid ranks, on good horses, with sabres glistening, & carbines hanging by their saddles, & their clothes showing hard service, but they mostly all good-looking hardy young men   then great masses of guns, batteries of cannon, four or six abreast, each drawn by six horses, with the gunners seated on the ammunition wagons   & these perhaps a long while in passing, nothing but batteries   (it seemed as if all the cannon in the world were here)   then great battalions of blacks, with axes & shovels & pick axes, (real southern darkies, black as tar)   then again hour after hour the old infantry regiments, the men all sunburnt   nearly every one with some old tatter all in shreds, (that had been a costly & beautiful flag)   the great drum corps of sixty or eighty drummers massed at the heads of the brigades, playing away   now and then a fine brass band   but oftener nothing but the drums & whistling fifes   but they sounded very lively   (perhaps a band of sixty drums & fifteen or twenty fifes playing \"Lannigan's ball\")   the different corps banners, the generals with their staffs &c   the Western Army, led by Gen. Sherman,1 (old Bill, the soldiers all call him)   well, dear mother, that is a brief sketch, give you some idea of the great panorama of the Armies that have been passing through here the last two days.", "I saw the President several times, stood close by him, & took a good look at him   & like his expression much   he is very plain & substantial   it seemed wonderful that just that plain middling-sized ordinary man, dressed in black, without the least badge or ornament, should be the master of all these myriads of soldiers, the best that ever trod the earth, with forty or fifty Major-Generals, around him or riding by, with their broad yellow-satin belts around their waists   and of all the artillery & cavalry   to say nothing of all the Forts & Ships, &c, &c. I saw Gen. Grant too several times   He is the noblest Roman of them all   none of the pictures do justice to him   about sundown I saw him again riding on a large fine horse, with his hat off in answer to the hurrahs   he rode by where I stood, & I saw him well, as he rode by on a slow canter, with nothing but a single orderly after him   He looks like a good man   (& I believe there is much in looks)   I saw Gen. Meade, Gen. Thomas,2 Secretary Stanton, & lots of other celebrated government officers & generals   but the rank & file was the greatest sight of all.", "The 51st was in the line Tuesday with the 9th Corps.", "I saw George, but did not get a chance to speak to him.", "He is well.", "George is now Major George W. Whitman3   has been commissioned & mustered in.", "(Col. Wright4 & Col. Shephard5 have done it, I think.", ") The 51st is over to the Old Convalescent camp, between here and Alexandria, doing provost duty.", "It (the old camp) is now called Augur General Hospital.", "If you should write direct, Major G. W. Whitman | 51st New York V. V. | on provost duty at | Augur Gen'l Hospital | near Alexandria | Va.", "It is thought that the 51st will not be mustered out for the present   It is thought the Government will retain the re-enlisted veteran regiments, such as the 51st   If that is so, George will remain as he is for the summer, or most of it   The reason I havn't seen him is, I knew they had left provost duty in the Prince st. prison, but didn't know where they had gone till Tuesday   I saw Capt.", "Caldwell6 Tuesday, also Col. Wright Tuesday night   they said they all have pleasant quarters over there.", "Dear brother Jeff, I was very sorry you wasn't able to come on to see the Review   we had perfect weather & every thing just as it should be   the streets now are full of soldiers scattered around loose, as the armies are in camp near here, getting ready to be mustered out.", "I am quite well & visit the Hospitals the same.", "Mother, you didn't write whether you got the package of 5 Drum-Taps   I keep thinking about you every few minutes all day   I wish I was home a couple of days   Jeff, you will take this acc't of the Review, same as if it was written to you.", "Walt "], "words": ["Indian", "Bureau", ",", "basement", "of", "Patent", "Office.", "house", "468", "M", "st", "2d", "door", "west", "of", "12th", "Washington", ",", "Thursday", ",", "May", "25", ",", "'65", "Dear", "Mother", ",", "I", "received", "your", "letter", "of", "the", "22d", "I", "feel", "uneasy", "about", "you", "all", "the", "time", ",", "&", "hope", "I", "shall", "get", "a", "letter", "to-day", ",", "&", "find", "you", "have", "recovered.", "Well", ",", "the", "Review", "is", "over", ",", "&", "it", "was", "very", "grand", "it", "was", "too", "much", "&", "too", "impressive", ",", "to", "be", "described", "but", "you", "will", "see", "a", "good", "deal", "about", "it", "in", "the", "papers.", "If", "you", "can", "imagine", "a", "great", "wide", "avenue", "like", "Flatbush", "avenue", ",", "quite", "flat", ",", "&", "stretching", "as", "far", "as", "you", "can", "see", ",", "with", "a", "great", "white", "building", "half", "as", "big", "as", "fort", "Greene", "on", "a", "hill", "at", "the", "commencement", "of", "the", "avenue", ",", "&", "then", "through", "this", "avenue", "marching", "solid", "ranks", "of", "soldiers", ",", "20", "or", "25", "abreast", ",", "just", "marching", "steady", "all", "day", "long", "for", "two", "days", ",", "without", "intermission", ",", "one", "regiment", "after", "another", ",", "real", "war-worn", "soldiers", ",", "that", "have", "been", "marching", "&", "fighting", "for", "years", "sometimes", "for", "an", "hour", "nothing", "but", "cavalry", ",", "just", "solid", "ranks", ",", "on", "good", "horses", ",", "with", "sabres", "glistening", ",", "&", "carbines", "hanging", "by", "their", "saddles", ",", "&", "their", "clothes", "showing", "hard", "service", ",", "but", "they", "mostly", "all", "good-looking", "hardy", "young", "men", "then", "great", "masses", "of", "guns", ",", "batteries", "of", "cannon", ",", "four", "or", "six", "abreast", ",", "each", "drawn", "by", "six", "horses", ",", "with", "the", "gunners", "seated", "on", "the", "ammunition", "wagons", "&", "these", "perhaps", "a", "long", "while", "in", "passing", ",", "nothing", "but", "batteries", "(", "it", "seemed", "as", "if", "all", "the", "cannon", "in", "the", "world", "were", "here", ")", "then", "great", "battalions", "of", "blacks", ",", "with", "axes", "&", "shovels", "&", "pick", "axes", ",", "(", "real", "southern", "darkies", ",", "black", "as", "tar", ")", "then", "again", "hour", "after", "hour", "the", "old", "infantry", "regiments", ",", "the", "men", "all", "sunburnt", "nearly", "every", "one", "with", "some", "old", "tatter", "all", "in", "shreds", ",", "(", "that", "had", "been", "a", "costly", "&", "beautiful", "flag", ")", "the", "great", "drum", "corps", "of", "sixty", "or", "eighty", "drummers", "massed", "at", "the", "heads", "of", "the", "brigades", ",", "playing", "away", "now", "and", "then", "a", "fine", "brass", "band", "but", "oftener", "nothing", "but", "the", "drums", "&", "whistling", "fifes", "but", "they", "sounded", "very", "lively", "(", "perhaps", "a", "band", "of", "sixty", "drums", "&", "fifteen", "or", "twenty", "fifes", "playing", "``", "Lannigan", "'s", "ball", "''", ")", "the", "different", "corps", "banners", ",", "the", "generals", "with", "their", "staffs", "&", "c", "the", "Western", "Army", ",", "led", "by", "Gen.", "Sherman,1", "(", "old", "Bill", ",", "the", "soldiers", "all", "call", "him", ")", "well", ",", "dear", "mother", ",", "that", "is", "a", "brief", "sketch", ",", "give", "you", "some", "idea", "of", "the", "great", "panorama", "of", "the", "Armies", "that", "have", "been", "passing", "through", "here", "the", "last", "two", "days.", "I", "saw", "the", "President", "several", "times", ",", "stood", "close", "by", "him", ",", "&", "took", "a", "good", "look", "at", "him", "&", "like", "his", "expression", "much", "he", "is", "very", "plain", "&", "substantial", "it", "seemed", "wonderful", "that", "just", "that", "plain", "middling-sized", "ordinary", "man", ",", "dressed", "in", "black", ",", "without", "the", "least", "badge", "or", "ornament", ",", "should", "be", "the", "master", "of", "all", "these", "myriads", "of", "soldiers", ",", "the", "best", "that", "ever", "trod", "the", "earth", ",", "with", "forty", "or", "fifty", "Major-Generals", ",", "around", "him", "or", "riding", "by", ",", "with", "their", "broad", "yellow-satin", "belts", "around", "their", "waists", "and", "of", "all", "the", "artillery", "&", "cavalry", "to", "say", "nothing", "of", "all", "the", "Forts", "&", "Ships", ",", "&", "c", ",", "&", "c.", "I", "saw", "Gen.", "Grant", "too", "several", "times", "He", "is", "the", "noblest", "Roman", "of", "them", "all", "none", "of", "the", "pictures", "do", "justice", "to", "him", "about", "sundown", "I", "saw", "him", "again", "riding", "on", "a", "large", "fine", "horse", ",", "with", "his", "hat", "off", "in", "answer", "to", "the", "hurrahs", "he", "rode", "by", "where", "I", "stood", ",", "&", "I", "saw", "him", "well", ",", "as", "he", "rode", "by", "on", "a", "slow", "canter", ",", "with", "nothing", "but", "a", "single", "orderly", "after", "him", "He", "looks", "like", "a", "good", "man", "(", "&", "I", "believe", "there", "is", "much", "in", "looks", ")", "I", "saw", "Gen.", "Meade", ",", "Gen.", "Thomas,2", "Secretary", "Stanton", ",", "&", "lots", "of", "other", "celebrated", "government", "officers", "&", "generals", "but", "the", "rank", "&", "file", "was", "the", "greatest", "sight", "of", "all.", "The", "51st", "was", "in", "the", "line", "Tuesday", "with", "the", "9th", "Corps.", "I", "saw", "George", ",", "but", "did", "not", "get", "a", "chance", "to", "speak", "to", "him.", "He", "is", "well.", "George", "is", "now", "Major", "George", "W.", "Whitman3", "has", "been", "commissioned", "&", "mustered", "in.", "(", "Col.", "Wright4", "&", "Col.", "Shephard5", "have", "done", "it", ",", "I", "think.", ")", "The", "51st", "is", "over", "to", "the", "Old", "Convalescent", "camp", ",", "between", "here", "and", "Alexandria", ",", "doing", "provost", "duty.", "It", "(", "the", "old", "camp", ")", "is", "now", "called", "Augur", "General", "Hospital.", "If", "you", "should", "write", "direct", ",", "Major", "G.", "W.", "Whitman", "|", "51st", "New", "York", "V.", "V.", "|", "on", "provost", "duty", "at", "|", "Augur", "Gen'l", "Hospital", "|", "near", "Alexandria", "|", "Va.", "It", "is", "thought", "that", "the", "51st", "will", "not", "be", "mustered", "out", "for", "the", "present", "It", "is", "thought", "the", "Government", "will", "retain", "the", "re-enlisted", "veteran", "regiments", ",", "such", "as", "the", "51st", "If", "that", "is", "so", ",", "George", "will", "remain", "as", "he", "is", "for", "the", "summer", ",", "or", "most", "of", "it", "The", "reason", "I", "hav", "n't", "seen", "him", "is", ",", "I", "knew", "they", "had", "left", "provost", "duty", "in", "the", "Prince", "st.", "prison", ",", "but", "did", "n't", "know", "where", "they", "had", "gone", "till", "Tuesday", "I", "saw", "Capt.", "Caldwell6", "Tuesday", ",", "also", "Col.", "Wright", "Tuesday", "night", "they", "said", "they", "all", "have", "pleasant", "quarters", "over", "there.", "Dear", "brother", "Jeff", ",", "I", "was", "very", "sorry", "you", "was", "n't", "able", "to", "come", "on", "to", "see", "the", "Review", "we", "had", "perfect", "weather", "&", "every", "thing", "just", "as", "it", "should", "be", "the", "streets", "now", "are", "full", "of", "soldiers", "scattered", "around", "loose", ",", "as", "the", "armies", "are", "in", "camp", "near", "here", ",", "getting", "ready", "to", "be", "mustered", "out.", "I", "am", "quite", "well", "&", "visit", "the", "Hospitals", "the", "same.", "Mother", ",", "you", "did", "n't", "write", "whether", "you", "got", "the", "package", "of", "5", "Drum-Taps", "I", "keep", "thinking", "about", "you", "every", "few", "minutes", "all", "day", "I", "wish", "I", "was", "home", "a", "couple", "of", "days", "Jeff", ",", "you", "will", "take", "this", "acc't", "of", "the", "Review", ",", "same", "as", "if", "it", "was", "written", "to", "you.", "Walt"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.268189854481", "recipient": "Louisa Van Velsor Whitman", "organizations": ["Review", "Flatbush", "Armies", "Whitman3", "Old", "Hospital", "Prince", "Caldwell6"], "sender": "Walt Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/wwh.00008.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Walt Whitman to Louisa Van Velsor Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Milford", "NNP"], ["C.", "NNP"], ["Reed", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Mr.", "Whitman Sir", "Book"], "money": [], "year": "1865", "locations": [], "month": "May", "parties": ["Milford C. Reed", "Walt Whitman"], "properDate": "May 26, 1865", "gpe": ["Washington", "Write"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[38.8951118, -77.0363658]], "text": "   Mr. Whitman Sir I am in great trouble again and of course must write to you about it.  I was in Washington the 2nd and I went to No 34 4 \u00bd Street and pawned my Watch a good American Lever, for $22.07 which I was to pay within a month but I was robbed of my pocket Book which contained a receipt which he gave me for the wach  now I want you to go there if you will and see the man (I dont know his name) and if the thief has not already been there and got the wach I want you to tell him not to let any one have it on that receipt.  I will soon be there myself and redeem it for I am going to be discharged within a few days when I will come and see you.  You will confer a great favor on me by going at once to see about it.  I would like to have the fellow arrested if he should bring the ticket for the Wach for I had another Stole from me at the same time.  Write to me as soon as you find out about the Wach for I am very anxious about it.  I dont want to loose both Waches  I have written this in a great hurry.  write to me soon from your good friend It is No 34 4 \u00bd St.   ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Mr.", "NNP"]], [["Whitman", "NNP"], ["Sir", "NNP"]], ["I", "NNP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["in", "IN"], ["great", "JJ"], ["trouble", "NN"], ["again", "RB"], ["and", "CC"], ["of", "IN"], ["course", "NN"], ["must", "MD"], ["write", "VB"], ["to", "TO"], ["you", "PRP"], ["about", "IN"], ["it", "PRP"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["was", "VBD"], ["in", "IN"], [["Washington", "NNP"]], ["the", "DT"], ["2nd", "CD"], ["and", "CC"], ["I", "PRP"], ["went", "VBD"], ["to", "TO"], ["No", "DT"], ["34", "CD"], ["4", "CD"], ["\u00bd"