ter", "to", "the", "young", "ones", "that", "sent", "you", "the", "money", "through", "Lane2", "they", "are", "all", "awfully", "disappointed", "they", "are", "all", "little", "girls", "of", "8", "and", "12", "years", "old", "(", "some", "even", "younger", ")", "and", "have", "been", "speculating", "what", "they", "should", "do", "with", "the", "letter", "which", "one", "it", "would", "be", "directed", "to", "&", "c", "at", "last", "they", "settled", "it", "by", "agreeing", "that", "each", "one", "should", "have", "the", "letter", "for", "a", "week", "at", "a", "time", "in", "regular", "order", "they", "have", "called", "to", "see", "Mr", "Lane", "several", "times", "to", "see", "if", "it", "had", "been", "received", "They", "of", "course", "are", "too", "young", "to", "know", "that", "the", "great", "point", "was", "to", "give", "it", "and", "of", "course", "look", "for", "the", "praise", "that", "is", "usually", "bestowed.", "Did", "Lane", "explain", "to", "you", "that", "they", "were", "the", "children", "of", "the", "people", "that", "sent", "you", "money", "last", "winter", "a", "year", "ago", "Durkee", "'s", ",", "Crany", ",", "Lanes", "&", "c", "&", "c3", "they", "remembered", "hearing", "your", "letters", "read", "to", "their", "fathers", "and", "mothers", ",", "and", "heard", "a", "great", "deal", "of", "talk", "about", "the", "great", "good", "you", "could", "do", "with", "even", "a", "few", "dollars", "This", "fair", "they", "got", "up", "entirely", "among", "themselves", "and", "resolved", "in", "solumn", "conclave", "(", "after", "voting", "down", "resolutions", "to", "give", "to", "the", "Sanitary", "Com.", "Christian", "Com", ",", "&", "c", "&", "c", ")", "to", "send", "the", "money", "to", "you", "to", "be", "spent", "&", "c", "Mattie", "and", "the", "children", "are", "very", "well", "I", "am", "writing", "this", "at", "the", "office", "with", "Hattie", "at", "my", "side", "she", "wants", "to", "send", "a", "kiss", "to", "Uncle", "Walt", "We", "do", "not", "hear", "from", "George", "I", "wonder", "why", "he", "do", "n't", "write", "I", "wish", "he", "would", "Mother", "gets", "very", "down", "hearted", "and", "a", "letter", "cheers", "her", "up", "wonderfully", "you", "must", "write", "her", "as", "often", "as", "you", "can", "too", "all", "send", "their", "love", "affectionately", "Jeff"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.269549843601", "recipient": "Walt Whitman", "organizations": ["yesterday1", "Mothers", "Lane", "Sanitary Com", "Com"], "sender": "Thomas Jefferson Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/loc.00439.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Thomas Jefferson Whitman to Walt Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["John", "NNP"], ["Swinton", "NNP"]], ["(", "NNP"], ["?", "."]], [[")", "NN"], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Walt"], "money": [], "year": "1865", "locations": [], "month": "Jun", "parties": ["Walt Whitman", "John Swinton"], "properDate": "Jun 9, 1865", "gpe": ["Washington", "Farewell"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[38.8951118, -77.0363658]], "text": "  Washington |  June 9, 1865.  My dear friend, The Homer2 has come & is now lying before me. I thank you deeply. I am very well, this summer, & go to the Hospitals daily & nightly   as I find a greater proportion of sad cases than ever   & for some reason or other there are few or no visitors. I enjoy my visits with a sad but profound joy & satisfaction   especially at night, when the light is nearly turned off, & I am soothing some suffering one. I send you, same mail with this, two copies of the little book Drum-Taps. Farewell. Walt Whitman3 ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Washington", "NNP"]], ["|", ":"], ["June", "NNP"], ["9", "CD"], [",", ","], ["1865", "CD"], [".", "."]], [["My", "PRP$"], ["dear", "NN"], ["friend", "NN"], [",", ","], [["The", "NNP"]], [["Homer2", "NNP"]], ["has", "VBZ"], ["come", "VBN"], ["&", "CC"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["now", "RB"], ["lying", "VBG"], ["before", "IN"], ["me", "PRP"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["thank", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], ["deeply", "RB"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["very", "RB"], ["well", "RB"], [",", ","], ["this", "DT"], ["summer", "NN"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["go", "VB"], ["to", "TO"], ["the", "DT"], [["Hospitals", "NNS"]], ["daily", "RB"], ["&", "CC"], ["nightly", "RB"], ["as", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["find", "VBP"], ["a", "DT"], ["greater", "JJR"], ["proportion", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["sad", "JJ"], ["cases", "NNS"], ["than", "IN"], ["ever", "RB"], ["&", "CC"], ["for", "IN"], ["some", "DT"], ["reason", "NN"], ["or", "CC"], ["other", "JJ"], ["there", "EX"], ["are", "VBP"], ["few", "JJ"], ["or", "CC"], ["no", "DT"], ["visitors", "NNS"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["enjoy", "VBP"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["visits", "NNS"], ["with", "IN"], ["a", "DT"], ["sad", "JJ"], ["but", "CC"], ["profound", "NN"], ["joy", "NN"], ["&", "CC"], ["satisfaction", "NN"], ["especially", "RB"], ["at", "IN"], ["night", "NN"], [",", ","], ["when", "WRB"], ["the", "DT"], ["light", "NN"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["nearly", "RB"], ["turned", "VBN"], ["off", "RP"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["soothing", "VBG"], ["some", "DT"], ["suffering", "NN"], ["one", "CD"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["send", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], [",", ","], ["same", "JJ"], ["mail", "NN"], ["with", "IN"], ["this", "DT"], [",", ","], ["two", "CD"], ["copies", "NNS"], ["of", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["little", "JJ"], ["book", "NN"], ["Drum-Taps", "NNS"], [".", "."]], [[["Farewell", "NNP"]], [".", "."]], [[["Walt", "NNP"]], [["Whitman3", "NNP"]]]], "sentences": ["  Washington |  June 9, 1865.", "My dear friend, The Homer2 has come & is now lying before me.", "I thank you deeply.", "I am very well, this summer, & go to the Hospitals daily & nightly   as I find a greater proportion of sad cases than ever   & for some reason or other there are few or no visitors.", "I enjoy my visits with a sad but profound joy & satisfaction   especially at night, when the light is nearly turned off, & I am soothing some suffering one.", "I send you, same mail with this, two copies of the little book Drum-Taps.", "Farewell.", "Walt Whitman3 "], "words": ["Washington", "|", "June", "9", ",", "1865.", "My", "dear", "friend", ",", "The", "Homer2", "has", "come", "&", "is", "now", "lying", "before", "me.", "I", "thank", "you", "deeply.", "I", "am", "very", "well", ",", "this", "summer", ",", "&", "go", "to", "the", "Hospitals", "daily", "&", "nightly", "as", "I", "find", "a", "greater", "proportion", "of", "sad", "cases", "than", "ever", "&", "for", "some", "reason", "or", "other", "there", "are", "few", "or", "no", "visitors.", "I", "enjoy", "my", "visits", "with", "a", "sad", "but", "profound", "joy", "&", "satisfaction", "especially", "at", "night", ",", "when", "the", "light", "is", "nearly", "turned", "off", ",", "&", "I", "am", "soothing", "some", "suffering", "one.", "I", "send", "you", ",", "same", "mail", "with", "this", ",", "two", "copies", "of", "the", "little", "book", "Drum-Taps.", "Farewell.", "Walt", "Whitman3"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.270229838161", "recipient": "John Swinton", "organizations": ["The", "Homer2", "Hospitals", "Whitman3"], "sender": "Walt Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/med.00312.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Walt Whitman to John Swinton ( ? ) ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], ["N.", "NNP"], ["M.", "NNP"], ["and", "CC"], [["John", "NNP"], ["B.", "NNP"], ["Pratt", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Alfred", "Sherman", "Alfred", "Armory Square Hospital", "Walt"], "money": [], "year": "1865", "locations": ["Western Armies"], "month": "Jun", "parties": ["Walt Whitman", "John B. Pratt"], "properDate": "Jun 10, 1865", "gpe": ["Washington", "Alfred", "Poor", "Alfred", "Write", "Direct", "Washington"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[38.8951118, -77.0363658], [44.3257819, -84.7687579], [44.3257819, -84.7687579], [38.8951118, -77.0363658], [39.3270677, -79.2802633], [48.21474509999999, -101.5805256]], "text": "  Washington |  June 10, 1865.  Mr. & Mrs. Pratt: As I am visiting your son Alfred occasionally, to cheer him up in his sickness in hospital, I thought you might like a few words, though from a stranger, yet a friend to your boy. I was there last night, and sat a while by the bed, as usual, & he showed me the letter he had just received from home. He wrote to you yesterday. He has had diarrhea pretty bad, but is now improved & goes about the hospital   but as the weather is pretty hot & powerful in the midst of the day, I advised him not to go outdoors much at present. What he wants most is rest, and a chance to get his strength again. I expect he will improve by degrees, & I hope it will not be very long before he will be sent home   though I don't know, as I am only a friend, occasionally visiting the hospitals. Alfred has good accommodations where he is, & a good doctor, & nursing   so you must not worry about him. I shall stop & see him a little every day, as he likes to have me, & I like him too. Poor young men, there are hundreds & thousands of them here, wounded or sick, in the great army hospitals   many of them suffering with amputations & wounds   others with sickness, & so faint & weak, this weather   it is enough to make one's heart bleed    As to Alfred, he is comparatively well off, there are so many with bad wounds &c.   the deaths are quite frequent. He will soon be restored, according to present appearances. We are having very hot weather here, & it is dry & dusty   The City is alive with soldiers from both the Army of the Potomac & the Western Armies, brought here by Sherman. There have been some great Reviews here, as you have seen in the papers   & thousands of soldiers are going home every day. You must write to Alfred often, as it cheers up a boy sick & away from home. Write all about domestic & farm incidents, and as cheerful as may be. Direct to him, in Ward C, Armory Square Hospital, Washington, D. C. Should any thing occur, I will write you again, but I feel confident he will continue doing well. For the present farewell. Walt WhitmanWashington | D C ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Washington", "NNP"]], ["|", ":"], ["June", "NNP"], ["10", "CD"], [",", ","], ["1865", "CD"], [".", "."]], [["Mr.", "NNP"], ["&", "CC"], ["Mrs.", "NNP"], ["Pratt", "NNP"], [":", ":"], ["As", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["visiting", "VBG"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["son", "NN"], [["Alfred", "NNP"]], ["occasionally", "RB"], [",", ","], ["to", "TO"], ["cheer", "VB"], ["him", "PRP"], ["up", "RP"], ["in", "IN"], ["his", "PRP$"], ["sickness", "NN"], ["in", "IN"], ["hospital", "NN"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["thought", "VBD"], ["you", "PRP"], ["might", "MD"], ["like", "VB"], ["a", "DT"], ["few", "JJ"], ["words", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["though", "IN"], ["from", "IN"], ["a", "DT"], ["stranger", "NN"], [",", ","], ["yet", "CC"], ["a", "DT"], ["friend", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["boy", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["was", "VBD"], ["there", "RB"], ["last", "JJ"], ["night", "NN"], [",", ","], ["and", "CC"], ["sat", "VB"], ["a", "DT"], ["while", "NN"], ["by", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["bed", "VBN"], [",", ","], ["as", "IN"], ["usual", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["he", "PRP"], ["showed", "VBD"], ["me", "PRP"], ["the", "DT"], ["letter", "NN"], ["he", "PRP"], ["had", "VBD"], ["just", "RB"], ["received", "VBN"], ["from", "IN"], ["home", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["He", "PRP"], ["wrote", "VBD"], ["to", "TO"], ["you", "PRP"], ["yesterday", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["He", "PRP"], ["has", "VBZ"], ["had", "VBN"], ["diarrhea", "NN"], ["pretty", "RB"],