after", "IN"], ["all", "DT"], [".", "."]], [["But", "CC"], ["you", "PRP"], ["shall", "MD"], ["have", "VB"], ["a", "DT"], ["larger", "JJR"], ["&", "CC"], ["better", "JJR"], ["one", "CD"], [",", ","], ["dear", "JJ"], ["son", "NN"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["will", "MD"], ["have", "VB"], ["it", "PRP"], ["prepared", "VBN"], ["&", "CC"], ["fix", "CD"], ["some", "DT"], ["way", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["send", "VB"], ["it", "PRP"], ["to", "TO"], ["you", "PRP"], [".", "."]], [["They", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["commenced", "VBN"], ["breaking", "VBG"], ["up", "RP"], [["Armory", "NNP"], ["Square", "NNP"]], [".", "."]], [["The", "DT"], ["picture", "NN"], ["in", "IN"], ["shirt", "NN"], ["sleeves", "NNS"], ["was", "VBD"], ["taken", "VBN"], ["in", "IN"], ["1854", "CD"], ["You", "PRP"], ["would", "MD"], ["not", "RB"], ["know", "VB"], ["it", "PRP"], ["was", "VBD"], ["me", "PRP"], ["now", "RB"], [",", ","], ["but", "CC"], ["it", "PRP"], ["was", "VBD"], ["taken", "VBN"], ["from", "IN"], ["life", "NN"], ["&", "CC"], ["was", "VBD"], ["first-rate", "JJ"], ["then", "RB"], [".", "."]], [[["Anson", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["when", "WRB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["write", "VBP"], ["tell", "RB"], ["me", "PRP"], ["all", "DT"], ["particulars", "NNS"], ["of", "IN"], ["yourself", "PRP"], [",", ","], ["folk", "VBP"], ["'s", "POS"], ["place", "NN"], ["&", "CC"], ["about", "IN"], [["Wood", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["c.", "NNP"], ["Your", "NNP"], ["true", "NN"], ["friend", "NN"], [",", ","], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]]]], "sentences": ["  ATTORNEY GENERAL'S OFFICE, Washington Aug. 15, 1865  Dear Anson, As there is a sort of lull and quiet for a short time in my work, I will improve the opportunity to write to you, dear friend.1 In this office, I am in the part where the Pardons are attended to.", "There is a perfect stream of Rebels coming in here all the time to get pardoned.", "All the Southerners that are worth more than $20,000 in property, have to get special pardons, & all who have been officers of the rank of Brig.", "Gen'l, or upwards, the same.", "Many old men come in here, and middle-aged & young ones too.", "I often talk with them.", "There are some real characters among them   (& you know I have a fancy for any thing a little out of the usual style)    Quite a good many women come up to Washington, & come to this office, about their pardons   some old, some young   all are drest in deep black.", "Then there are bushels of applications arriving every week by mail.", "When they are recommended by the Provisional Governors, or some well known Union person, they get their papers   Many have got their papers   but nearly all are waiting for the President's signature   I should think 3 or 4 000.", "He is n't in any hurry to sign them.", "I was down at Armory Square Sunday.", "Dr. Smith said he had rec'd a letter from you, & was just going to answer it.2 I went awhile in Ward I, among the rebels   they are in a wretched condition, & nobody goes among them.", "I shall go in & see Hiram in a day or so.", "I am in good health, & generally have easy times   As half the force of clerks here are off on leave, I some days have a pressure   & that is the case lately.", "But I shall be careful to make it up.", "We have pleasanter weather here the last ten days   quite cool mornings & nights.", "My dear friend; I am sorry you could not have been with me for a day or two before you left Washington, as it may be we shall not meet again.", "But you must not forget me, for I shall not you.", "Write to me from time to time, Anson, & I will you too.", "The picture you shall have   As I am writing this at the office, otherwise I would enclose one of the card photographs in it   they are up at my room   I will send one in my next.3 Write how your leg is   Give my best remembrances to Wood   he is a good man & I hope he will prosper through life   When you write, direct to me, Attorney General's Office, Washington, D. C. Blue coats here are getting quite scarce.", "Your letter of 9th came safe, & was welcome.", "I envy you the pure fresh country air & healthy influences, & I doubt not, fine scenery & quiet.", "When you write tell me  Walt Whitman   Wednesday morning, 16th Aug.  Anson, as I neglected to send this yesterday, I have brought down a couple of little pictures & enclose them, after all.", "But you shall have a larger & better one, dear son,   I will have it prepared & fix some way to send it to you.", "They have commenced breaking up Armory Square.", "The picture in shirt sleeves was taken in 1854   You would not know it was me now, but it was taken from life & was first-rate then.", "Anson, when you write tell me all particulars of yourself, folk's place & about Wood, &c.  Your true friend, Walt Whitman  "], "words": ["ATTORNEY", "GENERAL", "'S", "OFFICE", ",", "Washington", "Aug.", "15", ",", "1865", "Dear", "Anson", ",", "As", "there", "is", "a", "sort", "of", "lull", "and", "quiet", "for", "a", "short", "time", "in", "my", "work", ",", "I", "will", "improve", "the", "opportunity", "to", "write", "to", "you", ",", "dear", "friend.1", "In", "this", "office", ",", "I", "am", "in", "the", "part", "where", "the", "Pardons", "are", "attended", "to.", "There", "is", "a", "perfect", "stream", "of", "Rebels", "coming", "in", "here", "all", "the", "time", "to", "get", "pardoned.", "All", "the", "Southerners", "that", "are", "worth", "more", "than", "$", "20,000", "in", "property", ",", "have", "to", "get", "special", "pardons", ",", "&", "all", "who", "have", "been", "officers", "of", "the", "rank", "of", "Brig.", "Gen'l", ",", "or", "upwards", ",", "the", "same.", "Many", "old", "men", "come", "in", "here", ",", "and", "middle-aged", "&", "young", "ones", "too.", "I", "often", "talk", "with", "them.", "There", "are", "some", "real", "characters", "among", "them", "(", "&", "you", "know", "I", "have", "a", "fancy", "for", "any", "thing", "a", "little", "out", "of", "the", "usual", "style", ")", "Quite", "a", "good", "many", "women", "come", "up", "to", "Washington", ",", "&", "come", "to", "this", "office", ",", "about", "their", "pardons", "some", "old", ",", "some", "young", "all", "are", "drest", "in", "deep", "black.", "Then", "there", "are", "bushels", "of", "applications", "arriving", "every", "week", "by", "mail.", "When", "they", "are", "recommended", "by", "the", "Provisional", "Governors", ",", "or", "some", "well", "known", "Union", "person", ",", "they", "get", "their", "papers", "Many", "have", "got", "their", "papers", "but", "nearly", "all", "are", "waiting", "for", "the", "President", "'s", "signature", "I", "should", "think", "3", "or", "4", "000.", "He", "is", "n't", "in", "any", "hurry", "to", "sign", "them.", "I", "was", "down", "at", "Armory", "Square", "Sunday.", "Dr.", "Smith", "said", "he", "had", "rec", "'d", "a", "letter", "from", "you", ",", "&", "was", "just", "going", "to", "answer", "it.2", "I", "went", "awhile", "in", "Ward", "I", ",", "among", "the", "rebels", "they", "are", "in", "a", "wretched", "condition", ",", "&", "nobody", "goes", "among", "them.", "I", "shall", "go", "in", "&", "see", "Hiram", "in", "a", "day", "or", "so.", "I", "am", "in", "good", "health", ",", "&", "generally", "have", "easy", "times", "As", "half", "the", "force", "of", "clerks", "here", "are", "off", "on", "leave", ",", "I", "some", "days", "have", "a", "pressure", "&", "that", "is", "the", "case", "lately.", "But", "I", "shall", "be", "careful", "to", "make", "it", "up.", "We", "have", "pleasanter", "weather", "here", "the", "last", "ten", "days", "quite", "cool", "mornings", "&", "nights.", "My", "dear", "friend", ";", "I", "am", "sorry", "you", "could", "not", "have", "been", "with", "me", "for", "a", "day", "or", "two", "before", "you", "left", "Washington", ",", "as", "it", "may", "be", "we", "shall", "not", "meet", "again.", "But", "you", "must", "not", "forget", "me", ",", "for", "I", "shall", "not", "you.", "Write", "to", "me", "from", "time", "to", "time", ",", "Anson", ",", "&", "I", "will", "you", "too.", "The", "picture", "you", "shall", "have", "As", "I", "am", "writing", "this", "at", "the", "office", ",", "otherwise", "I", "would", "enclose", "one", "of", "the", "card", "photographs", "in", "it", "they", "are", "up", "at", "my", "room", "I", "will", "send", "one", "in", "my", "next.3", "Write", "how", "your", "leg", "is", "Give", "my", "best", "remembrances", "to", "Wood", "he", "is", "a", "good", "man", "&", "I", "hope", "he", "will", "prosper", "through", "life", "When", "you", "write", ",", "direct", "to", "me", ",", "Attorney", "General", "'s", "Office", ",", "Washington", ",", "D.", "C.", "Blue", "coats", "here", "are", "getting", "quite", "scarce.", "Your", "letter", "of", "9th", "came", "safe", ",", "&", "was", "welcome.", "I", "envy", "you", "the", "pure", "fresh", "country", "air", "&", "healthy", "influences", ",", "&", "I", "doubt", "not", ",", "fine", "scenery", "&", "quiet.", "When", "you", "write", "tell", "me", "Walt", "Whitman", "Wednesday", "morning", ",", "16th", "Aug.", "Anson", ",", "as", "I", "neglected", "to", "send", "this", "yesterday", ",", "I", "have", "brought", "down", "a", "couple", "of", "little", "pictures", "&", "enclose", "them", ",", "after", "all.", "But", "you", "shall", "have", "a", "larger", "&", "better", "one", ",", "dear", "son", ",", "I", "will", "have", "it", "prepared", "&", "fix", "some", "way", "to", "send", "it", "to", "you.", "They", "have", "commenced", "breaking", "up", "Armory", "Square.", "The", "picture", "in", "shirt", "sleeves", "was", "taken", "in", "1854", "You", "would", "not", "know", "it", "was", "me", "now", ",", "but", "it", "was", "taken", "from", "life", "&", "was", "first-rate", "then.", "Anson", ",", "when", "you", "write", "tell", "me", "all", "particulars", "of", "yourself", ",", "folk", "'s", "place", "&", "about", "Wood", ",", "&", "c.", "Your", "true", "friend", ",", "Walt", "Whitman"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.277437780498", "recipient": "Anson Ryder", "organizations": ["GENERAL", "Pardons", "Provisional", "Armory Square", "Ward"], "sender": "Walt Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/pri.00023.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Walt Whitman to Anson Ryder , Jr. ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Alfred", "NNP"], ["Pratt", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Walt", "Whitman Dear", "Ward", "Pleas"], "money": [], "year": "1865", "locations": [], "month": "Aug", "parties": ["Alfred Pratt", "Walt Whitman"], "properDate": "Aug 7, 1865", "gpe": ["Washington", "Washington"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[38.8951118, -77.0363658], [38.8951118, -77.0363658]], "text": "   Walt Whitman Dear Friend I am now at my own home but hav not got my discharge yet. I left Washington on trans furr to rochester. I have to go back to rochester to get my discharge. the day that I left thare went to the patent ofice to see you but you was not thare. and I had not time to go whare you was but, went back to Ward C and gave to no. 6 thare in the ward 70 cts to give to you he said that he would let you have it the first time that you come in. now pleas rite and let me know if you got it. I wanted to see you I would like to no if you got that money anyhow. I got home two weeks ago last friday. but I find myself rather weak yet  last friday I was on a lode of hay and went to down of from it and I fell and scard the horses one of them kicked me on the forehead and then they start to run and the wagon wheel struck me on the back of my head and hurt me bad but can sit up now. I think of no more at present. Pleas rite if you get this address.   My friends their respects Please if get this rite and if you will Please to sennd me that potographs of Abe and Washington like yours if you can find them I will pay you for it.  ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Walt", "NNP"]], [["Whitman", "NNP"], ["Dear", "NNP"]], ["Friend", "NNP"], ["I", "NNP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["now", "RB"], ["at", "IN"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["own", "JJ"], ["home", "NN"], ["but", "CC"], ["hav", "NN"], ["not", "RB"], ["got", "VBD"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["discharge", "NN"], ["yet", "RB"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["left", "VBD"], [["Washington", "NNP"]], ["on", "IN"], ["trans", "NNS"], ["furr", "VBP"], ["to", "TO"], ["rochester", "VB"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["to", "TO"], ["go", "VB"], ["back", "RB"], ["to", "TO"], ["rochester", "VB"], ["to", "TO"], ["get", "VB"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["discharge", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["the", "DT"], ["day", "NN"], ["that", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["left", "VBD"], ["thare", "JJ"], ["went", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["the", "DT"], ["patent", "NN"], ["ofice", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["see", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["but", "CC"], ["you", "PRP"], ["was", "VBD"], ["not", "RB"], ["thare", "JJ"], [".", "."]], [["and", "CC"], ["I", "PRP"], ["had", "VBD"], ["not", "RB"], ["time", "VB"], ["to", "TO"], ["go", "VB"], ["whare", "NN"], ["you", "PRP"], ["was", "VBD"], ["but", "CC"], [",", ","], ["went", "VBD"], ["back", "RB"], ["to", "TO"], [["Ward", "NNP"]], ["C", "NNP"], ["and", "CC"], ["gave", "VBD"], ["to", "TO"], ["no", "DT"], [".", "."]], [["6", "CD"], ["thare", "NN"], ["in", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["ward", "NN"], ["70", "CD"], ["cts", "NNS"], ["to", "TO"], ["give", "VB"], ["to", "TO"], ["you", "PRP"], ["he", "PRP"], ["said", "VBD"], ["that", "IN"], ["he", "PRP"], ["would", "MD"], ["let", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["have", "VB"], ["it", "PRP"], ["the", "DT"], ["first", "JJ"], ["time", "NN"], ["that", "WDT"], ["you", "PRP"], ["come", "VBP"], ["in", "IN"], [".", "."]], [["now", "RB"], ["pleas", "VBD"], ["rite", "JJ"], ["and", "CC"], ["let", "VB"], ["me", "PRP"], ["know", "VB"], ["if", "IN"], ["you", "PRP"], ["got", "VBD"], ["it", "PRP"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["wanted", "VBD"], ["to", "TO"], ["see", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["I", "PRP"], ["would", "MD"], ["like", "VB"], ["to", "TO"], ["no", "DT"], ["if", "IN"], ["you", "PRP"], ["got", "VBD"], ["that", "IN"], ["money", "NN"], ["anyhow", "WRB"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["got", "VBD"], ["home", "NN"], ["two", "CD"], ["weeks", "NNS"], ["ago", "IN"], ["last", "JJ"], ["friday", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["but", "CC"], ["I", "PRP"], ["find", "VBP"], ["myself", "PRP"], ["rather", "RB"], ["weak", "JJ"], ["yet", "RB"], ["last", "JJ"], ["friday", "NN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["was", "VBD"], ["on", "IN"], ["a", "DT"], ["lode", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["hay", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["went", "VBD"], ["to", "TO"], ["down", "VB"], ["of", "IN"], ["from", "IN"], ["it", "PRP"], ["and", "CC"], ["I", "PRP"], ["fell", "VBD"], ["and", "CC"], ["scard", "NN"], ["the", "DT"], ["horses", "NNS"], ["one", "CD"], ["of", "IN"], ["them", "PRP"], ["kicked", "VBD"], ["me", "PRP"], ["on", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["forehead", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["then", "RB"], ["they", "PRP"], ["start", "VBP"], ["to", "TO"], ["run", "VB"], ["and", "CC"], ["the", "DT"], ["wagon", "NN"], ["wheel", "NN"], ["struck", "NN"], ["me", "PRP"], ["on", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["back", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["head", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["hurt", "VBN"], ["me", "PRP"], ["bad", "JJ"], ["but", "CC"], ["can", "MD"], ["sit", "VB"], ["up", "RP"], ["now", "RB"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["think", "VBP"], ["of", "IN"], ["no", "DT"], ["more", "RBR"], ["at", "IN"], ["present", "NN"], [".", "."]], [[["Pleas", "NNP"]], ["rite", "VBD"], ["if", "IN"], ["you", "PRP"], ["get", "VBP"], ["this", "DT"], ["address", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["My", "PRP$"], ["friends", "NNS"], ["their", "PRP$"], ["respects", "NNS"], ["Please", "NNP"], ["if", "IN"], ["get", "NN"], ["this", "DT"], ["rite", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["if", "IN"], ["you", "PRP"], ["will", "MD"], ["Please", "VB"], ["to", "TO"], ["sennd", "VB"], ["me", "PRP"], ["that", "IN"], ["potographs", "NNS"], ["of", "IN"], [["Abe", "NNP"]], ["and", "CC"], [["Washington", "NNP"]], ["like", "IN"], ["yours", "NNS"], ["if", "IN"], ["you", "PRP"], ["can", "MD"], ["find", "VB"], ["them", "PRP"], ["I", "PRP"], ["will", "MD"], ["pay", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["for", "IN"], ["it", "PRP"], [".", "."]]], "sentences": ["   Walt Whitman Dear Friend I am now at my own home but hav not got my discharge yet.", "I left Washington on trans furr to rochester.", "I have to go back to rochester to get my discharge.", "the day that I left thare went to the patent ofice to see you but you was not thare.", "and I had not time to go whare you was but, went back to Ward C and gave to no.", "6 thare in the ward 70 cts to give to you he said that he would let you have it the first time that you come in.", "now pleas rite and let me know if you got it.", "I wanted to see you I would like to no if you got that money anyhow.", "I got home two weeks ago last friday.", "but I find myself rather weak yet  last friday I was on a lode of hay and went to down of from it and I fell and scard the horses one of them kicked me on the forehead and then they start to run and the wagon wheel struck me on the back of my head and hurt me bad but can sit up now.", "I think of no more at present.", "Pleas rite if you get this address.", "My friends their respects Please if get this rite and if you will Please to sennd me that potographs of Abe and Washington like yours if you can find them I will pay you for it.  "], "words": ["Walt", "Whitman", "Dear", "Friend", "I", "am", "now", "at", "my", "own", "home", "but", "hav", "not", "got", "my", "discharge", "yet.", "I", "left", "Washington", "on", "trans", "furr", "to", "rochester.", "I", "have", "to", "go", "back", "to", "rochester", "to", "get", "my", "discharge.", "the", "day", "that", "I", "left", "thare", "went", "to", "the", "patent", "ofice", "to", "see", "you", "but", "you", "was", "not", "thare.", "and", "I", "had", "not", "time", "to", "go", "whare", "you", "was", "but", ",", "went", "back", "to", "Ward", "C", "and", "gave", "to", "no.", "6", "thare", "in", "the", "ward", "70", "cts", "to", "give", "to", "you", "he", "said", "that", "he", "would", "let", "you", "have", "it", "the", "first", "time", "that", "you", "come", "in.", "now", "pleas", "rite", "and", "let", "me", "know", "if", "you", "got", "it.", "I", "wanted", "to", "see", "you", "I", "would", "like", "to", "no", "if", "you", "got", "that", "money", "anyhow.", "I", "got", "home", "two", "weeks", "ago", "last", "friday.", "but", "I", "find", "myself", "rather", "weak", "yet", "last", "friday", "I", "was", "on", "a", "lode", "of", "hay", "and", "went", "to", "down", "of", "from", "it", "and", "I", "fell", "and", "scard", "the", "horses", "one", "of", "them", "kicked", "me", "on", "the", "forehead", "and", "then", "they", "start", "to", "run", "and", "the", "wagon", "wheel", "struck", "me", "on", "the", "back", "of", "my", "head", "and", "hurt", "me", "bad", "but", "can", "sit", "up", "now.", "I", "think", "of", "no", "more", "at", "present.", "Pleas", "rite", "if", "you", "get", "this", "address.", "My", "friends", "their", "respects", "Please", "if", "get", "this", "rite", "and", "if", "you", "will", "Please", "to", "sennd", "me", "that", "potographs", "of", "Abe", "and", "Washington", "like", "yours", "if", "you", "can", "find", "them", "I", "will", "pay", "you", "for", "it", "."], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.27825377397", "recipient": "Walt Whitman", "organizations": ["Abe"], "sender": "Alfred Pratt", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/loc.00606.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Alfred Pratt to Walt Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Anson", "NNP"], ["Ryder", "NNP"]], ["Jr.", "NNP"], ["to", "TO"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Friend W", "Yours", "Anson Ryder", "Jun"], "money": [], "year": "1865", "locations": [], "month": "Aug", "parties": ["Anson Ryder", "Walt Whitman"], "properDate": "Aug 9, 1865", "gpe": ["Washington", "Wood", "Fraser"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[38.8951118, -77.0363658], [39.2154345, -81.47183869999999], [42.539202, -82.9493652]], "text": "   Friend W, I feel as though I ought to apologize to you for leaving Washington in the manner I did but I had so very little time to spare I did not have time to say good by to anybody scarcely but do not think for a moment that I forgot you then or now. Wood is with [me] here at my old home says it is not very natural here does not seem at all like an hospital. The weather here is splendid so cool and nice and real pure country air. I wish you could see us and be with us for a time. I think it would do you good. And now I must ask you about that photograph you promised me so long ago. I have never seen it yet, please do not let me have occasion to doubt your word though I think you agred to write me if I wrote you if you cannot (but I hope you can) please let Fraser have one for me and he will send it for I have written him.2   Please excuse haste, Yours with much love,  Anson Ryder, Jun.  ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Friend", "NN"], ["W", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["feel", "VBP"], ["as", "IN"], ["though", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["ought", "MD"], ["to", "TO"], ["apologize", "VB"], ["to", "TO"], ["you", "PRP"], ["for", "IN"], ["leaving", "VBG"], [["Washington", "NNP"]], ["in", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["manner", "NN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["did", "VBD"], ["but", "CC"], ["I", "PRP"], ["had", "VBD"], ["so", "RB"], ["very", "RB"], ["little", "JJ"], ["time", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["spare", "VB"], ["I", "PRP"], ["did", "VBD"], ["not", "RB"], ["have", "VB"], ["time", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["say", "VB"], ["good", "JJ"], ["by", "IN"], ["to", "TO"], ["anybody", "NN"], ["scarcely", "RB"], ["but", "CC"], ["do", "VBP"], ["not", "RB"], ["think", "VB"], ["for", "IN"], ["a", "DT"], ["moment", "NN"], ["that", "WDT"], ["I", "PRP"], ["forgot", "VBD"], ["you", "PRP"], ["then", "RB"], ["or", "CC"], ["now", "RB"], [".", "."]], [[["Wood", "NNP"]], ["is", "VBZ"], ["with", "IN"], ["[", "CD"], ["me", "PRP"], ["]", ":"], ["here", "RB"], ["at", "IN"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["old", "JJ"], ["home", "NN"], ["says", "VBZ"], ["it", "PRP"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["not", "RB"], ["very", "RB"], ["natural", "JJ"], ["here", "RB"], ["does", "VBZ"], ["not", "RB"], ["seem", "VB"], ["at", "IN"], ["all", "DT"], ["like", "IN"], ["an", "DT"], ["hospital", "JJ"], [".", "."]], [["The", "DT"], ["weather", "NN"], ["here", "RB"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["splendid", "VBN"], ["so", "RB"], ["cool", "JJ"], ["and", "CC"], ["nice", "JJ"], ["and", "CC"], ["real", "JJ"], ["pure", "NN"], ["country", "NN"], ["air", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["wish", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], ["could", "MD"], ["see", "VB"], ["us", "PRP"], ["and", "CC"], ["be", "VB"], ["with", "IN"], ["us", "PRP"], ["for", "IN"], ["a", "DT"], ["time", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["think", "VBP"], ["it", "PRP"], ["would", "MD"], ["do", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["good", "VB"], [".", "."]], [["And", "CC"], ["now", "RB"], ["I", "PRP"], ["must", "MD"], ["ask", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["about", "IN"], ["that", "DT"], ["photograph", "NN"], ["you", "PRP"], ["promised", "VBD"], ["me", "PRP"], ["so", "RB"], ["long", "RB"], ["ago", "RB"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["never", "RB"], ["seen", "VBN"], ["it", "PRP"], ["yet", "RB"], [",", ","], ["please", "VB"], ["do", "VBP"], ["not", "RB"], ["let", "VB"], ["me", "PRP"], ["have", "VB"], ["occasion", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["doubt", "VB"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["word", "NN"], ["though", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["think", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], ["agred", "VBD"], ["to", "TO"], ["write", "VB"], ["me", "PRP"], ["if", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["wrote", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], ["if", "IN"], ["you", "PRP"], ["can", "MD"], ["not", "RB"], ["(", "VB"], ["but", "CC"], ["I", "PRP"], ["hope", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], ["can", "MD"], [")", "VB"], ["please", "VB"], ["let", "JJ"], [["Fraser", "NNP"]], ["have", "VBP"], ["one", "CD"], ["for", "IN"], ["me", "PRP"], ["and", "CC"], ["he", "PRP"], ["will", "MD"], ["send", "VB"], ["it", "PRP"], ["for", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["written", "VBN"], ["him.2", "-NONE-"], ["Please", "NNP"], ["excuse", "NN"], ["haste", "NN"], [",", ","], [["Yours", "NNP"]], ["with", "IN"], ["much", "JJ"], ["love", "NN"], [",", ","], [["Anson", "NNP"], ["Ryder", "NNP"]], [",", ","], [["Jun", "NNP"]], [".", "."]]], "sentences": ["   Friend W, I feel as though I ought to apologize to you for leaving Washington in the manner I did but I had so very little time to spare I did not have time to say good by to anybody scarcely but do not think for a moment that I forgot you then or now.", "Wood is with [me] here at my old home says it is not very natural here does not seem at all like an hospital.", "The weather here is splendid so cool and nice and real pure country air.", "I wish you could see us and be with us for a time.", "I think it would do you good.", "And now I must ask you about that photograph you promised me so long ago.", "I have never seen it yet, please do not let me have occasion to doubt your word though I think you agred to write me if I wrote you if you cannot (but I hope you can) please let Fraser have one for me and he will send it for I have written him.2   Please excuse haste, Yours with much love,  Anson Ryder, Jun.  "], "words": ["Friend", "W", ",", "I", "feel", "as", "though", "I", "ought", "to", "apologize", "to", "you", "for", "leaving", "Washington", "in", "the", "manner", "I", "did", "but", "I", "had", "so", "very", "little", "time", "to", "spare", "I", "did", "not", "have", "time", "to", "say", "good", "by", "to", "anybody", "scarcely", "but", "do", "not", "think", "for", "a", "moment", "that", "I", "forgot", "you", "then", "or", "now.", "Wood", "is", "with", "[", "me", "]", "here", "at", "my", "old", "home", "says", "it", "is", "not", "very", "natural", "here", "does", "not", "seem", "at", "all", "like", "an", "hospital.", "The", "weather", "here", "is", "splendid", "so", "cool", "and", "nice", "and", "real", "pure", "country", "air.", "I", "wish", "you", "could", "see", "us", "and", "be", "with", "us", "for", "a", "time.", "I", "think", "it", "would", "do", "you", "good.", "And", "now", "I", "must", "ask", "you", "about", "that", "photograph", "you", "promised", "me", "so", "long", "ago.", "I", "have", "never", "seen", "it", "yet", ",", "please", "do", "not", "let", "me", "have", "occasion", "to", "doubt", "your", "word", "though", "I", "think", "you", "agred", "to", "write", "me", "if", "I", "wrote", "you", "if", "you", "can", "not", "(", "but", "I", "hope", "you", "can", ")", "please", "let", "Fraser", "have", "one", "for", "me", "and", "he", "will", "send", "it", "for", "I", "have", "written", "him.2", "Please", "excuse", "haste", ",", "Yours", "with", "much", "love", ",", "Anson", "Ryder", ",", "Jun", "."], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.278525771794", "recipient": "Walt Whitman", "organizations": [], "sender": "Anson Ryder", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/loc.00607.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Anson Ryder Jr. to Walt Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["William", "NNP"], ["F.", "NNP"], ["Bainbridge", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Esteemed Freind", "Recived", "Camp Grant"], "money": [], "year": "1865", "locations": [], "month": "Aug", "parties": ["William F. Bainbridge", "Walt Whitman"], "properDate": "Aug 23, 1865", "gpe": ["Freind"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [], "text": " My Dear & Esteemed Freind I take the present opporutnity to write you these few lines to inform you that i am well and in good health at Present time and i truly hope when these few lines reach you that they may find you enjoying good health. i answered your last letter1 and not having recivd any answer i think it very Strange i recived these two pictures and give one to wilson,2 and kept one my self and i was very glad to recive them for i would rather see your face than your picture at all wilson wrote the same time that i did and not having Recived any answer and wilson says he can not think What the reason is that he does not get and answer from you. Me and wilson expecty to come through there this fall and we will come and see you if ever you have the opportunity of calling around richmond please to call around Camp Grant and see us. please excuse this Short Letter Write soon good by I remain your Freind   ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["My", "PRP$"], ["Dear", "NNP"], ["&", "CC"], [["Esteemed", "NNP"], ["Freind", "NNP"]], ["I", "NNP"], ["take", "VBP"], ["the", "DT"], ["present", "NN"], ["opporutnity", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["write", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["these", "DT"], ["few", "JJ"], ["lines", "NNS"], ["to", "TO"], ["inform", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["that", "IN"], ["i", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["well", "RB"], ["and", "CC"], ["in", "IN"], ["good", "JJ"], ["health", "NN"], ["at", "IN"], ["Present", "NNP"], ["time", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["i", "PRP"], ["truly", "RB"], ["hope", "VBP"], ["when", "WRB"], ["these", "DT"], ["few", "JJ"], ["lines", "NNS"], ["reach", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], ["that", "IN"], ["they", "PRP"], ["may", "MD"], ["find", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["enjoying", "VBG"], ["good", "JJ"], ["health", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["i", "PRP"], ["answered", "VBD"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["last", "JJ"], [["letter1", "NNP"]], ["and", "CC"], ["not", "RB"], ["having", "VBG"], ["recivd", "NN"], ["any", "DT"], ["answer", "NN"], ["i", "PRP"], ["think", "VBP"], ["it", "PRP"], ["very", "RB"], ["Strange", "NNP"], ["i", "PRP"], ["recived", "VBD"], ["these", "DT"], ["two", "CD"], ["pictures", "NNS"], ["and", "CC"], ["give", "VB"], ["one", "CD"], ["to", "TO"], ["wilson,2", "-NONE-"], ["and", "CC"], ["kept",