"you", "]", "heard", "any", "thing", "lately", "from", "Han", "?", "1", "I", "write", "to", "her", "every", "now", "&", "then", "It", "is", "very", "pleasant", "weather", "here", ",", "quite", "cool", "to-day", "Good", "by", ",", "dear", "mother", ",", "Walt", "."], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.316333469332", "recipient": "Louisa Van Velsor Whitman", "organizations": ["GENERAL", "Quarter Master", "Volunteer Army"], "sender": "Walt Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/nyp.00207.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Walt Whitman to Louisa Van Velsor Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Anson", "NNP"], ["Ryder", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["Jr.", "NNP"], [",", ","]]], "people": [], "money": [], "year": "1866", "locations": [], "month": "May", "parties": ["Walt Whitman", "Anson Ryder"], "properDate": "May 16, 1866", "gpe": ["Well", "German"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[34.162526, -112.8507374]], "text": " . . . As to me, I lead rather a dull life here. I wish you were nearer, that we might be together frequently. I do not associate much with the department clerks, yet many appear to be good fellows enough. The contest between Congress and the President is quite exciting. I go up to the Capitol and listen to the speeches and arguments. Sometimes I feel as if one side had the best of it and then the other. Well, my dear comrade, I believe I have told you all the news   of Eicholtz,2 the German sergeant with the bad compound fracture, of Frazee3 and Dr. Smith.4 ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[".", "."]], [[".", "."]], [[".", "."]], [["As", "IN"], ["to", "TO"], ["me", "PRP"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["lead", "VBP"], ["rather", "RB"], ["a", "DT"], ["dull", "NN"], ["life", "NN"], ["here", "RB"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["wish", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], ["were", "