rom Walt Whitman to Louisa Van Velsor Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["John", "NNP"], ["Burroughs", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["John", "John", "Marine Band", "Walt"], "money": [], "year": "1866", "locations": [], "month": "Jul", "parties": ["Walt Whitman", "John Burroughs"], "properDate": "Jul 2, 1866", "gpe": ["Virginia", "New York"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[37.4315734, -78.6568942], [40.7143528, -74.00597309999999]], "text": " I went up to your house this morning and took a look at the garden   Everything growing first rate   potatoes, tomatoes, corn, cabbages, and all   I guess upon the whole the garden never looked better at this time of year. We have had opportune rains   I inquired about the cow, and received a favorable report. . . . John, about coming, I am not able to say anything decisive in this letter. . . . Up in your Bureau all seems to go on as usual . . . John, I send you the July Atlantic.2 . . . I am feeling hearty and in good spirits   go around more than usual   go to such doings as base-ball matches and the music Performances in the Public grounds   Marine Band, etc. . . . I hope your parents are well   I wish you to give them my love   tho' I don't know them, I hope to one of these days   remember me to the wife, also. I am writing this by my window in the office   the breeze is blowing moderate, and the view down the river and off along Virginia hills opposite is most delightful   the pardon clerks are middling busy   I have plenty of leisure, as usual   I spent yesterday afternoon at the Hospital, and took tea in the evening at O'Connor's.3 Piatt4 is trying to get transferred to New York, to the Custom House   Well, good by for present, you dear friend, and God bless you and wife, and bring you both safe back    Walt ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["I", "PRP"], ["went", "VBD"], ["up", "RP"], ["to", "TO"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["house", "NN"], ["this", "DT"], ["morning", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["took", "VBD"], ["a", "DT"], ["look", "NN"], ["at", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["garden", "NN"], ["Everything", "NNP"], ["growing", "VBG"], ["first", "JJ"], ["rate", "NN"], ["potatoes", "VBZ"], [",", ","], ["tomatoes", "VBZ"], [",", ","], ["corn", "NN"], [",", ","], ["cabbages", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["and", "CC"], ["all", "DT"], ["I", "PRP"], ["guess", "VBP"], ["upon", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["whole", "JJ"], ["the", "DT"], ["garden", "NN"], ["never", "RB"], ["looked", "VBD"], ["better", "RBR"], ["at", "IN"], ["this", "DT"], ["time", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["year", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["We", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["had", "VBN"], ["opportune", "NN"], ["rains", "NNS"], ["I", "PRP"], ["inquired", "VBD"], ["about", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["cow", "NN"], [",", ","], ["and", "CC"], ["received", "VBD"], ["a", "DT"], ["favorable", "JJ"], ["report", "NN"], [".", "."]], [[".", "."]], [[".", "."]], [[".", "."]], [[["John", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["about", "IN"], ["coming", "VBG"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["not", "RB"], ["able", "JJ"], ["to", "TO"], ["say", "VB"], ["anything", "NN"], ["decisive", "JJ"], ["in", "IN"], ["this", "DT"], ["letter", "NN"], [".", "."]], [[".", "."]], [[".", "."]], [[".", "."]], [["Up", "IN"], ["in", "IN"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["Bureau", "NNP"], ["all", "DT"], ["seems", "VBZ"], ["to", "TO"], ["go", "VB"], ["on", "IN"], ["as", "IN"], ["usual", "JJ"], [".", "."]], [[".", "."]], [[".", "."]], [[["John", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["send", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], ["the", "DT"], ["July", "NNP"], ["Atlantic.2", "NNP"], [".", "."]], [[".", "."]], [[".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["feeling", "VBG"], ["hearty", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["in", "IN"], ["good", "JJ"], ["spirits", "NNS"], ["go", "VBP"], ["around", "IN"], ["more", "JJR"], ["than", "IN"], ["usual", "JJ"], ["go", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["such", "JJ"], ["doings", "NNS"], ["as", "IN"], ["base-ball", "JJ"], ["matches