& full of blunders.", "I am in good health & all goes well.", "Andy, dear boy, I hope my delay of a few days will not put you out   Write to me, & tell me about the office, & my friends there.", "Don't forward any letters that come after Friday next, but put them in my drawer.", "Once more   I send my love to you & all.", "Walt "], "words": ["New", "York", ",", "Sept.", "10", ",", "1866.", "Dear", "Andy,1", "I", "rec", "'d", "your", "letter", "last", "Saturday", "I", "intended", "to", "return", "day", "after", "to-morrow", ",", "but", "shall", "not", "be", "able", "to", ",", "till", "the", "last", "of", "the", "week", ",", "or", "the", "early", "part", "of", "next", "week.", "The", "reason", "is", "that", "my", "book", ",", "which", "is", "a", "little", "more", "than", "half", "done", ",", "does", "not", "get", "along", "as", "fast", "as", "the", "printers", "agreed", "&", "if", "I", "do", "not", "stay", "&", "finish", "it", ",", "(", "the", "supervision", "of", "it", ",", ")", "it", "will", "be", "botched", "&", "full", "of", "blunders.", "I", "am", "in", "good", "health", "&", "all", "goes", "well.", "Andy", ",", "dear", "boy", ",", "I", "hope", "my", "delay", "of", "a", "few", "days", "will", "not", "put", "you", "out", "Write", "to", "me", ",", "&", "tell", "me", "about", "the", "office", ",", "&", "my", "friends", "there.", "Do", "n't", "forward", "any", "letters", "that", "come", "after", "Friday", "next", ",", "but", "put", "them", "in", "my", "drawer.", "Once", "more", "I", "send", "my", "love", "to", "you", "&", "all.", "Walt"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.332517339861", "recipient": "Andrew Kerr", "organizations": [], "sender": "Walt Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/nyp.00216.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Walt Whitman to Andrew Kerr ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["William", "NNP"], ["E.", "NNP"], ["Chapin", "NNP"]], ["&", "CC"], [["Company", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Mr. Ballow2", "Walt", "Whitman"], "money": [], "year": "1866", "locations": [], "month": "Sep", "parties": ["Walt Whitman", "William E. Chapin", "Company"], "properDate": "Sep 24, 1866", "gpe": ["Wm"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [], "text": "  Sept. 24th 1866.  Wm. E. Chapin & Co.1 please furnish Mr. Ballow2 with paper for end leaves, &c. similar to that you used for the book. Walt Whitman ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["Sept.", "NNP"], ["24th", "CD"], ["1866", "CD"], [".", "."]], [[["Wm", "NNP"]], [".", "."]], [["E.", "NNP"], ["Chapin", "NNP"], ["&", "CC"], ["Co.1", "NNP"], ["please", "NN"], ["furnish", "NN"], [["Mr.", "NNP"], ["Ballow2", "NNP"]], ["with", "IN"], ["paper", "NN"], ["for", "IN"], ["end", "NN"], ["leaves", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["c.", "NNP"], ["similar", "JJ"], ["to", "TO"], ["that", "DT"], ["you", "PRP"], ["used", "VBD"], ["for", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["book", "NN"], [".", "."]], [[["Walt", "NNP"]], [["Whitman", "NNP"]]]], "sentences": ["  Sept. 24th 1866.", "Wm.", "E. Chapin & Co.1 please furnish Mr. Ballow2 with paper for end leaves, &c. similar to that you used for the book.", "Walt Whitman "], "words": ["Sept.", "24th", "1866.", "Wm.", "E.", "Chapin", "&", "Co.1", "please", "furnish", "Mr.", "Ballow2", "with", "paper", "for", "end", "leaves", ",", "&", "c.", "similar", "to", "that", "you", "used", "for", "the", "book.", "Walt", "Whitman"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.334421324629", "recipient": "Company", "organizations": [], "sender": "Walt Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/loc.00711.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Walt Whitman to William E. Chapin & Company ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Mr.", "NNP"], ["Baker", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Mr.", "Light House Board", "Walt Whitman"], "money": [], "year": "1866", "locations": [], "month": "Sep", "parties": ["Walt Whitman", "Mr. Baker"], "properDate": "Sep 25, 1866", "gpe": ["Washington"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[38.8951118, -77.0363658]], "text": " Mr. O'Connor's address is Wm. D. O'Connor, Light House Board, Treasury Dep't. Washington, D. C. Yours respectfully, Walt Whitman ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Mr.", "NNP"]], ["O'Connor", "NNP"], ["'s", "POS"], ["address", "NN"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["Wm", "NNP"], [".", "."]], [["D.", "NNP"], ["O'Connor", "NNP"], [",", ","], [["Light", "NNP"], ["House", "NNP"], ["Board", "NNP"]], [",", ","], [["Treasury", "NNP"]], ["Dep't", "NNP"], [".", "."]], [[["Washington", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["D.", "NNP"], ["C.", "NNP"], ["Yours", "NNP"], ["respectfully", "RB"], [",", ","], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]]]], "sentences": [" Mr. O'Connor's address is Wm.", "D. O'Connor, Light House Board, Treasury Dep't.", "Washington, D. C. Yours respectfully, Walt Whitman "], "words": ["Mr.", "O'Connor", "'s", "address", "is", "Wm.", "D.", "O'Connor", ",", "Light", "House", "Board", ",", "Treasury", "Dep't.", "Washington", ",", "D.", "C.", "Yours", "respectfully", ",", "Walt", "Whitman"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.334557323541", "recipient": "Mr. Baker", "organizations": ["Treasury"], "sender": "Walt Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/and.00001.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Walt Whitman to Mr. Baker ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Alfred", "NNP"], ["Pratt", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Arlington Heights", "Walt", "Whitman"], "money": [], "year": "1866", "locations": [], "month": "Sep", "parties": ["Walt Whitman", "Alfred Pratt"], "properDate": "Sep 27, 1866", "gpe": ["Washington", "Dear", "Alfred", "Brooklyn", "New York", "Washington", "Al", "Alexandria"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[38.8951118, -77.0363658], [44.3257819, -84.7687579], [40.65, -73.95], [40.7143528, -74.00597309999999], [38.8951118, -77.0363658], [38.8048355, -77.0469214], [39.3270677, -79.2802633]], "text": "  ATTORNEY GENERAL'S OFFICE, Washington,  Sept. 27, 1866.  Dear boy, & comrade,1 I am not only alive, but as well & hearty as ever I was   & more [than] that, I often think about you, Alfred, & retain the same friendship that we formed when I used to sit down on your bed when you was so low in the hospital. If I hadn't got your letter of 23d, I should likely have written to you very soon, of my own accord, for I thought about you the last few weeks in particular. I have been home in Brooklyn the last two months, to see my mother, & pay a visit to New York, &c. and I only returned day before yesterday. I am still employed in this Department, shall probably remain here through the winter, (although nothing is certain now-days)   Washington is rather dull   no more soldiers around like there used to be   no more patrols marching around the streets   no more great racks of hospitals   I get along well enough in this city in pleasant weather, when one can go around, but it's rough in bad weather. Al, I got the picture, dear boy, & I have it yet, & take good care of it, & take a good look at it every now & then   I think it is a good likeness. It is now a year ago since you sent it   you spoke in that letter of your parents   You must give my love to them, & if it should be practicable I should like much to make them a call   but yet it does not seem likely as things are at present. But I wonder whether we shall ever come together again, you & I, my loving soldier boy. O how much comfort it would be to me, if things were so that we could have each other's society   for I think so much of such things. I am writing this at my table by a big window in the Office, where I can look out & see the Potomac away down to Alexandria, & across all up & down Arlington Heights, & near at hand the grounds south of the President's House   it is a splendid day to-day, bright & clear & just cool enough   & I feel in good health   & all the better on account of your letter arriving. Well I must draw to a close. I hope, dear comrade, you are trying to be an honorable & upright young man, for that is more than the greatest worldly prosperity, or learning either. I send you my love, & must now bid you farewell for present, dear soldier boy. Walt Whitman ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["ATTORNEY", "NN"], [["GENERAL", "NNP"]], ["'S", "POS"], ["OFFICE", "NNP"], [",", ","], [["Washington", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["Sept.", "NNP"], ["27", "CD"], [",", ","], ["1866", "CD"], [".", "."]], [[["Dear", "NNP"]], ["boy", "NN"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["comrade,1", "-NONE-"], ["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["not", "RB"], ["only", "RB"], ["alive", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["but", "CC"], ["as", "IN"], ["well", "RB"], ["&", "CC"], ["hearty", "NN"], ["as", "IN"], ["ever", "RB"], ["I", "PRP"], ["was", "VBD"], ["&", "CC"], ["more", "JJR"], ["[", ":"], ["than", "IN"], ["]", "CD"], ["that", "WDT"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["often", "RB"], ["think", "VBP"], ["about", "IN"], ["you", "PRP"], [",", ","], [["Alfred", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["retain", "VB"], ["the", "DT"], ["same", "JJ"], ["friendship", "NN"], ["that", "IN"], ["we", "PRP"], ["formed", "VBD"], ["when", "WRB"], ["I", "PRP"], ["used", "VBD"], ["to", "TO"], ["sit", "VB"], ["down", "RP"], ["on", "IN"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["bed", "VBN"], ["when", "WRB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["was", "VBD"], ["so", "RB"], ["low", "JJ"], ["in", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["hospital", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["If", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["had", "VBD"], ["n't", "RB"], ["got", "VBN"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["letter", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["23d", "CD"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["should", "MD"], ["likel