 has received, (he is on a Committee of Sold. & Sail. Union League)   I think it ought to be published in full. You make a brief introduction to it & let it go in a Sunday Chronicle.3 Let him have a proof when it is set up, to bring to me. Yours &c Walt Whitman ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["ATTORNEY", "NN"], [["GENERAL", "NNP"]], ["'S", "POS"], ["OFFICE", "NNP"], [",", ","], [["Washington", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["Nov.", "NNP"], ["3", "CD"], [",", ","], ["1866", "CD"], [".", "."]], [[["Dear", "NNP"]], [["Hinton", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["The", "NNP"], ["bearer", "NN"], [",", ","], ["my", "PRP$"], ["friend", "NN"], [",", ","], [["Mr.", "NNP"], ["Shambaugh,2", "NNP"]], ["was", "VBD"], ["showing", "VBG"], ["me", "PRP"], ["a", "DT"], ["letter", "NN"], ["he", "PRP"], ["has", "VBZ"], ["received", "VBN"], [",", ","], ["(", "NNP"], ["he", "PRP"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["on", "IN"], ["a", "DT"], [["Committee", "NNP"]], ["of", "IN"], [["Sold", "NNP"]], [".", "."]], [["&", "CC"], ["Sail", "NNP"], [".", "."]], [[["Union", "NN"], ["League", "NNP"]], [")", "NNP"], ["I", "NNP"], ["think", "VBP"], ["it", "PRP"], ["ought", "MD"], ["to", "TO"], ["be", "VB"], ["published", "VBN"], ["in", "IN"], ["full", "JJ"], [".", "."]], [["You", "PRP"], ["make", "VBP"], ["a", "DT"], ["brief", "JJ"], ["introduction", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["it", "PRP"], ["&", "CC"], ["let", "VB"], ["it", "PRP"], ["go", "VB"], ["in", "IN"], ["a", "DT"], ["Sunday", "NNP"], ["Chronicle.3", "NNP"], ["Let", "NNP"], ["him", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["a", "DT"], ["proof", "JJ"], ["when", "WRB"], ["it", "PRP"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["set", "VBN"], ["up", "RP"], [",", ","], ["to", "TO"], ["bring", "VB"], ["to", "TO"], ["me", "PRP"], [".", "."]], [["Yours", "NNS"], ["&", "CC"], ["c", "NN"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]]]], "sentences": ["  ATTORNEY GENERAL'S OFFICE, Washington,  Nov. 3, 1866.", "Dear Hinton, The bearer, my friend, Mr. Shambaugh,2 was showing me a letter he has received, (he is on a Committee of Sold.", "& Sail.", "Union League)   I think it ought to be published in full.", "You make a brief introduction to it & let it go in a Sunday Chronicle.3 Let him have a proof when it is set up, to bring to me.", "Yours &c Walt Whitman "], "words": ["ATTORNEY", "GENERAL", "'S", "OFFICE", ",", "Washington", ",", "Nov.", "3", ",", "1866.", "Dear", "Hinton", ",", "The", "bearer", ",", "my", "friend", ",", "Mr.", "Shambaugh,2", "was", "showing", "me", "a", "letter", "he", "has", "received", ",", "(", "he", "is", "on", "a", "Committee", "of", "Sold.", "&", "Sail.", "Union", "League", ")", "I", "think", "it", "ought", "to", "be", "published", "in", "full.", "You", "make", "a", "brief", "introduction", "to", "it", "&", "let", "it", "go", "in", "a", "Sunday", "Chronicle.3", "Let", "him", "have", "a", "proof", "when", "it", "is", "set", "up", ",", "to", "bring", "to", "me.", "Yours", "&", "c", "Walt", "Whitman"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.33986128111", "recipient": "Richard J. Hinton", "organizations": ["GENERAL", "Hinton", "Committee"], "sender": "Walt Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/khs.00001.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Walt Whitman to Richard J. Hinton ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Bayard", "NNP"], ["Taylor", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Kennett", "Penna", "Sir", "Bayard Taylor"], "money": [], "year": "1866", "locations": [], "month": "Nov", "parties": ["Bayard Taylor", "Walt Whitman"], "properDate": "Nov 12, 1866", "gpe": ["St. John", "Washington"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[47.5605413, -52.71283150000001], [38.8951118, -77.0363658]], "text": "  Kennett Square, Penna. Nov. 12, 1866  My dear Sir: I send to you by the same mail which takes this note, a copy of my last poem The Picture of St. John.  I do not know whether the subject of the poem (the growth and development of the artist-nature, and its relation to life) will much interest you, but I hope you will here and there find something drawn immediately from nature.  I am, at least, not aware that anything in the book is simulated or forced:  whether successful or not, it is an honest conscientious effort. I value, above all things, sincerity  in literature; hence I am not one of those who overlook your remarkable powers of expression, your broad, vital reverence for humanity, because some things you have said repel them.  The age is over-squeamish, and, for my part, I prefer the honest nude to the suggestive half-draped.  I think the proper question to be asked is:  does a certain thing need to be said?  If so, let it be said!  The worst form of immorality, I have found, veils itself in decent words. There is one quality I recognize in you, which warmly and constantly attracts me.  That is, your deep and tender reverence for Man   your unwearied, affectionate, practical fraternity.  There is too little of this quality in the world, and the race will be better and happier in proportion as it is manifested. I shall be in Washington on the 27th of December, to lecture, and hope that I shall then be able to meet you personally.  If you can spare me an hour or two after the lecture, you will greatly oblige  Your friend, Bayard Taylor  ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Kennett", "NNP"]], [["Square", "NNP"]], [",", ","], [["Penna", "NNP"]], [".", "."]], [["Nov.", "NNP"], ["12", "CD"], [",", ","], ["1866", "CD"], ["My", "NNP"], ["dear", "NN"], [["Sir", "NNP"]], [":", ":"], ["I", "PRP"], ["send", "VBP"], ["to", "TO"], ["you", "PRP"], ["by", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["same", "JJ"], ["mail", "NN"], ["which", "WDT"], ["takes", "VBZ"], ["this", "DT"], ["note", "NN"], [",", ","], ["a", "DT"], ["copy", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["last", "JJ"], ["poem", "NN"], ["The", "DT"], [["Picture", "NNP"]], ["of", "IN"], [["St.", "NNP"], ["John", "NNP"]], [".",