ar my clothes a long while    Walt.", "Mother, I would rather you would use the money to get things for yourself   shoes, stockings, underclothes    "], "words": ["I", "suppose", "you", "got", "a", "letter", "last", "Saturday", "as", "well", "as", "the", "previous", "Wednesday", "I", "am", "better", "than", "I", "was", "last", "week", "not", "as", "well", "as", "I", "would", "like", "to", "be", ",", "but", "well", "enough", "to", "keep", "on", "with", "my", "work", ",", "&", "c.", "just", "the", "same", "as", "ever", "I", "feel", "real", "well", ",", "sometimes", ",", "for", "a", "day", "but", "then", "comes", "the", "trouble", "in", "the", "head", "again", "Did", "you", "get", "the", "``", "Galaxy", "''", "of", "Dec.", "1st", "?", "I", "think", "it", "a", "very", "good", "piece.", "Every", "thing", "here", "in", "the", "office", "goes", "on", "as", "usual.", "I", "got", "your", "letter", ",", "mother.", "I", "wrote", "to", "Han", "last", "week.", "It", "is", "beautiful", "weather", "here", "to-day", "I", "have", "got", "my", "new", "trowsers", "$", "20", "!", "!", "only", "think", "of", "that", "!", "it", "is", "lucky", "I", "wear", "my", "clothes", "a", "long", "while", "Walt.", "Mother", ",", "I", "would", "rather", "you", "would", "use", "the", "money", "to", "get", "things", "for", "yourself", "shoes", ",", "stockings", ",", "underclothes"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.343125254998", "recipient": "Louisa Van Velsor Whitman", "organizations": [], "sender": "Walt Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/tex.00151.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Walt Whitman to Louisa Van Velsor Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["John", "NNP"], ["S.", "NNP"], ["Jenks", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["John", "Sir", "Walt", "Whitman"], "money": [], "year": "1866", "locations": [], "month": "Nov", "parties": ["Walt Whitman", "John S. Jenks"], "properDate": "Nov 28, 1866", "gpe": ["Washington"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[38.8951118, -77.0363658]], "text": "  ATTORNEY GENERAL'S OFFICE, Washington.  Nov. 28, 1866.  John S. Jenks, Sir, In answer to yours of the 27th I reply that no letter from you, of the 17th has come to hand   & of course I have not rec'd $3.1 But as I am not willing you should be the loser, in such a manner, I send you my book, by same mail with this. Walt Whitman ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["ATTORNEY", "NN"], [["GENERAL", "NNP"]], ["'S", "POS"], ["OFFICE", "NNP"], [",", ","], [["Washington", "NNP"]], [".", "."]], [["Nov.", "NNP"], ["28", "CD"], [",", ","], ["1866", "CD"], [".", "."]], [[["John", "NNP"]], ["S.", "NNP"], ["Jenks", "NNP"], [",", ","], [["Sir", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["In", "NNP"], ["answer", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["yours", "NNS"], ["of", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["27th", "JJ"], ["I", "PRP"], ["reply", "RB"], ["that", "IN"], ["no", "DT"], ["letter", "NN"], ["from", "IN"], ["you", "PRP"], [",", ","], ["of", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["17th", "JJ"], ["has", "VBZ"], ["come", "VBN"], ["to", "TO"], ["hand", "VB"], ["&", "CC"], ["of", "IN"], ["course", "NN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["not", "RB"], ["rec", "JJ"], ["'d", "JJ"], ["$", "$"], ["3.1", "CD"], ["But", "CC"], ["as", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["not", "RB"], ["willing", "JJ"], ["you", "PRP"], ["should", "MD"], ["be", "VB"], ["the", "DT"], ["loser", "NN"], [",", ","], ["in", "IN"], ["such", "JJ"], ["a", "DT"], ["manner", "NN"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["send", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["book", "NN"], [",", ","], ["by", "IN"], ["same", "JJ"], ["mail", "NN"], ["with", "IN"], ["this", "DT"], [".", "."]], [[["Walt", "NNP"]], [["Whitman", "NNP"]]]], "sentences": ["  ATTORNEY GENERAL'S OFFICE, Washington.", "Nov. 28, 1866.", "John S. Jenks, Sir, In answer to yours of the 27th I reply that no letter from you, of the 17th has come to hand   & of course I have not rec'd $3.1 But as I am not willing you should be the loser, in such a manner, I send you my book, by same mail with this.", "Walt Whitman "], "words": ["ATTORNEY", "GENERAL", "'S", "OFFICE", ",", "Washington.", "Nov.", "28", ",", "1866.", "John", "S.", "Jenks", ",", "Sir", ",", "In", "answer", "to", "yours", "of", "the", "27th", "I", "reply", "that", "no", "letter", "from", "you", ",", "of", "the", "17th", "has", "come", "to", "hand", "&", "of", "course", "I", "have", "not", "rec", "'d", "$", "3.1", "But", "as", "I", "am", "not", "willing", "you", "should", "be", "the", "loser", ",", "in", "such", "a", "manner", ",", "I", "send", "you", "my", "book", ",", "by", "same", "mail", "with", "this.", "Walt", "Whitman"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.34326125391", "recipient": "John S. Jenks", "organizations": ["GENERAL"], "sender": "Walt Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/loc.00714.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Walt Whitman to John S. Jenks ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Charles", "NNP"], ["L.", "NNP"], ["Heyde", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]]]], "people": ["Burlington", "Whitman", "Richard", "Grant White", "Laus Veneris", "Orchard", "Han"], "money": [], "year": "1866", "locations": [], "month": "Dec", "parties": ["Charles L. Heyde", "Walt Whitman"], "properDate": "Dec 0, 1866", "gpe": ["Swinburne"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [], "text": "  Burlington Dec 1866  Friend Walt. I have sent to you the \"Galaxy\"; It contains two articles, one on Whitman and one on Swinburne,2   I have read both criticisms, with great satisfaction. Richard Grant White has but paid just sympathy to a true poet \"Swinburne\"; The criticism is a \"Poem,\" in itself. It has the comprehensiveness, and the fearless recognition of the divine idea, or sentiment of \"Love,\" as expressed by the Poet, he writes upon   Swinburne electrifies me. I read one verse of his \"Laus Veneris,\" in a store, and bought the book   When critics or ordinary readers, or writers scribble him down, the Sun will cease to procreate and vitalize the earth. He is cultivated, and \"passion\" is his subject   \"St Dorothy\" is saddening, and the \"Leper\" oh how passionately full of piteous Love   and the \"Orchard\" oh! the night is all starrd by it, and earth burdend with dewy fragrancies    There is enough beauty in your \"Leaves\" to make a rare book, and not cast out sensuous extravagance either. But you are wonderfully, woefully mistaken in the privileage you take of being merely savagely material, and consequently offensively vulgar    Han is much better than usual, and is continualy promising to write to her Mother.  C L Heyde  ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Burlington", "NNP"]], ["Dec", "NNP"], ["1866", "CD"], ["Friend", "NNP"], ["Walt", "NNP"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["sent", "VBN"], ["to", "TO"], ["you", "PRP"], ["the", "DT"], ["``", "``"], ["Galaxy", "NNP"], ["''", "''"], [";", ":"], ["It", "PRP"], ["contains", "VBZ"], ["two", "CD"], ["articles", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["one", "CD"], ["on", "IN"], [["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["and", "CC"], ["one", "CD"], ["on", "IN"], ["Swinburne,2", "-NONE-"], ["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["read", "VBN"], ["both", "DT"], ["criticisms", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["with", "IN"], ["great", "JJ"], ["satisfaction", "NN"], [".", "."]], [[["Richard", "NNP"]], [["Grant", "NNP"], ["White", "NNP"]], ["has", "VBZ"], ["but", "CC"], ["paid", "VBN"], ["just", "RB"], ["sympathy", "JJ"], ["to", "TO"], ["a", "DT"], ["true", "JJ"], ["poet", "NN"], ["``", "``"], ["Swinburne", "NNP"], ["''", "''"], [";", ":"], ["The", "DT"], ["criticism", "NN"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["a", "DT"], ["``", "``"], ["Poem", "NNP"], [",", ","], ["''", "''"], ["in", "IN"], ["itself", "PRP"], [".", "."]], [["It", "PRP"], ["has", "VBZ"], ["the", 