"to", "make", "a", "rare", "book", ",", "and", "not", "cast", "out", "sensuous", "extravagance", "either.", "But", "you", "are", "wonderfully", ",", "woefully", "mistaken", "in", "the", "privileage", "you", "take", "of", "being", "merely", "savagely", "material", ",", "and", "consequently", "offensively", "vulgar", "Han", "is", "much", "better", "than", "usual", ",", "and", "is", "continualy", "promising", "to", "write", "to", "her", "Mother.", "C", "L", "Heyde"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.343533251734", "recipient": "Walt Whitman", "organizations": ["Poet", "Sun"], "sender": "Charles L. Heyde", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/med.00330.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Charles L. Heyde to Walt Whitman"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["John", "NNP"], ["S.", "NNP"], ["Jenks", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["John", "Sir", "Walt", "Whitman"], "money": [], "year": "1866", "locations": [], "month": "Dec", "parties": ["Walt Whitman", "John S. Jenks"], "properDate": "Dec 1, 1866", "gpe": ["Washington", "Please"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[38.8951118, -77.0363658]], "text": "  ATTORNEY GENERAL'S OFFICE, Washington,  Dec. 1, 1866.  John S. Jenks, My dear Sir, I have rec'd your note of 30th Nov. with $3. Please accept my special acknowledgments. Should the letter of Nov. 17, ever appear, I will return it to you. Walt Whitman ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["ATTORNEY", "NN"], [["GENERAL", "NNP"]], ["'S", "POS"], ["OFFICE", "NNP"], [",", ","], [["Washington", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["Dec.", "NNP"], ["1", "CD"], [",", ","], ["1866", "CD"], [".", "."]], [[["John", "NNP"]], ["S.", "NNP"], ["Jenks", "NNP"], [",", ","], ["My", "NNP"], ["dear", "NN"], [["Sir", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["rec", "JJ"], ["'d", "JJ"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["note", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["30th", "CD"], ["Nov.", "NNP"], ["with", "IN"], ["$", "$"], ["3", "CD"], [".", "."]], [[["Please", "NN"]], ["accept", "VBD"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["special", "JJ"], ["acknowledgments", "NNS"], [".", "."]], [["Should", "MD"], ["the", "DT"], ["letter", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["Nov.", "NNP"], ["17", "CD"], [",", ","], ["ever", "RB"], ["appear", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["will", "MD"], ["return", "VB"], ["it", "PRP"], ["to", "TO"], ["you", "PRP"], [".", "."]], [[["Walt", "NNP"]], [["Whitman", "NNP"]]]], "sentences": ["  ATTORNEY GENERAL'S OFFICE, Washington,  Dec. 1, 1866.", "John S. Jenks, My dear Sir, I have rec'd your note of 30th Nov. with $3.", "Please accept my special acknowledgments.", "Should the letter of Nov. 17, ever appear, I will return it to you.", "Walt Whitman "], "words": ["ATTORNEY", "GENERAL", "'S", "OFFICE", ",", "Washington", ",", "Dec.", "1", ",", "1866.", "John", "S.", "Jenks", ",", "My", "dear", "Sir", ",", "I", "have", "rec", "'d", "your", "note", "of", "30th", "Nov.", "with", "$", "3.", "Please", "accept", "my", "special", "acknowledgments.", "Should", "the", "letter", "of", "Nov.", "17", ",", "ever", "appear", ",", "I", "will", "return", "it", "to", "you.", "Walt", "Whitman"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.343669250646", "recipient": "John S. Jenks", "organizations": ["GENERAL"], "sender": "Walt Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/loc.00715.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Walt Whitman to John S. Jenks ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Bayard", "NNP"], ["Taylor", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Kennett", "Penna", "Whitman", "Willard", "Bayard Taylor"], "money": [], "year": "1866", "locations": [], "month": "Dec", "parties": ["Bayard Taylor", "Walt Whitman"], "properDate": "Dec 2, 1866", "gpe": ["New York", "Life", "Washington"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[40.7143528, -74.00597309999999], [38.8951118, -77.0363658]], "text": "  Kennett Square, Penna. Dec. 2, 1866  My dear Whitman: I find your book and cordial letter, on returning home from a lecturing tour in New York, and heartily thank you for both.  I have had the first edition of your Leaves of Grass among my books, since its first appearance, and have read it many times.  I may say, frankly, that there are two things in it which I find nowhere else in literature, though I find them in my own nature.  I mean the awe and wonder and reverence and beauty of Life, as expressed in the human body, with the physical attraction and delight of mere contact which it inspires, and that tender and noble love of man for man which once certainly existed, but now almost seems to have gone out of the experience of the race.  I think there is nothing in your volume which I do not fully comprehend in the sense in which you wrote; I always try to judge an author from his own standpoint rather than mine, but in this case the two nearly coincide.  We should differ rather in regard to form than substance, I suspect.  There is not one word of your large and beautiful sympathy for men, which I cannot take into my own heart, nor one of those subtle and wonderful physical affinities you describe which I cannot comprehend.  I say these things, not in the way of praise, but because I know from my own experience that correct appreciation of an author is less frequent than it should be.  It is welcome to me, and may be so to you. I did not mean to write so much when I commenced, and will only say that I will be in Washington on the 27th   only for that night   and would be very glad if we can come together for awhile after my lecture is over.  I am afraid I shall not arrive in time to call at the Dep't before the lecture, but if I can I will.  If not, will you either come to Willard's or tell me where to find you, and oblige  Your friend, Bayard Taylor  ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Kennett", "NNP"]], [["Square", "NNP"]], [",", ","], [["Penna", "NNP"]], [".", "."]], [["Dec.", "NNP"], ["2", "CD"], [",", ","], ["1866", "CD"], ["My", "NNP"], ["dear", "NN"], [["Whitman", "NNP"]], [":", ":"], ["I", "PRP"], ["find", "VBP"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["book", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["cordial", "JJ"], ["letter", "NN"], [",", ","], ["on", "IN"], ["returning", "NN"], ["home", "NN"], ["from", "IN"], ["a", "DT"], ["lecturing", "NN"], ["tour", "NN"], ["in", "IN"], [["New", "NNP"], ["York", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["and", "CC"], ["heartily", "RB"], ["thank", "NN"], ["you", "PRP"], ["for", "IN"], ["both", "DT"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["had", "VBN"], ["the", "DT"], ["first", "JJ"], ["edition", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["Leaves", "NNP"], ["of", "IN"], [["Grass", "NNP"]], ["among", "IN"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["books", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["since", "IN"], ["its", "PRP$"], ["first", "JJ"], ["appearance", "NN"], [",", ","], ["and", "CC"], ["have", "VBP"], ["read", "VBN"], ["it", "PRP"], ["many", "JJ"], ["times", "NNS"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["may", "MD"], ["say", "VB"], [",", ","], ["frankly", "RB"], [",", ","], ["that", "IN"], ["there", "EX"], ["are", "VBP"], ["two", "CD"], ["things", "NNS"], ["in", "IN"], ["it", "PRP"], ["which", "WDT"], ["I", "PRP"], ["find", "VBP"], ["nowhere", "RB"], ["else", "RB"], ["in", "IN"], ["literature", "NN"], [",", ","], ["though", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["find", "VBP"], ["them", "PRP"], ["in", "IN"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["own", "JJ"], ["nature", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["mean", "VBP"], ["the", "DT"], ["awe", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["wonder", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["reverence", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["beauty", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], [["Life", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["as", "IN"], ["expressed", "VBN"], ["in", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["human", "JJ"], ["body", "NN"], [",", ","], ["with", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["physical", "JJ"], ["attraction", "NN"], ["and", "CC"], ["deli