r the stereotype plates, \"Imprints of the Leaves of Grass\" Would be pleased to hear from you soon  Resptly Yours H. Wentworth  ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Boston", "NNP"]], ["Dec", "NNP"], ["17", "CD"], ["/", "CD"], ["66", "CD"], ["Mr", "NNP"], ["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"], [",", ","], [["Sir", "NNP"], ["What", "NNP"]], ["will", "MD"], ["you", "PRP"], ["give", "VB"], ["me", "PRP"], ["for", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["stereotype", "NN"], ["plates", "VBZ"], [",", ","], ["``", "``"], ["Imprints", "NNS"], ["of", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], [["Leaves", "NNP"]], ["of", "IN"], [["Grass", "NNP"]], ["''", "''"], ["Would", "NNP"], ["be", "VB"], ["pleased", "VBN"], ["to", "TO"], ["hear", "VB"], ["from", "IN"], ["you", "PRP"], ["soon", "RB"], ["Resptly", "RB"], [["Yours", "NNP"], ["H.", "NNP"], ["Wentworth", "NNP"]]]], "sentences": ["  Boston Dec 17 / 66  Mr Walt Whitman, Sir What will you give me for the stereotype plates, \"Imprints of the Leaves of Grass\" Would be pleased to hear from you soon  Resptly Yours H. Wentworth  "], "words": ["Boston", "Dec", "17", "/", "66", "Mr", "Walt", "Whitman", ",", "Sir", "What", "will", "you", "give", "me", "for", "the", "stereotype", "plates", ",", "``", "Imprints", "of", "the", "Leaves", "of", "Grass", "''", "Would", "be", "pleased", "to", "hear", "from", "you", "soon", "Resptly", "Yours", "H.", "Wentworth"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.345845233238", "recipient": "Walt Whitman", "organizations": ["Leaves", "Grass"], "sender": "Horace Wentworth", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/cw/tei/yal.00102.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Letter from Horace Wentworth to Walt Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[["Letter", "NNP"], ["from", "IN"], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Louisa", "NNP"], ["Van", "NNP"], ["Velsor", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Dearest", "Aunt Kitty", "Mother", "Jeff", "Uncle Walt"], "money": [], "year": "1866", "locations": [], "month": "Dec", "parties": ["Walt Whitman", "Louisa Van Velsor Whitman"], "properDate": "Dec 18, 1866", "gpe": ["Washington", "Mother", "Maine", "Walt"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[38.8951118, -77.0363658], [45.253783, -69.4454689]], "text": "  ATTORNEY GENERAL'S OFFICE, Washington,  Dec. 18, 1866.  Dearest Mother, I rec'd your letter Sunday morning last   It has been very cold here too, but is pleasant now. I sent you a copy of \"Leaves of Grass\"   which I suppose you have rec'd. Every thing here with me remains the same   I am free from the distress in my head   Mrs. Grayson1 is very sick   she sent my old washerwoman, old Aunt Kitty, around this morning to see if I had any of \"that bread my mother used to send me\"   I suppose she meant the sweet Dyer bread   I gave her a piece a long while ago, & she liked it   poor woman, I think she is on her dying bed   Mother, you must write to me how Jeff is, & how he is getting along   tell Hattie I hope she will take a lesson on the piano every day, and learn to play for her Uncle Walt   so when he comes home, she can play a beautiful tune2    I have been down to the Hospital a great deal lately   A friend of mine that I have known over three years, a Maine soldier named Racliffe,3 was very low with consumption & bleeding at the lungs   He died Sunday morning   it was a great relief, for he suffered much    Well, mother, I believe that is all this time. Walt. ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["ATTORNEY", "NN"], [["GENERAL", "NNP"]], ["'S", "POS"], ["OFFICE", "NNP"], [",", ","], [["Washington", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["Dec.", "NNP"], ["18", "CD"], [",", ","], ["1866", "CD"], [".", "."]], [[["Dearest", "NNP"]], [["Mother", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["rec", "VBP"], ["'d", "JJ"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["letter", "NN"], ["Sunday", "NNP"], ["morning", "NN"], ["last", "JJ"], ["It", "PRP"], ["has", "VBZ"], ["been", "VBN"], ["very", "RB"], ["cold