"TO"], ["express", "NN"], ["genuine", "NN"], ["pleasure", "NN"], ["with", "IN"], ["gratitude", "NN"], ["both", "DT"], ["to", "TO"], ["its", "PRP$"], ["editor", "NN"], ["&", "CC"], ["publisher", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["And", "CC"], ["now", "RB"], [",", ","], ["my", "PRP$"], ["dear", "NN"], ["sir", "NN"], [",", ","], ["please", "NN"], ["accept", "VBD"], ["with", "IN"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["trust", "NN"], ["in", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["success", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["enterprise", "NN"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["kindest", "NN"], ["respects", "NNS"], ["to", "TO"], ["yourself", "PRP"], ["personally", "RB"], [".", "."]]], "sentences": ["  Feb 18   1868                                  Dear Sir:              In response to your letter of the 5th instant, which has just reached me, I have to                 say that I accept the proposal made in it respecting your English publication of my                 poems   & hereby agree that you have the privilege of selling that                 publication in the United States, on payment to me, or my agent, of a royalty of one                 shilling, (or 25 cents gold,) upon every copy sold in the U. S.              Of course it is distinctly understood that this grant from me does not affect my                 copyright here, but that said copyright, in each of its particulars & in the                 whole, is absolutely fully & exclusively retained by me.", "It is not improbable that a very handsome & steady sale of the English volume                 may be effected here, by the right business manipulation, a moderate, judicious                 advertising &c. My book has never been really published here at all                 & the market is in a sort vacant of supplies.", "I will probably suggest to you                 something more on these points, in a future letter.", "I received yesterday a letter from Mr. Conway, conveying your proposition, to which I                 mailed an immediate answer, to the same effect as herewith.", "Accept my thanks for the William Blake.", "It has not yet come from the post office, but I know                 it will prove to me a profoundly interesting study, and a handsome gift.", "It is, in                 fact, a book I was wanting.", "After the reception of the copy you speak of   my own volume   (now                 probably on its way)   I shall doubtless have occasion to express genuine                 pleasure   with gratitude both to its editor & publisher.", "And now, my dear sir, please accept with my trust in the success of the enterprise my                 kindest respects to yourself personally.  "], "words": ["Feb", "18", "1868", "Dear", "Sir", ":", "In", "response", "to", "your", "letter", "of", "the", "5th", "instant", ",", "which", "has", "just", "reached", "me", ",", "I", "have", "to", "say", "that", "I", "accept", "the", "proposal", "made", "in", "it", "respecting", "your", "English", "publication", "of", "my", "poems", "&", "hereby", "agree", "that", "you", "have", "the", "privilege", "of", "selling", "that", "publication", "in", "the", "United", "States", ",", "on", "payment", "to", "me", ",", "or", "my", "agent", ",", "of", "a", "royalty", "of", "one", "shilling", ",", "(", "or", "25", "cents", "gold", ",", ")", "upon", "every", "copy", "sold", "in", "the", "U.", "S.", "Of", "course", "it", "is", "distinctly", "understood", "that", "this", "grant", "from", "me", "does", "not", "affect", "my", "copyright", "here", ",", "but", "that", "said", "copyright", ",", "in", "each", "of", "its", "particulars", "&", "in", "the", "whole", ",", "is", "absolutely", "fully", "&", "exclusively", "retained", "by", "me.", "It", "is", "not", "improbable", "that", "a", "very", "handsome", "&", "steady", "sale", "of", "the", "English", "volume", "may", "be", "effected", "here", ",", "by", "the", "right", "business", "manipulation", ",", "a", "moderate", ",", "judicious", "advertising", "&", "c.", "My", "book", "has", "never", "been", "really", "published", "here", "at", "all", "&", "the", "market", "is", "in", "a", "sort", "vacant", "of", "supplies.", "I", "will", "probably", "suggest", "to", "you", "something", "more", "on", "these", "points", ",", "in", "a", "future", "letter.", "I", "received", "yesterday", "a", "letter", "from", "Mr.", "Conway", ",", "conveying", "your", "proposition", ",", "to", "which", "I", "mailed", "an", "immediate", "answer", ",", "to", "the", "same", "effect", "as", "herewith.", "Accept", "my", "thanks", "for", "the", "William", "Blake.", "It", "has", "not", "yet", "come", "from", "the", "post", "office", ",", "but", "I", "know", "it", "will", "prove", "to", "me", "a", "profoundly", "interesting", "study", ",", "and", "a", "handsome", "gift.", "It", "is", ",", "in", "fact", ",", "a", "book", "I", "was", "wanting.", "After", "the", "reception", "of", "the", "copy", "you", "speak", "of", "my", "own", "volume", "(", "now", "probably", "on", "its", "way", ")", "I", "shall", "doubtless", "have", "occasion", "to", "express", "genuine", "pleasure", "with", "gratitude", "both", "to", "its", "editor", "&", "publisher.", "And", "now", ",", "my", "dear", "sir", ",", "please", "accept", "with", "my", "trust", "in", "the", "success", "of", "the", "enterprise", "my", "kindest", "respects", "to", "yourself", "personally", "."], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.404052767578", "recipient": "John Camden Hotten", "organizations": [], "sender": "Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/reconstruction/tei/loc.01573.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Walt Whitman to John Camden Hotten ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[[["Walt", "NNP"]], [["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["George", "NNP"], ["Routledge", "NNP"]], ["&", "CC"], [["Sons", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Broadway Dear Sirs", "Mr. Edmund Routledge"], "money": [], "year": "1868", "locations": [], "month": "Feb", "parties": ["Walt", "Whitman", "George Routledge", "Sons"], "properDate": "Feb 19, 1868", "gpe": ["New York"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[40.7143528, -74.00597309999999]], "text": "  Messrs. Routledge: Publishers Broadway Dear Sirs:              By your note of 18th, from New York, just received, I find that Mr. Edmund Routledge,                  editor, would (I quote) like to keep & use an original poem   three-page poem   sent him from me, but demurs to my first-asked price   that he directs you to offer me 10 pounds   which you can send me, $50: in gold   and that, (the terms being settled, &c.)                  he will advertise it very largely.              I accept the terms offered   $50 in gold   and you can forward me the am't as soon as convenient.                  I repeat, that I distinctly reserve the right of printing the piece in a future edition of my poems.              Sending best wishes & respects to editor & publishers, I remain. ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["Messrs.", "NNPS"], ["Routledge", "NNP"], [":", ":"], ["Publishers", "NNPS"], [["Broadway", "NNP"], ["Dear", "NNP"], ["Sirs", "NNP"]], [":", ":"], ["By", "IN"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["note", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["18th", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["from", "IN"], [["New", "NNP"], ["York", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["just", "RB"], ["received", "VBD"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["find", "VBP"], ["that", "IN"], [["Mr.", "NNP"], ["Edmund", "NNP"], ["Routledge", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["editor", "NN"], [",", ","], ["would", "MD"], ["(", "VB"], ["I", "PRP"], ["quote", "VBP"], [")", ":"], ["like", "IN"], ["to", "TO"], ["keep", "VB"], ["&", "CC"], ["use", "VB"], ["an", "DT"], ["original", "JJ"], ["poem", "NN"], ["three-page", "NN"], ["poem", "NN"], ["sent", "NN"], ["him", "PRP"], ["from", "IN"], ["me", "PRP"], [",", ","], ["but", "CC"], ["demurs", "NNS"], ["to", "TO"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["first-asked", "JJ"], ["price", "NN"], ["that", "WDT"], ["he", "PRP"], ["directs", "VBZ"], ["you", "PRP"], ["to", "TO"], ["offer", "VB"], ["me", "PRP"], [