"], ["of", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["deficient", "NN"], ["signatures", "NNS"], ["of", "IN"], ["``", "``"], ["Drum-Taps", "JJ"], ["''", "''"], ["etc.", "NNP"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["will", "MD"], ["require", "VB"], ["to", "TO"], ["finish", "VB"], ["up", "RP"], ["the", "DT"], ["edition", "NN"], [".", "."]], [[["Please", "NN"]], ["acknowledge", "NN"], ["the", "DT"], ["reception", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["this", "DT"], [",", ","], ["with", "IN"], ["check", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["(", "NN"], ["check", "VBD"], ["for", "IN"], ["$", "$"], ["31:50", "CD"], ["enclosed", "VBN"], [")", "-NONE-"]]], "sentences": ["  Attorney General's Office,                     Washington,                     February 19, 1868  Your letter of 13th was rec'd    Please find herewith a check for $31:50, which I suppose is the am't of your bill for binding 90 copies, Leaves of Grass, at 35 cts.", "Please put up 40 copies in good substantial wrapping envelope, & send me by express.", "Direct Walt Whitman, Attorney Gen's Office, Treasury Building, Washington, D. C.   Please keep the remaining 50 copies till I send some order about them.", "You have overlooked one thing.", "When I called upon you 2d January, we found a discrepancy in the two lists of sheets on hand   yours had it that Sheet B, 2d consisted of only 225 sheets   while my list had it that Sheet B 2d consisted of 325 sheets   I wish you to carefully count sheet B 2d & inform me how many there are   as it will decide how many of the deficient signatures of \"Drum-Taps\" etc., I will require to finish up the edition.", "Please acknowledge the reception of this, with check.", "(check for $31:50 enclosed) "], "words": ["Attorney", "General", "'s", "Office", ",", "Washington", ",", "February", "19", ",", "1868", "Your", "letter", "of", "13th", "was", "rec", "'d", "Please", "find", "herewith", "a", "check", "for", "$", "31:50", ",", "which", "I", "suppose", "is", "the", "am't", "of", "your", "bill", "for", "binding", "90", "copies", ",", "Leaves", "of", "Grass", ",", "at", "35", "cts.", "Please", "put", "up", "40", "copies", "in", "good", "substantial", "wrapping", "envelope", ",", "&", "send", "me", "by", "express.", "Direct", "Walt", "Whitman", ",", "Attorney", "Gen", "'s", "Office", ",", "Treasury", "Building", ",", "Washington", ",", "D.", "C.", "Please", "keep", "the", "remaining", "50", "copies", "till", "I", "send", "some", "order", "about", "them.", "You", "have", "overlooked", "one", "thing.", "When", "I", "called", "upon", "you", "2d", "January", ",", "we", "found", "a", "discrepancy", "in", "the", "two", "lists", "of", "sheets", "on", "hand", "yours", "had", "it", "that", "Sheet", "B", ",", "2d", "consisted", "of", "only", "225", "sheets", "while", "my", "list", "had", "it", "that", "Sheet", "B", "2d", "consisted", "of", "325", "sheets", "I", "wish", "you", "to", "carefully", "count", "sheet", "B", "2d", "&", "inform", "me", "how", "many", "there", "are", "as", "it", "will", "decide", "how", "many", "of", "the", "deficient", "signatures", "of", "``", "Drum-Taps", "''", "etc.", ",", "I", "will", "require", "to", "finish", "up", "the", "edition.", "Please", "acknowledge", "the", "reception", "of", "this", ",", "with", "check.", "(", "check", "for", "$", "31:50", "enclosed", ")"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.40418876649", "recipient": "Archer", "organizations": ["Leaves", "Walt Whitman", "Treasury Building"], "sender": "Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/reconstruction/tei/med.00401.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Walt Whitman to Anderson & Archer ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[[["Walt", "NNP"]], [["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Francis", "NNP"], ["P.", "NNP"], ["Church", "NNP"]], ["and", "CC"], [["William", "NNP"], ["C.", "NNP"], ["Church", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Church", "Walt Whitman"], "money": [], "year": "1868", "locations": [], "month": "Feb", "parties": ["Walt", "Whitman", "Francis P. Church", "William C. Church"], "properDate": "Feb 21, 1868", "gpe": ["Washington", "Individuality", "American", "American", "United States", "Please"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[38.8951118, -77.0363658]], "text": "  Washington, February 21, 1868.                  Messrs Church.                                  My friends,              I have now ready the prose article   (will make, I should think, about 14                 printed pages)   which I mentioned to W. F. Church, at an interview here not long since. I cannot give you any complete description of the piece   but will say that                 it takes up the subject of Democracy where the article by                 that name in the Galaxy of December, left it   and                 applies to Individuality   sketches the portrait of the ideal American of                 the future   also characterizations of the American                 woman   overhauls the Culture theory, shows its deficiencies, tested by any                 grand, practical Democratic test   argues that the main thing wanted for                 the literary, esthetic, & moral areas of the United States is to institute                 what must result in copious supplies, among the masses, of healthy, acute, handsome                 Individualities, modernized, & fully adapted to our soil, our days, city                 & country. The name of my piece is                                                                            Personalism.                                                                Don't be alarmed at the (perhaps at first sight) oddity of the word   it is the right                 title for the article, and will justify itself, & remain. The piece is a following up of Democracy   &                 is, as a literary performance, I think better than that paper   &                 will arouse more attention. Of course there is nothing in it which you would demur                 to print in the magazine. Are your plans such that you would probably like the piece for your April number?                 Could you print it positively as the leader? Please give me definite &                 immediate answers. The piece is all ready.  Walt Whitman.              ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Washington", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["February", "NNP"], ["21", "CD"], [",", ","], ["1868", "CD"], [".", "."]], [["Messrs", "NNS"], [["Church", "NNP"]], [".", "."]], [["My", "PRP$"], ["friends", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["now", "RB"], ["ready", "RB"], ["the", "DT"], ["prose", "NN"], ["article", "NN"], ["(", ":"], ["will", "MD"], ["make", "VB"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["should", "MD"], ["think", "VB"], [",", ","], ["about", "IN"], ["14", "CD"], ["printed", "VBN"], ["pages", "NNS"], [")", ":"], ["which", "WDT"], ["I", "PRP"], ["mentioned", "VBD"], ["to", "TO"], ["W.", "NNP"], ["F.", "NNP"], ["Church", "NNP"], [",", ","], ["at", "IN"], ["an", "DT"], ["interview", "NN"], ["here", "RB"], ["not", "RB"], ["long", "RB"], ["since", "IN"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["can", "MD"], ["not", "RB"], ["give", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["any", "DT"], ["complete", "JJ"], ["description", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["piece", "NN"], ["but", "CC"], ["will", "MD"], ["say", "VB"], ["that", "IN"], ["it", "PRP"], ["takes", "VBZ"], ["up", "RP"], ["the", "DT"], ["subject", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], [["Democracy", "NNP"]], ["where", "WRB"], ["the", "DT"], ["article", "NN"], ["by", "IN"], ["that", "DT"], ["name", "NN"], ["in", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], [["Galaxy", "NNP"]], ["of", "IN"], ["December", "NNP"], [",", ","], ["left", "VBD"], ["it", "PRP"], ["and", "CC"], ["applies", "VBZ"], ["to", "TO"], [["Individuality", "NNP"]], ["sketches", "NNS"], ["the", "DT"], ["portrait", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["ideal", "NN"], [["American", "NNP"]], ["of", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["future", "NN"], ["also", "RB"], ["characterizations", "NNS"], ["of", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], [["Ame