 received your kind note. I gladly accept your invitation & hospitality.                  My leave of absence continues for some time yet, & I should probably like to visit you                  for a few days, just subsequently to the middle of October   But I will write you a day or two before I come.              I send my best respects & love to Mrs. Channing. As I write we are having a rainy,                  dark sulky Sunday   after a rainy night. I am well & quietly enjoying holiday.              I wish you & wife to read my last piece in The Broadway                  London Magazine for October. You can get it at any good bookstand.               Walt Whitman.              ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["New", "NNP"], ["York", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["September", "NNP"], ["27", "CD"], [",", ","], ["1868", "CD"], [".", "."]], [["My", "PRP$"], ["dear", "NN"], ["Dr.", "NNP"], ["Channing", "NNP"], [":", ":"], ["I", "PRP"], ["yesterday", "NN"], ["received", "VBD"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["kind", "NN"], ["note", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["gladly", "RB"], ["accept", "VB"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["invitation", "NN"], ["&", "CC"], ["hospitality", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["My", "PRP$"], ["leave", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["absence", "NN"], ["continues", "VBZ"], ["for", "IN"], ["some", "DT"], ["time", "NN"], ["yet", "RB"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["I", "PRP"], ["should", "MD"], ["probably", "RB"], ["like", "IN"], ["to", "TO"], ["visit", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["for", "IN"], ["a", "DT"], ["few", "JJ"], ["days", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["just", "RB"], ["subsequently", "RB"], ["to", "TO"], ["the", "DT"], ["middle", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["October", "NNP"], ["But", "CC"], ["I", "PRP"], ["will", "MD"], ["write", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["a", "DT"], ["day", "NN"], ["or", "CC"], ["two", "CD"], ["before", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["come", "VBP"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["send", "VBP"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["best", "JJS"], ["respects", "NNS"], ["&", "CC"], ["love", "VB"], ["to", "TO"], ["Mrs.", "NNP"], ["Channing", "NNP"], [".", "."]], [["As", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["write", "VBP"], ["we", "PRP"], ["are", "VBP"], ["having", "VBG"], ["a", "DT"], ["rainy", "NN"], [",", ","], ["dark", "NN"], ["sulky", "NN"], ["Sunday", "NNP"], ["after", "IN"], ["a", "DT"], ["rainy", "NN"], ["night", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["well", "RB"], ["&", "CC"], ["quietly", "RB"], ["enjoying", "VBG"], ["holiday", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["wish", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], ["&", "CC"], ["wife", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], ["read", "VB"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["last", "JJ"], ["piece", "NN"], ["in", "IN"], ["The", "DT"], [["Broadway", "NNP"], ["London", "NNP"], ["Magazine", "NNP"]], ["for", "IN"], ["October", "NNP"], [".", "."]], [["You", "PRP"], ["can", "MD"], ["get", "VB"], ["it", "PRP"], ["at", "IN"], ["any", "DT"], ["good", "JJ"], ["bookstand", "NN"], [".", "."]], [[["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [".", "."]]], "sentences": ["  New York,                     September 27, 1868.", "My dear Dr. Channing:              I yesterday received your kind note.", "I gladly accept your invitation & hospitality.", "My leave of absence continues for some time yet, & I should probably like to visit you                  for a few days, just subsequently to the middle of October   But I will write you a day or two before I come.", "I send my best respects & love to Mrs. Channing.", "As I write we are having a rainy,                  dark sulky Sunday   after a rainy night.", "I am well & quietly enjoying holiday.", "I wish you & wife to read my last piece in The Broadway                  London Magazine for October.", "You can get it at any good bookstand.", "Walt Whitman.              "], "words": ["New", "York", ",", "September", "27", ",", "1868.", "My", "dear", "Dr.", "Channing", ":", "I", "yesterday", "received", "your", "kind", "note.", "I", "gladly", "accept", "your", "invitation", "&", "hospitality.", "My", "leave", "of", "absence", "continues", "for", "some", "time", "yet", ",", "&", "I", "should", "probably", "like", "to", "visit", "you", "for", "a", "few", "days", ",", "just", "subsequently", "to", "the", "middle", "of", "October", "But", "I", "will", "write", "you", "a", "day", "or", "two", "before", "I", "come.", "I", "send", "my", "best", "respects", "&", "love", "to", "Mrs.", "Channing.", "As", "I", "write", "we", "are", "having", "a", "rainy", ",", "dark", "sulky", "Sunday", "after", "a", "rainy", "night.", "I", "am", "well", "&", "quietly", "enjoying", "holiday.", "I", "wish", "you", "&", "wife", "to", "read", "my", "last", "piece", "in", "The", "Broadway", "London", "Magazine", "for", "October.", "You", "can", "get", "it", "at", "any", "good", "bookstand.", "Walt", "Whitman", "."], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.434244526044", "recipient": "William Francis Channing", "organizations": ["Broadway London Magazine"], "sender": "Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/reconstruction/tei/rdi.00002.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Walt Whitman to William Francis Channing ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[[["Walt", "NNP"]], [["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Peter", "NNP"], ["Doyle", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Pete", "Hinton", "Star", "Peter", "Dear", "Blair", "Jim Sorrell", "Charley"], "money": [], "year": "1868", "locations": [], "month": "Sep", "parties": ["Walt", "Whitman", "Peter Doyle"], "properDate": "Sep 29, 1868", "gpe": ["Dear", "Heaven", "Brooklyn", "New York", "Brooklyn", "Jimmy"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[40.65, -73.95], [40.7143528, -74.00597309999999], [40.65, -73.95], [38.9592201, -85.8902547]], "text": "  Sept 29.                                  Dear boy Pete,              It is splendid here to-day, & I am feeling first-rate. We have had quite a                  dark & rainy spell   but now the prospect is good weather, clear sky,                  bright sun, coolish, & no dust. I shall spend an hour or two on the river to-day.                  Your letter of 27th, Sunday, came this morning. Also two Stars, 25th & 26,                  the latter with Hinton's speech, the other containing an item about me.                  The previous Star arrived with your note of 23d, written just as you were                  going to see the Black Crook   & next morning another Star came.                  Peter, you are a good boy, & shall have your reward in Heaven, if not on earth.              Now how about that cold? I see you went to work Saturday. You seem to be                  under the weather more than I thought. Dear comrade, I hope this will find you all right                  & well as ever. I suppose you are working this week. Yesterday I spent most                  of the day in Brooklyn helping the folks to finish up the moving business.                  Got through just after dark. I have not been to any amusements yet.                  Somehow I dont seem to care about them, & I go around enough during the day.                  There is considerable political excitement here   banners swung across the streets                  almost every block, & big transparences in front of the different headquarters.                  I have seen several splendid torch-light processions, & outdoor meetings, &c.                  Of course the great majority in New York & Brooklyn is for Seymour & Blair. To Jim Sorrell: Dear Jimmy: You may not understand it, what that lady said about the bedfellow business,                  but it's all right & regular   besides, I guess you understand it well enough.                  Jimmy, dear boy, I wish you was here with me   we could have such good times.                  I send you my love   & to Charley the same   Mention how Charley's young one is getting along    I will now bid you good bye for this time, my loving friend, & God bless you, dear comrade,                  & keep you all right. I will write a line to No. 6, & will speak to the other boys in my next.              ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["Sept", "NNP"], ["29", "CD"], [".", "."]], [[["Dear", "NNP"]], ["boy", "NN"], [["Pete", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["It", "PRP"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["splendid", "VBN"], ["here", "RB"], ["to-day", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["feeling", "VBG"], ["first-rate", "JJ"], [".", "."]], [["We", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["had", "VBN"], ["quite", "RB"], ["a", "DT"], ["dark", "JJ"], ["&", "CC"], ["rainy", "NN"], ["spell", "NN"], ["but", "CC"], ["now", "RB"], ["the", "DT"], ["prospect", "NN"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["good", "JJ"], ["weather", "NN"], [",", ","], ["clear", "JJ"], ["sky", "NN"], [",", ","], ["bright", "JJ"], ["sun", "NN"], [",", ","], ["coolish", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["no", "DT"], ["dust", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["shall", "VBP"], ["spend", "VBP"], ["an", "DT"], ["hour", "NN"], ["or", "CC"], ["two", "CD"], ["on", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["river", "NN"], ["to-day", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["Your", "PRP$"], ["letter", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["27th", "CD"], [",", ","], ["Sunday", "NNP"], [",", ","], ["came", "VBD"], ["this", "DT"], ["morning", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["Also", "RB"], ["two", "CD"], ["Stars", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["25th", "JJ"], ["&", "CC"], ["26", "CD"], [",", ","], ["the", "DT"], ["latter", "NN"], ["with", "IN"], [["Hinton", "NNP"]], ["'s", "POS"], ["speech", "NN"], [",", ","], ["the", "DT"], ["other", "JJ"], ["containing", "NN"], ["an", "DT"], ["item", "NN"], ["about", "IN"], ["me", "PRP"], [".", "."]], [["The", "DT"], ["previous", "JJ"], [["Star", "NNP"]], ["arrived", "VBD"], ["with", "IN"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["note", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["23d", "CD"], [",", ","], ["written", "VBN"], ["just", "RB"], ["as", "IN"], ["you", "PRP"], ["were", "VBD"], ["going", "VBG"], ["to", "TO"], ["see", "VB"], ["the", "DT"], [["Black", "NNP"], ["Crook", "NNP"]], ["&", "CC"], ["next", "JJ"], ["morning", "NN"], ["another", "DT"], [