from New York, Walt Whitman informed the Benedicts of the date                     of his return to Washington.] ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["[", "NN"], ["Writing", "VBG"], ["from", "IN"], [["New", "NNP"], ["York", "NNP"]], [",", ","], [["Walt", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["informed", "VBD"], ["the", "DT"], [["Benedicts", "NNP"]], ["of", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["date", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["his", "PRP$"], ["return", "NN"], ["to", "TO"], [["Washington", "NNP"]], [".", "."]], [["]", "NN"]]], "sentences": [" [Writing from New York, Walt Whitman informed the Benedicts of the date                     of his return to Washington.", "] "], "words": ["[", "Writing", "from", "New", "York", ",", "Walt", "Whitman", "informed", "the", "Benedicts", "of", "the", "date", "of", "his", "return", "to", "Washington", ".", "]"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.43805249558", "recipient": "Newton Benedict", "organizations": ["Benedicts"], "sender": "Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/reconstruction/tei/med.00402.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Walt Whitman to Newton Benedict and Mrs. Newton Benedict ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[[["Walt", "NNP"]], [["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Thomas", "NNP"], ["Jefferson", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Jeff", "Wilson", "Clinton", "Mat", "Wilson", "Mat", "Mat", "Enos", "Matty", "Mother", "George", "Walt"], "money": [], "year": "1868", "locations": [], "month": "Oct", "parties": ["Walt", "Whitman", "Thomas Jefferson Whitman"], "properDate": "Oct 25, 1868", "gpe": ["New York", "Dear", "Providence", "Matty", "Gates", "St.", "Brooklyn", "Mother", "Washington", "St. Louis"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[40.7143528, -74.00597309999999], [41.8239891, -71.4128343], [35.8384082, -89.40618359999999], [40.65, -73.95], [38.8951118, -77.0363658], [38.6270025, -90.19940419999999]], "text": "  New York,                     Sunday forenoon, Oct. 25 1868.                                  Dear brother Jeff,              I suppose you rec'd the letter I wrote four or five days ago from Providence, R. I.                  I came back Thursday night, & was over home on Friday. I received your letter.                  Matty has had an examination of her lungs, by Dr. A. D. Wilson, 30 Gates Av.                  near Clinton av. I had not seen Dr. W.   it was the Thursday before I returned   yesterday I went down to see Dr. Enos, waited some time, but did not see him   I intended to make an appointment, & go down with Mat but, as I say, came away                  without seeing him   Then I went up to Gates av. & found Dr. Wilson in, & had a                  long talk with him about Mat. The impression he made upon me was that he is a                  man who knows his business thoroughly, very candid, & probably a little disposed                  to state things on the most unfavorable side, rather than the other   He said he could tell better in ten or twelve days   one of Mat's lungs is affected   thinks there is no imminent danger at all   thinks that the physician in St. Louis                  who advised a change from there here, couldn't have had any knowledge of Brooklyn                  climate or situation   nevertheless thinks that the journey & a temporary change                  will be very salutary, & do her good   advised whiskey, wine, condensed milk, &c   did not advise any drug medicines   was evidently interested, & took hold of the                  case not merely as a matter of business   After seeing him & talking [to] him,                  I abandoned the idea of consulting Enos   at least for the present.              My idea is that Matty has the possibilities of consumption in her system   but that with ordinary good luck, she can & will get over it. She has good spirits,                  is very comfortably situated   has a good, cheerfull, warm room, with southern exposure   has a good stove, gas, &c   Upon the whole, as to personal surroundings, &c                  she could not be happier in them   for Mother, & George, & Ed too, think & do                  every thing that the tenderest mother & brothers could   George is very kind   Mat realizes it all perfectly, & is herself very kind & affectionate as indeed she always was.              Mother & all wish you to arrange without fail to come on, on or before 1st December   before,                  if convenient   Mother is well, but shows her old age more & more. I return to Washington to-morrow,                  as my leave is up. The little girls are hearty as ever. Best love     Walt.              It is certain that her cough is not near as bad here as it was in St. Louis, in that house.                  ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["New", "NNP"], ["York", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["Sunday", "NNP"], ["forenoon", "NN"], [",", ","], ["Oct.", "NNP"], ["25", "CD"], ["1868", "CD"], [".", "."]], [[["Dear", "NNP"]], ["brother", "NN"], [["Jeff", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["suppose", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], ["rec", "VBP"], ["'d", "JJ"], ["the", "DT"], ["letter", "NN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["wrote", "VBD"], ["four", "CD"], ["or", "CC"], ["five", "CD"], ["days", "NNS"], ["ago", "RB"], ["from", "IN"], [["Providence", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["R.", "NNP"], ["I.", "NNP"], ["I", "NNP"], ["came", "VBD"], ["back", "RP"], ["Thursday", "NNP"], ["night", "NN"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["was", "VBD"], ["over", "IN"], ["home", "NN"], ["on", "IN"], ["Friday", "NNP"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["received", "VBD"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["letter", "NN"], [".", "."]], [[["Matty", "NNP"]], ["has", "VBZ"], ["had", "VBN"], ["an", "DT"], ["examination", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["her", "PRP$"], ["lungs", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["by", "IN"], ["Dr.", "NNP"], ["A.", "NNP"], ["D.", "NNP"], [["Wilson", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["30", "CD"], ["Gates", "NNP"], ["Av", "NNP"], [".", "."]], [["near"