 "pleasant", "afternoon", ",", "or", "Sunday", "but", "I", "tell", "you", "I", "miss", "New", "York.", "We", "had", "a", "long", "spell", "of", "splendid", "weather.", "But", "now", "it", "is", "colder", ",", "with", "some", "snow", "a", "couple", "of", "days", "since.", "Jack", ",", "you", "must", "write", "often", "as", "you", "can", "anything", "from", "my", "loving", "boy", "will", "be", "welcome", "you", "need", "n't", "be", "particular", "about", "the", "writing", "you", "might", "write", "in", "the", "car", "with", "pencil", ",", "when", "you", "have", "any", "time.", "I", "will", "write", "to", "you", "too.", "I", "will", "now", "close", "for", "this", "time.", "Dear", "Jack", ",", "I", "send", "you", "my", "love.", "Walt", "Whitman", "."], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.441860465116", "recipient": "John Flood", "organizations": ["Congress", "Navy Yard"], "sender": "Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/reconstruction/tei/med.00403.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Walt Whitman to John Flood , Jr. ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[[["Walt", "NNP"]], [["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Louisa", "NNP"], ["Van", "NNP"], ["Velsor", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Dearest", "Grant", "Mr. Evarts", "Grant", "Benedict", "Martha", "George", "Martha Has George"], "money": [], "year": "1868", "locations": ["Western Pennsylvania"], "month": "Nov", "parties": ["Walt", "Whitman", "Louisa Van Velsor Whitman"], "properDate": "Nov 24, 1868", "gpe": ["Washington", "Mother", "Portland", "Write", "Walt"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[38.8951118, -77.0363658], [45.5234515, -122.6762071]], "text": "  Attorney General's Office, Washington. Nov. 24, 1868.                  Dearest Mother,              I suppose you got my letter last Saturday, 21st   All goes along at present the                 same old story   nothing new in the office   I shall be glad when Grant                 comes in, & a new Attorney Gen'l appointed   if I weather it out till                 then   though I am well enough off, at present, & probably safe   I                 don't think there is any show for Mr. Evarts remaining here after Grant comes in    We are having a splendid spell of weather again, after the storm of Saturday                 last   To-day it is very fine   I should like to be with you on                 Thanksgiving, Thursday   I shall take dinner at my boarding house   Mrs.                     Benedict told me yesterday to bring any of my friends to dinner I wanted                 to   I still have the same room   I make a fire mornings, & have it                 quite comfortable    Is Jeff home? Martha must keep up good                 spirits   I have no doubt she will get all right again   I approve                 what you advised her about the wine   it is as George said, you can't get any                 real pure port wine   I shall keep watch of the place in Western Pennsylvania I                 spoke of, & if they have any genuine wine, as I was informed they would in                 January, I shall get some for Martha    Has George done any thing about the Portland av. house, yet? Write to me all the news. Your letter came last week, &                 was welcome. I am quite busy to-day   have several jobs of work in the office                 that keep me hard at it    Love to you, dearest mother   & to all    I have had to scratch off my letter in a hurry, but I wanted you to have something,                 according to promise in my last.   Walt.              ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["Attorney", "NNP"], ["General", "NNP"], ["'s", "POS"], ["Office", "NNP"], [",", ","], [["Washington", "NNP"]], [".", "."]], [["Nov.", "NNP"], ["24", "CD"], [",", ","], ["1868", "CD"], [".", "."]], [[["Dearest", "NNP"]], [["Mother", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["suppose", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], ["got", "VBD"], 