, "PRP$"], ["letter", "NN"], ["came", "VBD"], ["last", "JJ"], ["week", "NN"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["was", "VBD"], ["welcome", "VBN"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["quite", "RB"], ["busy", "JJ"], ["to-day", "NN"], ["have", "VBP"], ["several", "JJ"], ["jobs", "NNS"], ["of", "IN"], ["work", "NN"], ["in", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["office", "NN"], ["that", "WDT"], ["keep", "VB"], ["me", "PRP"], ["hard", "RB"], ["at", "IN"], ["it", "PRP"], ["Love", "NNP"], ["to", "TO"], ["you", "PRP"], [",", ","], ["dearest", "VBP"], ["mother", "NN"], ["&", "CC"], ["to", "TO"], ["all", "DT"], ["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["had", "VBN"], ["to", "TO"], ["scratch", "VB"], ["off", "RP"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["letter", "NN"], ["in", "IN"], ["a", "DT"], ["hurry", "NN"], [",", ","], ["but", "CC"], ["I", "PRP"], ["wanted", "VBD"], ["you", "PRP"], ["to", "TO"], ["have", "VB"], ["something", "NN"], [",", ","], ["according", "VBG"], ["to", "TO"], ["promise", "VB"], ["in", "IN"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["last", "JJ"], [".", "."]], [[["Walt", "NNP"]], [".", "."]]], "sentences": ["  Attorney General's Office, Washington.", "Nov. 24, 1868.", "Dearest Mother,              I suppose you got my letter last Saturday, 21st   All goes along at present the                 same old story   nothing new in the office   I shall be glad when Grant                 comes in, & a new Attorney Gen'l appointed   if I weather it out till                 then   though I am well enough off, at present, & probably safe   I                 don't think there is any show for Mr. Evarts remaining here after Grant comes in    We are having a splendid spell of weather again, after the storm of Saturday                 last   To-day it is very fine   I should like to be with you on                 Thanksgiving, Thursday   I shall take dinner at my boarding house   Mrs.                     Benedict told me yesterday to bring any of my friends to dinner I wanted                 to   I still have the same room   I make a fire mornings, & have it                 quite comfortable    Is Jeff home?", "Martha must keep up good                 spirits   I have no doubt she will get all right again   I approve                 what you advised her about the wine   it is as George said, you can't get any                 real pure port wine   I shall keep watch of the place in Western Pennsylvania I                 spoke of, & if they have any genuine wine, as I was informed they would in                 January, I shall get some for Martha    Has George done any thing about the Portland av.", "house, yet?", "Write to me all the news.", "Your letter came last week, &                 was welcome.", "I am quite busy to-day   have several jobs of work in the office                 that keep me hard at it    Love to you, dearest mother   & to all    I have had to scratch off my letter in a hurry, but I wanted you to have something,                 according to promise in my last.", "Walt.              "], "words": ["Attorney", "General", "'s", "Office", ",", "Washington.", "Nov.", "24", ",", "1868.", "Dearest", "Mother", ",", "I", "suppose", "you", "got", "my", "letter", "last", "Saturday", ",", "21st", "All", "goes", "along", "at", "present", "the", "same", "old", "story", "nothing", "new", "in", "the", "office", "I", "shall", "be", "glad", "when", "Grant", "comes", "in", ",", "&", "a", "new", "Attorney", "Gen'l", "appointed", "if", "I", "weather", "it", "out", "till", "then", "though", "I", "am", "well", "enough", "off", ",", "at", "present", ",", "&", "probably", "safe", "I", "do", "n't", "think", "there", "is", "any", "show", "for", "Mr.", "Evarts", "remaining", "here", "after", "Grant", "comes", "in", "We", "are", "having", "a", "splendid", "spell", "of", "weather", "again", ",", "after", "the", "storm", "of", "Saturday", "last", "To-day", "it", "is", "very", "fine", "I", "should", "like", "to", "be", "with", "you", "on", "Thanksgiving", ",", "Thursday", "I", "shall", "take", "dinner", "at", "