ecial with me, these days.", "I am well as usual   am still                 employed in the Attorney General's Office.", "A new edition of my book will be printed                 this fall, with another small volume in prose.", "You shall have                 early copies, may-be in sheets.", "Farewell for the present.", "I send you my love   Write whenever you can.", "Walt Whitman              "], "words": ["Washington", ",", "July", "21", ",", "1870.", "My", "dear", "friend", ",", "I", "have", "just", "received", "your", "letter", "of", "the", "7th", "inst.", "I", "appreciate", "your", "kindness", "in", "the", "matter", "of", "the", "poem.", "I", "send", "herewith", "a", "verbatim", "copy", "of", "Emerson", "'s", "note", ",", "as", "requested.", "Nothing", "very", "new", "or", "special", "with", "me", ",", "these", "days.", "I", "am", "well", "as", "usual", "am", "still", "employed", "in", "the", "Attorney", "General", "'s", "Office.", "A", "new", "edition", "of", "my", "book", "will", "be", "printed", "this", "fall", ",", "with", "another", "small", "volume", "in", "prose.", "You", "shall", "have", "early", "copies", ",", "may-be", "in", "sheets.", "Farewell", "for", "the", "present.", "I", "send", "you", "my", "love", "Write", "whenever", "you", "can.", "Walt", "Whitman"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.524275805794", "recipient": "Moncure D. Conway", "organizations": [], "sender": "Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/reconstruction/tei/col.00003.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Walt Whitman to Moncure D. Conway ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[[["Walt", "NNP"]], [["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["William", "NNP"], ["D.", "NNP"]], ["O'Connor", "NNP"], [",", ","]]], "people": ["George", "Wm Swinton", "Emily", "Nelly", "Jenny", "Martha", "Charles Eldridge", "Nelly Nelly", "Jeannie"], "money": [], "year": "1870", "locations": [], "month": "Aug", "parties": ["Walt", "Whitman", "William D."], "properDate": "Aug 2, 1870", "gpe": ["Brooklyn", "Jersey", "New York", "California", "St.", "St. Paul", "Walt"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[40.65, -73.95], [40.7143528, -74.00597309999999], [36.778261, -119.4179324], [44.9537029, -93.0899578]], "text": "  Brooklyn                     Aug. 2.                                  Dear friend,              I write a line just to give an account of myself. I am well as usual, & in good spirits.                  My Mother, brother George, & all, are well. I came through finely on the RR. last Wednesday   & found myself received very agreebly just as I crossed Jersey flats, approaching New York,                  by an entire change in the weather   the distressing heat gone   & in its place summer atmosphere,                  of course, but moderate enough   which has continued every day since. I enjoy it all, home here,                  day & night   especially the nights   which are fine.   I hear that Wm Swinton is here, from California. Your name was just mentioned on the editorial page                  of last Saturday's (I believe Saturday's) Tribune. I have seen Mrs. Price, she is ill with asthma.                  Her daughter Emily has had a fine little baby boy, now about a month resident in this mad world   (I write about the baby for Nelly and Jenny)   My sister Martha & the children have migrated from St. Louis                  to St. Paul, (Iowa) for a few weeks. They are as well as usual.  I am quite busy flying around   the printers & stereotypers commence on my immortal work to-morrow   My dear, dear friend, I hope you are well & in good spirits   I send you my love   also to Charles Eldridge,                  if he is there   the package of letters & paper came promptly   & I will heartily thank you to continue                  watching the letters &c. and forwarding them to me in same manner    Please enclose this in your next letter to Nelly   Nelly, my darling, I hope you are having comfortable times,                  & that all goes well   & Jeannie too   I think often about you both   & send you my best love   in which I am joined by my Mother.   Walt.              ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Brooklyn", "NNP"]], ["Aug.", "NNP"], ["2", "CD"], [".", "."]], [["Dear", "NNP"], ["friend", "VBP"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["write", "VBP"], ["a", "DT"], ["line", "NN"], ["just", "RB"], ["to", "TO"], ["give", "VB"], ["an", "DT"], ["account", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["myself", "PRP"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["well", "RB"], ["as", "IN"], ["usual", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["in", "IN"], ["good", "JJ"], ["spirits", "NNS"], [".", "."]], [["My", "PRP$"], ["Mother", "NNP"], [",", ","], ["brother", "RB"], [["George", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["all", "DT"], [",", ","], ["are", "VBP"], ["well", "RB"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["came", "VBD"], ["through", "IN"], ["finely", "RB"], ["on", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], [["RR", "NNP"]], [".", "."]], [["last", "JJ"], ["Wednesday", "NNP"], ["&", "CC"], ["found", "VBD"], ["myself", "PRP"], ["received", "VBD"], ["very", "RB"], ["agreebly", "RB"], ["just", "RB"], ["as", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["crossed", "VBD"], [["Jersey", "NNP"]], ["flats", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["approaching", "VBG"], [["New", "NNP"], ["York", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["by", "IN"], ["an", "DT"], ["entire", "JJ"], ["change", "NN"], ["in", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["weather", "NN"], ["the", "DT"], ["distressing", "NN"], ["heat", "NN"], ["gone", "NN"], ["&", "CC"], ["in", "IN"], ["its", "PRP$"], ["place", "NN"], ["summer", "NN"], ["atmosphere", "RB"], [",", ","], ["of", "IN"], ["course", "NN"], [",", ","], ["but", "CC"], ["moderate", "JJ"], ["enough", "RB"], ["which", "WDT"], ["has", "VBZ"], ["continued", "VBN"], ["every", "DT"], ["day", "NN"], ["since", "IN"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["enjoy", "VBP"], ["it", "PRP"], ["all", "DT"], [",", ","], ["home", "NN"], ["here", "RB"], [",", ","], ["day", "NN"], ["&", "CC"],