 leaving them to some future issue    Rec'd a letter from Mrs. Gilchrist in England   she has been reading \"Wake Robin\" & takes to it greatly   says Rossetti dined at her house not long since   (You know she is the authoress of the \"Woman's Estimate,\" in the Radical)    John, I think it likely I shall return about the 1st of April   Mother has had a bad spell for three days, but is about as usual again, yesterday & to-day   direct to me here                     Love to all,                 Walt.              "], "words": ["107", "north", "Portland", "av.", "Brooklyn", ",", "N.", "Y.", "March", "15.", "We", "have", "had", "cold", "&", "spiteful", "weather", "all", "the", "time", "of", "my", "visit", "here", "over", "a", "month", "&", "I", "have", "not", "had", "my", "usual", "outdoor", "enjoyment", ",", "loafing", "about", "&", "c", "have", "been", "indoors", "most", "of", "the", "time", "I", "also", "caught", "cold", "just", "on", "coming", "here", ",", "&", "it", "has", "bothered", "ever", "since.", "How", "are", "you", ",", "dear", "friend", "?", "&", "how", "is", "'Sula", "dear", "friend", ",", "too", "Write", "me", "a", "few", "lines", ",", "John", "let", "me", "know", "how", "Chauncey", "is", "getting", "along", "if", "he", "finds", "any", "difficulty", "but", "I", "guess", "not", "I", "guess", "he", "is", "getting", "along", "well", "Is", "there", "any", "thing", "new", "among", "my", "friends", "there", "in", "Wash'n", "?", "I", "have", "got", "out", "my", "new", "edition", ",", "from", "same", "plates", "as", "the", "last", ",", "only", "all", "bound", "in", "One", "Vol.", "neatly", "done", "in", "green", "cloth", ",", "vellum", "looks", "the", "best", "&", "most", "ship-shape", "of", "any", "edition", "yet", "have", "not", "added", "any", "of", "my", "later", "pieces", "in", "this", "leaving", "them", "to", "some", "future", "issue", "Rec", "'d", "a", "letter", "from", "Mrs.", "Gilchrist", "in", "England", "she", "has", "been", "reading", "``", "Wake", "Robin", "''", "&", "takes", "to", "it", "greatly", "says", "Rossetti", "dined", "at", "her", "house", "not", "long", "since", "(", "You", "know", "she", "is", "the", "authoress", "of", "the", "``", "Woman", "'s", "Estimate", ",", "''", "in", "the", "Radical", ")", "John", ",", "I", "think", "it", "likely", "I", "shall", "return", "about", "the", "1st", "of", "April", "Mother", "has", "had", "a", "bad", "spell", "for", "three", "days", ",", "but", "is", "about", "as", "usual", "again", ",", "yesterday", "&", "to-day", "direct", "to", "me", "here", "Love", "to", "all", ",", "Walt", "."], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.606283149735", "recipient": "John Burroughs", "organizations": ["Estimate", "Radical"], "sender": "Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/reconstruction/tei/nyp.00301.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Walt Whitman to John Burroughs ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[[["Walt", "NNP"]], [["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["William", "NNP"], ["J.", "NNP"], ["Linton", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Linton"], "money": [], "year": "1872", "locations": [], "month": "Mar", "parties": ["Walt", "Whitman", "William J. Linton"], "properDate": "Mar 22, 1872", "gpe": ["North Portland", "Brooklyn", "Washington"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[40.65, -73.95], [38.8951118, -77.0363658]], "text": "  107 North Portland av. Brooklyn,                     March 22.                                  My dear Linton,              Your kind letter came duly to hand. I have been delaying to write you about the portrait in answer   wanting you to do it   & wanting, if I could arrange it, to give you the full price   I will not have the job done by any second-rater, & have concluded to give it up for the present   unless it could be done by you for $50, which, I am fully aware, would not be your due engagement. I return to Washington in ten or twelve days. Is there any chance of your coming on there? ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["107", "CD"], [["North", "NNP"], ["Portland", "NNP"]], ["av", "NN"], [".", "."]], [[["Brooklyn", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["March", "NNP"], ["22", "CD"], [".", "."]], [["My", "PRP$"], ["dear", "NN"], [["Linton", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["Your", "NNP"], ["kind", "NN"], ["letter", "NN"], ["came", "VBD"], ["duly", "RB"], ["to", "TO"], ["hand", "VB"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["been", "VBN"], ["delaying", "VBG"], ["to", "TO"], ["write", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["about", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["portrait", "NN"], ["in", "IN"], ["answer", "NN"], ["wanting", "VBG"], ["you", "PRP"], ["to", "TO"], ["do", "VB"], ["it", "PRP"], ["&", "CC"], ["wanting", "VBG"], [",", ","], ["if", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["could", "MD"], ["arrange", "VB"], ["it", "PRP"], [",", ","], ["to", "TO"], ["give", "VB"], ["you", "PRP"], ["the", "DT"], ["full", "JJ"], ["price", "NN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["will", "MD"], ["not", "RB"], ["have", "VB"], ["the", "DT"], ["job", "NN"], ["done", "NN"], ["by", "IN"], ["any", "DT"], ["second-rater", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["have", "VBP"], ["concluded", "VBN"], ["to", "TO"], ["give", "VB"], ["it", "PRP"], ["up", "RP"], ["for", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["present", "NN"], ["unless", "IN"], ["it", "PRP"], ["could", "MD"], ["be", "VB"], ["done", "VBN"], ["by", "IN"], ["you", "PRP"], ["for", "IN"], ["$", "$"], ["50", "CD"], [",", ","], ["which", "WDT"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["am", "VBP"], ["fully", "RB"], ["aware", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["would", "MD"], ["not", "RB"], ["be", "VB"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["due", "JJ"], ["engagement", "NN"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["return", "VBP"], ["to", "TO"], [["Washington", "NNP"]], ["in", "IN"], ["ten", "NN"], ["or", "CC"], ["twelve", "VB"], ["days", "NNS"], [".", "."]], [["Is", "VBZ"], ["there", "EX"], ["any", "DT"], ["chance", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["coming", "VBG"], ["on", "IN"], ["there", "EX"], ["?", "."]]], "sentences": ["  107 North Portland av.