 Velsor Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[[["Walt", "NNP"]], [["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Louisa", "NNP"], ["Van", "NNP"], ["Velsor", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Peter", "Doyle", "Love"], "money": [], "year": "1873", "locations": [], "month": "Mar", "parties": ["Walt", "Whitman", "Louisa Van Velsor Whitman"], "properDate": "Mar 9, 1873", "gpe": ["Dearest", "Mother"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [], "text": "  Sunday afternoon 5 o'clock.                             Dearest mother,        I will not write much to-day, as I have just come in from being out over two hours,          & I feel quite tired. I cannot walk any to speak of, but I have been out taking a          ride in the cars, and sitting in the parks a little while. Peter Doyle has been with me.          It is as pleasant and warm as summer here to-day. I have not rec'd any letters for the last two days            I suppose you got my letter Saturday   I have been out more to-day than any day yet,          as it has been so warm & fine   Love to you, mama dear, & to all            Walt.        Mother, write me what envelopes you would like to have me direct, & enclose you              I have not been over to the office yet, except that one time ten or twelve days ago.          ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["Sunday", "NNP"], ["afternoon", "NN"], ["5", "CD"], ["o'clock", "NN"], [".", "."]], [[["Dearest", "NNP"]], ["mother", "NN"], [",", ","], ["I", "PRP"], ["will", "MD"], ["not", "RB"], ["write", "VB"], ["much", "JJ"], ["to-day", "NN"], [",", ","], ["as", "IN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["just", "RB"], ["come", "VBN"], ["in", "IN"], ["from", "IN"], ["being", "VBG"], ["out", "IN"], ["over", "IN"], ["two", "CD"], ["hours", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["I", "PRP"], ["feel", "VBP"], ["quite", "RB"], ["tired", "JJ"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["can", "MD"], ["not", "RB"], ["walk", "VB"], ["any", "DT"], ["to", "TO"], ["speak", "VB"], ["of", "IN"], [",", ","], ["but", "CC"], ["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["been", "VBN"], ["out", "RP"], ["taking", "VBG"], ["a", "DT"], ["ride", "NN"], ["in", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["cars", "NNS"], [",", ","], ["and", "CC"], ["sitting", "VBG"], ["in", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["parks", "NNS"], ["a", "DT"], ["little", "RB"], ["while", "IN"], [".", "."]], [[["Peter", "NNP"]], [["Doyle", "NNP"]], ["has", "VBZ"], ["been", "VBN"], ["with", "IN"], ["me", "PRP"], [".", "."]], [["It", "PRP"], ["is", "VBZ"], ["as", "IN"], ["pleasant", "JJ"], ["and", "CC"], ["warm", "NN"], ["as", "IN"], ["summer", "NN"], ["here", "RB"], ["to-day", "JJ"], [".", "."]], [["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["not", "RB"], ["rec", "JJ"], ["'d", "JJ"], ["any", "DT"], ["letters", "NNS"], ["for", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["last", "JJ"], ["two", "CD"], ["days", "NNS"], ["I", "PRP"], ["suppose", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], ["got", "VBD"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["letter", "NN"], ["Saturday", "NNP"], ["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["been", "VBN"], ["out", "RP"], ["more", "RBR"], ["to-day", "JJ"], ["than", "IN"], ["any", "DT"], ["day", "NN"], ["yet", "RB"], [",", ","], ["as", "IN"], ["it", "PRP"], ["has", "VBZ"], ["been", "VBN"], ["so", "RB"], ["warm", "NN"], ["&", "CC"], ["fine", "NN"], [["Love", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], ["you", "PRP"], [",", ","], ["mama", "VBP"], ["dear", "JJ"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["to", "TO"], ["all", "DT"], ["Walt", "NNP"], [".", "."]], [[["Mother", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["write", "JJ"], ["me", "PRP"], ["what", "WP"], ["envelopes", "NNS"], ["you", "PRP"], ["would", "MD"], ["like", "VB"], ["to", "TO"], ["have", "VB"], ["me", "PRP"], ["direct", "VB"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["enclose", "DT"], ["you", "PRP"], ["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["not", "RB"], ["been", "VBN"], ["over", "IN"], ["to", "TO"], ["the", "DT"], ["office", "NN"], ["yet", "RB"], [",", ","], ["except", "IN"], ["that", "DT"], ["one", "CD"], ["time", "NN"], ["ten", "VBN"], ["or", "CC"], ["twelve", "VB"], ["days", "NNS"], ["ago", "IN"], [".", "."]]], "sentences": ["  Sunday afternoon 5 o'clock.", "Dearest mother,        I will not write much to-day, as I have just come in from being out over two hours,          & I feel quite tired.", "I cannot walk any to speak of, but I have been out taking a          ride in the cars, and sitting in the parks a little while.", "Peter Doyle has been with me.", "It is as pleasant and warm as summer here to-day.", "I have not rec'd any letters for the last two days            I suppose you got my letter Saturday   I have been out more to-day than any day yet,          as it has been so warm & fine   Love to you, mama dear, & to all            Walt.", "Mother, write me what envelopes you would like to have me direct, & enclose you              I have not been over to the office yet, except that one time ten or twelve days ago.          "], "words": ["Sunday", "afternoon", "5", "o'clock.", "Dearest", "mother", ",", "I", "will", "not", "write", "much", "to-day", ",", "as", "I", "have", "just", "come", "in", "from", "being", "out", "over", "two", "hours", ",", "&", "I", "feel", "quite", "tired.", "I", "can", "not", "walk", "any", "to", "speak", "of", ",", "but", "I", "have", "been", "out", "taking", "a", "ride", "in", "the", "cars", ",", "and", "sitting", "in", "the", "parks", "a", "little", "while.", "Peter", "Doyle", "has", "been", "with", "me.", "It", "is", "as", "pleasant", "and", "warm", "as", "summer", "here", "to-day.", "I", "have", "not", "rec", "'d", "any", "letters", "for", "the", "last", "two", "days", "I", "suppose", "you", "got", "my", "letter", "Saturday", "I", "have", "been", "out", "more", "to-day", "than", "any", "day", "yet", ",", "as", "it", "has", "been", "so", "warm", "&", "fine", "Love", "to", "you", ",", "mama", "dear", ",", "&", "to", "all", "Walt.", "Mother", ",", "write", "me", "what", "envelopes", "you", "would", "like", "to", "have", "me", "direct", ",", "&", "enclose", "you", "I", "have", "not", "been", "over", "to", "the", "office", "yet", ",", "except", "that", "one", "time", "ten", "or", "twelve", "days", "ago", "."], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.655106759146", "recipient": "Louisa Van Velsor Whitman", "organizations": [], "sender": "Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/reconstruction/tei/nyp.00314.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Walt Whitman to Louisa Van Velsor Whitman ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[[["Walt", "NNP"]], [["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Louisa", "NNP"], ["Van", "NNP"], ["Velsor", "NNP"], ["Whitman", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": [], "money": [], "year": "1873", "locations": [], "month": "Mar", "parties": ["Walt", "Whitman", "Louisa Van Velsor Whitman"], "properDate": "Mar 17, 1873", "gpe": ["Mother"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [], "text": "  Monday afternoon March 17                       Well, mother dear, I feel quite well to-day considering   in good spirits,          & free from any pain   I suppose you got my letter Saturday last            The doctor has been here to-day, first time in three days            (so you see he don't think me a very critical case.)        We have had real March weather here for two or three days, strong & sudden winds, & dust            but it is pleasanter to-day   it is now about \u00bd past 1   I have had my lunch          & Mrs. O'Connor has come in for a few moments           I have a little piece in the N. Y. Graphic of Saturday afternoon, March 17   it is a daily afternoon paper   I write for it, so far   they pay moderately.        Mother, I feel to-day as if I was getting well   (but my leg is so clumsy yet            & my head has to avoid much talking or being talked to)   I hope this will          find you all right, dearest mother   I think about you much            Walt.        Mrs. O'Connor wishes me to give her love to you.          ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["Monday", "NNP"], ["afternoon", "NN"], ["March", "NNP"], ["17", 