 than usual   But my inward feeling & faith are not seriously demoralized yet.", "We are having it warm          & bright & spring like here at present   very attractive out, but my head prevents me          going out with any good enjoyment of it.", "My nieces are well   the one with the hair a          la Chinois is California, (Jessie,) the younger   the other is Mannahatta   Jeff is still at St. Louis, full of work   both my brothers have plenty of noble, manly work,          & very remunerative.", "I have just heard from John Burroughs   he is full of house     Walt        "], "words": ["431", "Stevens", "st.", "cor", "West.", "Camden", ",", "N.", "Jersey", ",", "Monday", ",", "Feb.", "23", "2\u00bd", "p.m.", "Dear", "Nelly", ",", "I", "write", "mostly", "to", "send", "the", "pictures", "you", "need", "n't", "hurry", "at", "all", "about", "returning", "them", "not", "that", "I", "have", "any", "thing", "special", "to", "write", "about.", "It", "has", "not", "been", "well", "with", "me", "now", "for", "some", "ten", "days", "not", "even", "as", "well", "as", "usual", "Still", "I", "am", "up", "&", "around", "every", "day.", "I", "suffer", "much", "with", "my", "head", ",", "&", "locomotion", "is", "more", "clumsy", "&", "paralyzed", "even", "than", "usual", "But", "my", "inward", "feeling", "&", "faith", "are", "not", "seriously", "demoralized", "yet.", "We", "are", "having", "it", "warm", "&", "bright", "&", "spring", "like", "here", "at", "present", "very", "attractive", "out", ",", "but", "my", "head", "prevents", "me", "going", "out", "with", "any", "good", "enjoyment", "of", "it.", "My", "nieces", "are", "well", "the", "one", "with", "the", "hair", "a", "la", "Chinois", "is", "California", ",", "(", "Jessie", ",", ")", "the", "younger", "the", "other", "is", "Mannahatta", "Jeff", "is", "still", "at", "St.", "Louis", ",", "full", "of", "work", "both", "my", "brothers", "have", "plenty", "of", "noble", ",", "manly", "work", ",", "&", "very", "remunerative.", "I", "have", "just", "heard", "from", "John", "Burroughs", "he", "is", "full", "of", "house", "Walt"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.702842377261", "recipient": "Ellen M.", "organizations": ["St. Louis"], "sender": "Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/reconstruction/tei/nyp.00328.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Walt Whitman to Ellen M. O'Connor ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[[["Walt", "NNP"]], [["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Ellen", "NNP"], ["M.", "NNP"]], ["O'Connor", "NNP"], [",", ","]]], "people": [], "money": [], "year": "1874", "locations": [], "month": "Mar", "parties": ["Walt", "Whitman", "Ellen M."], "properDate": "Mar 3, 1874", "gpe": ["Camden"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[51.55170589999999, -0.1588255]], "text": "  Camden, N.J.           March 3.                            Yours just rec'd   welcomed, late bad spell seems to have mainly passed over   am better to-day     W W        ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[[["Camden", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["N.J.", "NNP"], ["March", "NNP"], ["3", "CD"], [".", "."]], [["Yours", "NNS"], ["just", "RB"], ["rec", "VBP"], ["'d", "JJ"], ["welcomed", "VBN"], [",", ","], ["late", "JJ"], ["bad", "JJ"], ["spell", "NN"], ["seems", "VBZ"], ["to", "TO"], ["have", "VB"], ["mainly", "RB"], ["passed", "VBN"], ["over", "IN"], ["am", "NN"], ["better", "NN"], ["to-day", "NN"], ["W", "NNP"], ["W", "NNP"]]], "sentences": ["  Camden, N.J.           March 3.", "Yours just rec'd   welcomed, late bad spell seems to have mainly passed over   am better to-day     W W        "], "words": ["Camden", ",", "N.J.", "March", "3.", "Yours", "just", "rec", "'d", "welcomed", ",", "late", "bad", "spell", "seems", "to", "have", "mainly", "passed", "over", "am", "better", "to-day", "W", "W"], "date": [], "normalizedTime": "0.703930368557", "recipient": "Ellen M.", "organizations": [], "sender": "Whitman", "url": "http://www.whitmanarchive.org/biography/correspondence/reconstruction/tei/nyp.00329.html", "doc": {"headline": "doc", "text": ""}, "pastTO": true, "time": [], "heading": " Walt Whitman to Ellen M. O'Connor ,"}, {"taggedHeading": [[[["Walt", "NNP"]], [["Whitman", "NNP"]], ["to", "TO"], [["Abby", "NNP"], ["H.", "NNP"], ["Price", "NNP"]], [",", ","]]], "people": ["Stevens st.", "Camden", "Abby", "Eddy", "Jeff", "Walt", "Whitman Abby"], "money": [], "year": "1874", "locations": ["West"], "month": "Mar", "parties": ["Walt", "Whitman", "Abby H. Price"], "properDate": "Mar 3, 1874", "gpe": ["Washington", "Easton"], "facility": [], "latlngs": [[38.8951118, -77.0363658], [40.688432, -75.2207323], [38.6270025, -90.19940419999999]], "text": "  431 Stevens st. cor West. Camden N. Jersey,           March 3.                             Dear friend Abby, (& Dear friends all)        The letter of the 28th reached me yesterday after going wrong and was truly welcome.          (I suppose you rec'd my postal card acknowledging your previous one, briefly, & saying I should prefer the upper room.)          Since then I have had another bad spell   has lasted some fifteen days   head, legs,          gastric region, all bad   but am to-day feeling decidedly better. I shall quite          certainly come on   cannot now [pla]n the time, but will write before   & take up my quarters a while with you, as it seems to be agreeable, & the moderate sum          you mention I should pay thankfully   Though badly disabled, I am perfectly able          to take care of myself, & my sister says I am no trouble   I am sure we would all get along well together    I have just rec'd a letter from Mrs. O'Connor, from Washington, today. Her daughter,          (just 16,) is not well, has had a form of measles, a second attack, quite severe,          & is otherwise ailing, but I think will probably come out of it all, & grow stronger.          I was glad to hear about your dear grandchildren   and about our friends          Mrs. Davis & Mrs. Rein   I am alone, in the house to-day, (except Eddy)   as my sister has gone out          to spend the day, & my brother has gone to Easton, about his work. My brother Jeff,          at St. Louis, is well   his girls are growing finely.        I am sitting here in the parlor   it is about 11\u00bd   the sun has just come out, after a cloudy          half-rainy morning   is mild & warm   I go out for about an hour generally about noon,          with my cane, (& accompanied by my little yellow & white dog, a most faithful affectionate          companion)   frequently take a ride in the cars, or across in the boat   the men quite all know me, & are very kind.         Walt Whitman        Abby   mind the address   your last letter went wrong   had the wrong state    ", "dateText": "", "percents": [], "taggedText": [[["431", "CD"], [["Stevens", "NNP"], ["st.", "NNP"]], ["cor", "NN"], [["West", "NNP"]], [".", "."]], [[["Camden", "NNP"]], ["N.", "NNP"], ["Jersey", "NNP"], [",", ","], ["March", "NNP"], ["3", "CD"], [".", "."]], [["Dear", "NNP"], ["friend", "VBP"], [["Abby", "NNP"]], [",", ","], ["(", "NNP"], ["&", "CC"], ["Dear", "NNP"], ["friends", "NNS"], ["all", "DT"], [")", "NNP"], ["The", "NNP"], ["letter", "NN"], ["of", "IN"], ["the", "DT"], ["28th", "JJ"], ["reached", "JJ"], ["me", "NN"], ["yesterday", "NN"], ["after", "IN"], ["going", "VBG"], ["wrong", "JJ"], ["and", "CC"], ["was", "VBD"], ["truly", "RB"], ["welcome", "VB"], [".", "."]], [["(", "NN"], ["I", "PRP"], ["suppose", "VBP"], ["you", "PRP"], ["rec", "VBP"], ["'d", "JJ"], ["my", "PRP$"], ["postal", "NN"], ["card", "NN"], ["acknowledging", "VBG"], ["your", "PRP$"], ["previous", "JJ"], ["one", "CD"], [",", ","], ["briefly", "RB"], [",", ","], ["&", "CC"], ["saying", "VBG"], ["I", "PRP"], ["should", "MD"], ["prefer", "VB"], ["the", "DT"], ["upper", "JJ"], ["room", "NN"], [".", "."]], [[")", "NN"], ["Since", "IN"], ["then", "RB"], ["I", "PRP"], ["have", "VBP"], ["had", "VBN"], ["another", "DT"], ["bad", "